      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Formalize and lock in the Hybrid Layered (Option C) architecture for the\n  document-driven runtime, ensuring deterministic state enforcement,\n  bounded orchestration autonomy, and DRA-level rigor.\n\narchitectural_decision:\n  selected_model: C_hybrid_layered\n  rationale: >\n    Preserve a deterministic CLI/state-machine core as the sole authority\n    over request state transitions while adding a thin orchestration layer\n    that automates lifecycle steps without bypassing enforcement logic.\n\ncore_principle:\n  \"All state transitions must flow through a single deterministic authority.\"\n\nauthoritative_core:\n  file: scripts/communicate_scan.py\n  responsibilities:\n    - Parse canonical store (MD or JSON).\n    - Enforce request lifecycle state machine.\n    - Validate monotonic transitions:\n        NEW -> ACKED -> IN_PROGRESS -> DONE | BLOCKED\n    - Reject illegal transitions.\n    - Prevent modification of terminal states (DONE/BLOCKED immutable).\n    - Require explicit request_id for all mutations.\n    - Fail closed on parse errors.\n    - Emit exact repair instructions on BLOCKED.\n\norchestration_layer:\n  purpose: >\n    Provide convenience command (e.g., `communicate`) that sequentially\n    invokes core transitions:\n      1. consume INPUT PAD\n      2. create NEW request block\n      3. ack (append plan)\n      4. mark IN_PROGRESS\n      5. execute repo actions\n      6. complete or block\n  constraints:\n    - May not mutate state directly.\n    - Must call CLI APIs for each transition.\n    - Must abort if any step fails validation.\n\nstate_machine_rules:\n  required_statuses:\n    - NEW\n    - ACKED\n    - IN_PROGRESS\n    - DONE\n    - BLOCKED\n  invariants:\n    - Terminal states are immutable.\n    - request_id must be unique and stable.\n    - Timestamps must be monotonic.\n    - No implicit transitions.\n    - No re-execution of DONE.\n  concurrency_handling:\n    - File lock or atomic write strategy required.\n    - Detect concurrent modification and abort safely.\n\ncanonical_store_decision:\n  authority: JSON_canonical (recommended)\n  rendered_view: communicate.md (derived or synchronized)\n  requirement:\n    - Parsing must not depend on free-form Markdown.\n    - Protected regions clearly delimited if MD-only mode retained.\n\nerror_handling_policy:\n  - On parse ambiguity \u2192 BLOCKED with exact repair instructions.\n  - On illegal transition \u2192 refuse and log violation.\n  - On concurrent write \u2192 abort with retry guidance.\n  - No silent correction.\n\nconstraint_tightening:\n  - Runtime directory name fixed unless explicitly reconfigured.\n  - No renaming of package without spec revision.\n  - Orchestrator may not introduce new states.\n  - All commands must reference explicit request_id.\n  - Direct file edits to canonical store outside CLI invalidate run.\n\nevaluation_standard:\n  - Re-running `communicate` does not duplicate or mutate DONE.\n  - Manual corruption produces deterministic BLOCKED state.\n  - All lifecycle transitions are test-covered.\n  - Orchestration layer contains no state logic.\n\ndeliverables_required_from_codex:\n  - Refactor existing implementation to enforce single state authority.\n  - Add transition validation tests.\n  - Add immutability tests for terminal states.\n  - Add concurrency test (simulated double write).\n  - Document state machine contract in README.\n  - Document extension boundary between CLI core and orchestrator.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - No background daemon.\n  - No hidden state outside canonical store.\n  - No dynamic schema mutation.\n\nsuccess_condition:\n  The runtime is deterministic at its core, ergonomic at its surface,\n  and resistant to drift under DRA scrutiny.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Refactor runtime so JSON is canonical state authority with MD sync; add strict transition/immutability/concurrency enforcement; add orchestrator wrapper with no state logic; expand tests and docs for deterministic Option C architecture.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T00:08:32+00:00 Implemented JSON-authoritative state core, orchestrator boundary script, and expanded deterministic tests.",
      "outputs": "Implemented Option C hardening: communicate_scan.py now uses communicate.json as canonical state authority with markdown synchronization; added lock-based concurrent-write detection, monotonic timestamp validation, terminal-state immutability checks, explicit request_id mutation model, fail-closed parse/schema handling with repair guidance, and a thin communicate_orchestrator.py that invokes CLI transitions only. Added tests for transition validation, terminal immutability, and simulated lock contention. Updated README and Codex instructions to document state contract and extension boundary.",
