      "request_text": "problem_type: descriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Independently verify Codex\u2019s claimed Hybrid Layered runtime implementation,\n  ensuring architectural compliance with the binding constraints and DRA-level\n  enforcement guarantees.\n\nverification_scope:\n  - commscribe/communicate.json (canonical authority)\n  - commscribe/communicate.md (rendered/synced view)\n  - commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py (state authority)\n  - commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py (thin orchestration layer)\n  - commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py\n  - Makefile targets\n  - CODEX_COMMUNICATE_INSTRUCTIONS.md\n\nverification_requirements:\n\n  1_state_authority_validation:\n    - Confirm communicate_scan.py is the sole module mutating canonical state.\n    - Confirm all transitions pass through validated functions.\n    - Confirm no direct JSON mutation occurs outside scan module.\n\n  2_state_machine_enforcement:\n    - Validate monotonic transitions:\n        NEW -> ACKED -> IN_PROGRESS -> DONE | BLOCKED\n    - Confirm terminal states (DONE/BLOCKED) are immutable.\n    - Confirm illegal transitions raise deterministic failure.\n    - Confirm explicit request_id required for mutation.\n\n  3_canonical_integrity:\n    - Confirm communicate.json is authoritative.\n    - Confirm communicate.md is derived or synchronized (not authoritative).\n    - Confirm synchronization is deterministic and one-directional.\n\n  4_orchestrator_boundary_check:\n    - Confirm communicate_orchestrator.py contains:\n        * No state mutation logic.\n        * Only calls to communicate_scan API functions.\n    - Confirm orchestrator aborts on validation failure.\n\n  5_idempotence_check:\n    - Run `make communicate` with no new INPUT PAD data.\n    - Confirm:\n        * No new request blocks created.\n        * No timestamp mutation.\n        * No status changes.\n        * Deterministic \u201cNothing to do\u201d behavior.\n\n  6_concurrency_and_locking:\n    - Inspect for file locking or atomic write mechanism.\n    - Validate test coverage for concurrent write attempt.\n    - Confirm fail-closed behavior under contention.\n\n  7_parse_failure_handling:\n    - Intentionally corrupt communicate.json.\n    - Confirm:\n        * Process fails closed.\n        * BLOCKED status emitted with exact repair instructions.\n        * No silent correction.\n\n  8_protocol_integrity:\n    - Confirm INPUT PAD consumption removes or marks content atomically.\n    - Confirm no duplicate REQ-* creation on repeated runs.\n    - Confirm stable ID generation format.\n\nevidence_standard:\n  - Cite specific functions and line references.\n  - Distinguish verified vs inferred behavior.\n  - No reliance on test success claims without inspection.\n\nevaluation_output_required:\n  - Compliance matrix (Spec vs Implementation).\n  - Any deviations from Hybrid C architecture.\n  - Drift or hidden coupling risks.\n  - Hard-failure findings (if any).\n  - Confidence level: High / Medium / Low.\n\nconstraints:\n  - Do not assume correctness based on test pass alone.\n  - Treat test coverage as necessary but not sufficient.\n  - Prioritize structural guarantees over surface behavior.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Perform independent verification against requested scope: inspect authoritative modules and tests, execute idempotence/concurrency/parse-failure checks, produce compliance matrix with line-referenced evidence and explicit deviations.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T00:10:12+00:00 Started independent architecture compliance verification for Hybrid C runtime.\n- 2026-02-13T00:10:59+00:00 Completed code-level and runtime verification checks, including idempotence hash comparison and corrupted-JSON fail-closed probes.",
      "outputs": "Compliance Matrix (Spec vs Implementation)\n\n1) State authority validation: PARTIAL PASS\n- Verified: communicate_scan.py is the only module writing communicate.json via _atomic_write_json (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:88-91, 319, 332, 350, 373, 395).\n- Verified: transitions are centralized through _transition and command handlers (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:244-252, 325-397).\n- Verified: no other script writes communicate.json directly in active code paths (search across commscribe/).\n- Inferred risk: UI writes communicate.md directly (commscribe/scripts/start_communicate_ui.py:31, 69-71), which is acceptable for INPUT PAD staging but can temporarily desync human view vs JSON until next core operation.\n\n2) State machine enforcement: PASS\n- Verified transition map NEW->ACKED->IN_PROGRESS->DONE|BLOCKED (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:27-33).\n- Verified terminal immutability enforcement (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:246-247, 389-390).\n- Verified explicit request_id required on mutating commands via argparse flags --id (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:409-419 and corresponding parsers).\n- Verified deterministic failure on illegal transitions (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:248-249, 346, 369).\n\n3) Canonical integrity: PARTIAL PASS\n- Verified JSON canonical path and loader precedence (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:205-219, 222-223).\n- Verified markdown is synchronized from JSON after mutations (_sync_markdown) (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:254-263, 320, 333, 351, 374, 396).\n- Deviation: if communicate.json is missing, state is bootstrapped from markdown queue (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:192-202, 217-219). This weakens strict one-directional guarantee under file-loss scenarios.\n\n4) Orchestrator boundary check: PARTIAL PASS\n- Verified orchestrator contains no JSON/MD state mutation logic; it shells out to communicate_scan transitions only (commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py:31-43, 50, 66, 71, 78-88, 100-111, 120-130).\n- Verified abort-on-validation-failure by returncode checks after each step (commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py:51-54, 67-69, 72-74, 90-92, 113-115, 132-134).\n- Note: requirement text said API functions; implementation uses CLI subprocess calls instead.\n\n5) Idempotence check: PASS\n- Verified by command run: make communicate twice with no input.\n- Verified no mutation: SHA256 unchanged for communicate.md and communicate.json; request count unchanged (before_count=3, after_count=3).\n- Verified deterministic output: No new INPUT PAD content. Nothing to do.\n\n6) Concurrency and locking: PASS\n- Verified lock mechanism via lockfile create-excl and timeout fail (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:266-281).\n- Verified atomic write path for JSON and markdown (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:82-91).\n- Verified test coverage for contention (commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py:78-85).\n\n7) Parse failure handling: HARD FAILURE vs requested BLOCKED behavior\n- Verified fail-closed with exact repair instructions for invalid JSON parse (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:209-213).\n- Verified runtime behavior: scanner exits non-zero and prints repair guidance.\n- Deviation: no BLOCKED status is emitted on parse failure because state cannot be loaded and no fallback block-record mechanism exists.\n\n8) Protocol integrity: PARTIAL PASS\n- Verified INPUT PAD consumption marks placeholder in same consume operation and writes request entry (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:295-321).\n- Verified stable ID format REQ-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS with suffix collision handling (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:226-235).\n- Verified repeated no-input runs do not create duplicate requests.\n- Risk: JSON and markdown writes are atomic per file but not cross-file transactional; crash between writes can leave temporary divergence until next successful sync.\n\nDeviations from Hybrid C target\n- Missing BLOCKED emission path for parse/schema corruption failures.\n- Strict one-directional canonical flow is softened by markdown bootstrap when JSON is missing.\n- Orchestrator uses CLI subprocess interface, not direct internal API calls (still preserves boundary).\n\nDrift / hidden coupling risks\n- UI can edit markdown INPUT PAD directly; if non-pad sections are modified manually, sync safety depends on marker integrity checks.\n- Cross-file transaction gap (JSON write then markdown sync) can produce transient mismatch after interruption.\n\nHard-failure findings\n- Parse-failure BLOCKED emission requirement is not implemented.\n\nConfidence level\n- Medium-High. Core enforcement behavior is strongly verified via code inspection plus runtime probes. Confidence is not High due to the identified hard failure and bootstrap/transaction edge cases.",
      "evidence": "Verification commands executed:\n1) python3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py --file commscribe/communicate.md --json commscribe/communicate.json consume\n2) nl -ba commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py\n3) nl -ba commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py\n4) nl -ba commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py\n5) nl -ba Makefile\n6) nl -ba commscribe/CODEX_COMMUNICATE_INSTRUCTIONS.md\n7) rg -n \"communicate\\.json|_atomic_write_json|write_text\\(|json\\.dump|json\\.dumps\" commscribe -S\n8) make communicate (run twice) with before/after SHA256 and request-count comparison\n9) Corruption probe in temp workspace:\n   - communicate_scan consume on invalid JSON -> exit 1 + repair guidance\n   - communicate_orchestrator with invalid JSON -> exit 1 + repair guidance\n\nObserved deterministic idempotence evidence:\n- before_md == after_md\n- before_json == after_json\n- before_count == after_count == 3\n- output consistently: No new INPUT PAD content. Nothing to do.\n\nObserved parse-failure evidence:\n- scan_code=1, orch_code=1\n- error message contains: JSON parse failure ... Repair: fix JSON syntax before rerun.\n- no BLOCKED transition persisted for that failure path.",
