      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Address the identified hard failure in the Hybrid Layered runtime:\n  parse-failure path fails closed but does not persist a BLOCKED request state.\n  Modify the architecture so all structural failures produce a durable,\n  auditable BLOCKED record without violating canonical integrity.\n\nfailure_identified:\n  description: >\n    When communicate.json parsing fails, the system aborts with repair guidance\n    but does not create or persist a BLOCKED request entry documenting the failure.\n  severity: hard_failure\n  impact:\n    - Breaks audit trail completeness.\n    - Violates requirement: \"fail closed with BLOCKED status.\"\n    - Reduces post-mortem traceability.\n    - Weakens DRA-level determinism guarantees.\n\nrequired_behavior_change:\n\n  1_failure_capture_contract:\n    - On parse failure:\n        * Do NOT mutate corrupted canonical file.\n        * Create a separate failure artifact documenting the failure.\n    - Artifact must include:\n        - timestamp\n        - error type\n        - error details\n        - repair instructions\n        - hash of corrupted file (if readable)\n        - runtime version\n\n  2_persistence_strategy:\n    option_A_recovery_log:\n      file: commscribe/failure_log.json\n      rule:\n        - Append structured BLOCKED entry.\n        - Never overwrite.\n        - Independent of canonical store integrity.\n\n    option_B_shadow_block:\n      file: commscribe/communicate.recovery.json\n      rule:\n        - Persist BLOCKED state entry referencing failed request_id.\n        - Used only for recovery and audit.\n\n    selection_rule:\n      - Must not attempt to write to corrupted communicate.json.\n      - Must not silently repair.\n      - Must preserve original corrupted file unchanged.\n\n  3_state_machine_extension:\n    - Introduce meta-status: SYSTEM_BLOCKED\n    - Distinct from user-request BLOCKED.\n    - Cannot transition until manual repair confirmed.\n\n  4_cli_behavior_update:\n    - communicate_scan.py must:\n        * Catch parse exceptions.\n        * Persist failure artifact.\n        * Emit deterministic error message.\n        * Exit non-zero.\n    - communicate_orchestrator.py must:\n        * Detect SYSTEM_BLOCKED.\n        * Refuse further execution.\n\n  5_test_expansion:\n    Add tests for:\n      - Corrupted JSON \u2192 failure artifact created.\n      - Original corrupted file remains unchanged.\n      - No duplicate failure artifacts on rerun.\n      - Recovery after repair clears SYSTEM_BLOCKED.\n      - Hash recorded matches corrupted content.\n\n  6_documentation_update:\n    - Update README with:\n        * Failure handling guarantees.\n        * Recovery protocol.\n    - Update CODEX_COMMUNICATE_INSTRUCTIONS.md:\n        * Explicit parse-failure contract.\n\nconstraints:\n  - No silent canonical mutation.\n  - No auto-repair.\n  - No data loss.\n  - Failure artifacts must be deterministic and append-only.\n  - Core state authority remains single source of truth.\n\nevaluation_standard:\n  - Corrupt communicate.json \u2192 deterministic failure artifact created.\n  - Re-running without repair does not create duplicates.\n  - After repair, system resumes normal lifecycle.\n  - Audit trail remains complete and reconstructible.\n\nsuccess_condition:\n  Every structural failure produces a durable, inspectable,\n  non-destructive record while preserving canonical integrity.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Implement deterministic parse-failure persistence via append-only failure artifact, add SYSTEM_BLOCKED detection path and dedup semantics, propagate blocking to orchestrator, add regression tests for corruption/idempotence/recovery, and update runtime docs.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T00:13:02+00:00 Started implementing durable parse-failure audit artifact and SYSTEM_BLOCKED behavior.\n- 2026-02-13T00:15:16+00:00 Implemented SYSTEM_BLOCKED failure artifact path, deduplicated rerun behavior, recovery signaling, orchestrator guard, and expanded tests.",
      "outputs": "Implemented durable structural-failure auditing without mutating corrupted canonical state. communicate_scan.py now persists append-only SYSTEM_BLOCKED events to failure_log.json on parse/schema failures, records timestamp/error/repair/file hash/runtime version, deduplicates repeated failures against the same corrupted hash, and exposes system-status with SYSTEM_BLOCKED gating plus SYSTEM_RECOVERED append event after successful manual repair validation. communicate_orchestrator.py now checks system-status before execution and refuses to proceed when blocked. Added test coverage for corrupted JSON artifact creation, unchanged corrupted file, duplicate suppression on rerun, recovery clearing behavior, and hash correctness; retained existing lifecycle/concurrency tests.",
      "evidence": "Validation: python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v (8/8 passing); make communicate => deterministic no-op with empty INPUT PAD. Updated files: commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py, commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py, commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py, commscribe/README.md, commscribe/CODEX_COMMUNICATE_INSTRUCTIONS.md, Makefile.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "problem_type: prescriptive"
