      "outputs": "Compliance Matrix (Spec vs Implementation)\n\n1) Single state authority: PASS\n- Confirmed: canonical JSON writes are only in scan module via _atomic_write_json (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:105-109, 235, 268, 463, 476, 494, 517).\n- Confirmed: orchestrator has no JSON/MD mutation logic and only shells to scan commands (commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py:32-46, 61-147).\n- Confirmed: no canonical write paths outside scan in scoped files.\n\n2) Failure artifact integrity: PASS\n- Confirmed append-only behavior: _append_failure_event always appends then writes (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:265-268).\n- Confirmed required fields: event includes timestamp, error_type, error_details, repair_instructions, file_hash, runtime_version (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:315-325).\n- Confirmed dedupe by active block + same hash + same error_type (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:310-313).\n- Confirmed corrupted communicate.json remains unchanged in corruption probe (observed content stayed `{bad json`).\n\n3) SYSTEM_BLOCKED state machine: PARTIAL PASS\n- Confirmed blocked gating: unresolved SYSTEM_BLOCKED prevents execution via _maybe_clear_system_block (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:338-342).\n- Confirmed explicit validation-based recovery: only after hash change + successful _load_state does SYSTEM_RECOVERED append (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:344-355).\n- Confirmed orchestrator refusal with non-zero exit when blocked (commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py:53-59; probe returned code 2).\n- Deviation: if input pad is empty, consume returns early before canonical validation (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:438-442), so blocked state is not surfaced on that path.\n\n4) Idempotence and determinism: PASS\n- make communicate with empty input produced deterministic no-op output.\n- No mutation observed: md/json/failure_log hashes unchanged; request count and failure event count unchanged.\n\n5) Concurrency guarantees: PASS\n- Confirmed lock acquisition and timeout fail-closed behavior (_lock) (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:410-433).\n- Confirmed lock contention test exists (commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py:82-89).\n- Confirmed atomic write strategy for JSON/MD (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:99-109).\n\n6) Protocol resilience: PASS\n- Stable request IDs with collision suffix strategy (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:370-378).\n- Terminal immutability enforced (_transition) (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:388-396).\n- Illegal transitions rejected (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:392-393 and command guards).\n- Markdown marker checks protect structured regions during sync (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:57-77, 398-407).\n\n7) Test coverage quality: PASS\n- Coverage present for transition validation, terminal immutability, lock contention, parse-failure artifacting, dedupe/no mutation, and recovery path (commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py:65-150).\n- Catch-all exists in main, but not silent: errors are surfaced and non-zero returned with explicit message (commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py:564-582).\n\nRemaining structural gap\n- SYSTEM_BLOCKED is not enforced on consume no-op path due to early return before _load_state validation.\n\nDrift/future fragility risks\n- Failure dedupe key is hash+error_type; different parser errors on same corrupted blob could append multiple events.\n- Cross-file JSON->MD sync is not transactional across both files (atomic per file only), allowing transient mismatch after interruption.\n\nConfidence rating\n- High.\n\nFinal verdict\n- DRA-adequate (not DRA-hard compliant due to one enforcement gap on empty-input consume path).",
      "evidence": "Inspected files and references:\n- commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py (line-referenced)\n- commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py (line-referenced)\n- commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py (line-referenced)\n- Makefile\n- commscribe/README.md\n- commscribe/CODEX_COMMUNICATE_INSTRUCTIONS.md\n\nRuntime probes executed:\n1) Idempotence probe:\n   - make communicate\n   - md/json/failure_log SHA256 unchanged\n   - request count unchanged (5->5)\n   - failure event count unchanged (0->0)\n2) SYSTEM_BLOCKED probe in isolated tmp workspace:\n   - first consume with corrupted JSON: exit 1 and SYSTEM_BLOCKED persisted\n   - second consume without repair: exit 1 unresolved SYSTEM_BLOCKED\n   - system-status: exit 2 unresolved SYSTEM_BLOCKED\n   - orchestrator --exec-cmd true: exit 2 unresolved SYSTEM_BLOCKED\n   - failure_log events=1 (dedup confirmed)\n   - corrupted JSON content remained unchanged (`{bad json`)\n3) Regression tests:\n   - python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v\n   - result: 8/8 passing",
