      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T03:30:06+00:00 Started independent meta-validation of post-REQ-20260212-212001 DRA-hard claim.\n- 2026-02-13T03:31:01+00:00 Ran deterministic probes for healthy no-op, markdown recovery, JSON recovery, and UI concurrent write; all outcomes matched expected invariants.",
      "outputs": "Meta-Compliance Summary (Pass/Fail by Invariant Group)\n\n1) Compliance record integrity: PASS\n- Verified REQ-20260212-212001 exists in both `commscribe/communicate.md` and `commscribe/communicate.json` and has `DONE` status.\n- Verified completion payload includes the required compliance matrix dimensions (state authority, source-aware recovery, lock/atomic contract, UI race resolution, idempotence) and includes evidence section.\n- Verified evidence pointers remain valid to current files in scope.\n\n2) Invariant recheck: PASS\n- Monotonic transitions and terminal immutability enforcement remain in scanner state machine logic and corresponding tests pass.\n- SYSTEM_BLOCKED surfacing on all entrypaths remains enforced via preflight checks.\n- Source-aware failure dedupe is active (`source_file` + `source_hash` + `failure_scope` + `error_type`).\n- Markdown-only recovery clears blocked state without requiring JSON mutation (validated probe and test).\n- No recovery-time canonical JSON mutation occurred in markdown-origin recovery probe.\n- No hidden behavioral side-effects observed from `runtime_io` abstraction.\n\n3) Cross-project portability check: PASS\n- No hard-coded machine-specific absolute paths in runtime code or docs; runtime paths are argument-driven with repo-relative defaults.\n- Locking uses portable lockfile create-excl semantics (no OS-specific fcntl/flock dependency).\n- No environment-specific service/daemon assumptions introduced.\n- Runtime still operates as repo-local scripts + files.\n\n4) Reproducibility probe: PASS\n- Healthy empty-input no-op: deterministic message + exit 0 + no MD/JSON hash change.\n- Markdown-only corruption + recovery: consume fails closed (exit 1), repair markdown only, system-status returns SYSTEM_OK (exit 0), JSON unchanged during recovery check.\n- JSON-only corruption + recovery: consume fails closed (exit 1), manual JSON repair, system-status returns SYSTEM_OK (exit 0).\n- UI concurrent write scenario: targeted concurrency test passed with no queue/index clobber.\n\n5) Drift detection: PASS\n- No new mutable global state introduced.\n- No silent auto-repair logic introduced.\n- No UI bypass of scanner authority remains on input writes.\n- Compliance doc updates are aligned with implementation.\n\nResidual architectural fragility\n- Low: structural failure classification currently relies on error-message matching for markdown marker failures; message-shape changes could require classifier update.\n\nFinal portability classification\n- Transplant-ready with cautions\n\nConfidence\n- High",
      "evidence": "Meta-validation evidence:\n\nIntegrity probe:\n1) Checked REQ existence/status in both stores\n   - md_has_req True\n   - json_has_req True\n   - json_status DONE\n\nSuite execution:\n2) python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v\n   - Result: 15/15 passing\n\nRepro probes (isolated tmp dirs):\n3) Healthy no-op consume probe\n   - A_code=0\n   - A_noop_msg=1\n   - A_md_unchanged=yes\n   - A_json_unchanged=yes\n\n4) Markdown-only corruption + recovery\n   - B_consume_code=1\n   - B_status_code=0\n   - B_json_changed_during_recovery=no\n\n5) JSON-only corruption + recovery\n   - C_consume_code=1\n   - C_status_code=0\n\n6) UI concurrent write scenario\n   - python3 -m unittest commscribe.tests.test_communicate_ui.CommunicateUiTests.test_concurrent_set_input_and_consume_no_queue_clobber -v\n   - D_code=0\n\nCode/doc inspection covered:\n- commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py\n- commscribe/scripts/runtime_io.py\n- commscribe/scripts/start_communicate_ui.py\n- commscribe/scripts/communicate_orchestrator.py\n- commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py\n- commscribe/tests/test_communicate_ui.py\n- commscribe/docs/COMPLIANCE_DRA_HARD.md",
