      "request_text": "problem_type: descriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Evaluate the runtime after being transplanted into this new project\n  (not the original commscribe repo), and determine whether it remains\n  structurally sound, invariant-preserving, and safe for reuse in additional projects.\n\ncontext:\n  - Runtime was originally developed and verified as DRA-hard compliant.\n  - It has now been copied into a separate, real project.\n  - All tests pass (15/15).\n  - Meta-compliance groups PASS.\n  - Portability classification: \"Transplant-ready with cautions.\"\n\nanalysis_requirements:\n\n  1_environmental_stress_check:\n    - Confirm no hidden assumptions tied to original repo layout.\n    - Confirm no path collisions with host project.\n    - Confirm no Makefile or tooling conflicts.\n    - Confirm lock + atomic I/O behave correctly in this environment.\n\n  2_invariant_revalidation:\n    - Verify:\n        * Monotonic state transitions\n        * Terminal immutability\n        * SYSTEM_BLOCKED surfacing everywhere\n        * Source-aware failure recovery\n        * UI + scanner concurrency integrity\n    - Confirm no regressions specific to this host project.\n\n  3_host_project_interaction_risk:\n    - Identify whether:\n        * Large file trees affect performance.\n        * Existing test runners interfere.\n        * Pre-existing JSON or markdown conventions collide.\n        * Existing UI/server processes introduce lock contention.\n\n  4_portability_caution_clarification:\n    - Explicitly define what \u201cTransplant-ready with cautions\u201d means\n      in the context of this host project.\n    - Classify cautions:\n        * correctness risk\n        * operational risk\n        * scaling risk\n    - State whether any caution blocks further reuse.\n\n  5_reuse_readiness_verdict:\n    - One of:\n        * Safe to copy into additional projects now\n        * Safe with validation checklist\n        * Requires hardening before wider reuse\n    - Justify briefly.\n\nconstraints:\n  - No redesign proposals.\n  - No feature expansion.\n  - Validation only.\n  - Distinguish between structural guarantees and environmental variance.\n\ndeliverable_format:\n  - Structured validation report.\n  - Clear PASS / RISK / CAUTION markers.\n  - Final reuse classification with confidence level.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Validate transplanted-runtime behavior in this host project: environment assumptions, invariant preservation, host interaction risks, caution classification, and final reuse readiness verdict.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T03:35:51+00:00 Started host-project structural validation for transplanted runtime.\n- 2026-02-13T03:36:38+00:00 Completed host-environment stress/invariant checks, including no-op non-mutation probe, isolated JSON corruption-recovery probe, collision scan, and full 15-test suite.",
      "outputs": "Structured Validation Report\n\nPASS\n- Environmental stress check:\n  - No hidden dependency on original repository path detected; runtime uses repo-relative defaults under `commscribe/*` and argument-driven paths.\n  - No path collision with host project components observed outside `commscribe/`.\n  - Lock + atomic I/O behavior remains correct in this environment (shared `runtime_io` used by scanner paths and UI-set-input path).\n\nPASS\n- Invariant revalidation:\n  - Monotonic transitions and terminal immutability remain enforced and validated by passing tests.\n  - SYSTEM_BLOCKED surfacing remains active across entrypaths (scan preflight + system-status gate).\n  - Source-aware failure dedupe and recovery remain functional.\n  - UI + scanner concurrency integrity holds under contention tests.\n\nPASS\n- Host project interaction risk check:\n  - Large host tree did not affect runtime determinism in probes/tests.\n  - Existing project test tooling did not interfere with isolated `commscribe/tests` execution.\n  - No convention collision found for `communicate.json` / `communicate.md` because files remain namespaced in `commscribe/`.\n  - Existing process contention scenario is fail-closed through lock timeout behavior.\n\nRISK\n- Correctness risk: none observed.\n\nCAUTION\n- Operational risk: this host repo currently has no `Makefile`, so `make communicate`, `make communicate-ui`, and `make communicate-orchestrate` are unavailable unless manually added. Direct `python3 commscribe/scripts/...` commands work.\n\nCAUTION\n- Scaling risk: lockfile strategy serializes writers by design; under very high concurrent UI/scanner write load, retries/timeouts are expected behavior rather than data corruption.\n\nPortability caution clarification in this host project\n- \u201cTransplant-ready with cautions\u201d here means structural guarantees are intact, but operator ergonomics depend on host integration details (notably missing make targets). The cautions are operational/scaling, not correctness-blocking.\n\nFinal reuse readiness verdict\n- Safe with validation checklist\n\nConfidence\n- High",
      "evidence": "Evidence and probes:\n\n1) Full runtime suite:\n- python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v\n- Result: 15/15 passing\n\n2) Host no-op determinism probe:\n- python3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py consume\n- Result: noop_code=0, noop_msg=1, md_unchanged=yes, json_unchanged=yes\n\n3) Isolated JSON corruption + recovery probe:\n- consume on corrupt json: exit 1\n- system-status after manual json repair: exit 0\n- Result summary: json_corrupt_code=1, json_recover_code=0\n\n4) Host Makefile check:\n- ls -1 | rg '^[Mm]akefile$'\n- Result: none present in host root\n\n5) Collision/assumption scan:\n- rg -n \"commscribe|communicate_scan|communicate_orchestrator|failure_log\\.json|communicate\\.json|communicate\\.md\" -S .\n- Result: references scoped to commscribe artifacts and docs; no conflicting host runtime module found.",
