      "request_text": "problem_type: descriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Translate the \u201cSafe with validation checklist\u201d verdict into a concrete,\n  minimal operational checklist required before copying this runtime\n  into additional projects beyond this first transplanted host.\n\ncontext:\n  - Structural invariants PASS in first external host.\n  - No correctness risks identified.\n  - Operational/scaling cautions only:\n      * No host Makefile targets by default.\n      * Lock serialization under high contention.\n  - Confidence: High.\n\nrequired_output:\n\n  1_validation_checklist:\n    Provide a minimal, repeatable checklist to run immediately\n    after pasting into any new repository:\n\n      - Step 1: Healthy no-op verification\n      - Step 2: Markdown corruption + recovery probe\n      - Step 3: JSON corruption + recovery probe\n      - Step 4: Concurrent UI + scanner contention probe\n      - Step 5: Confirm Makefile target integration (if used)\n\n    Each step must include:\n      * exact command\n      * expected exit code\n      * expected observable state change (or no change)\n\n  2_operational_cautions_explained:\n    Clarify:\n      - When lack of Makefile target matters.\n      - When lock serialization could become noticeable.\n      - Whether contention is correctness-safe or only performance-impacting.\n\n  3_scaling_threshold_estimate:\n    Provide qualitative guidance on:\n      - Expected behavior under:\n          * low request volume\n          * moderate request volume\n          * heavy concurrent UI use\n      - Whether degradation is graceful or failure-prone.\n\n  4_reuse_boundary_statement:\n    State clearly:\n      - This runtime is suitable for:\n          * solo developer projects\n          * small teams\n          * AI-heavy dev workflows\n      - This runtime is not yet optimized for:\n          * high-concurrency multi-user server environments\n          * distributed deployments\n\nconstraints:\n  - No redesign suggestions.\n  - No feature expansion.\n  - No marketing language.\n  - Keep checklist deterministic and concise.\n\ndeliverable_format:\n  - Structured Markdown checklist.\n  - Clear PASS criteria for each step.\n  - Final reuse readiness statement with confidence level.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Produce minimal post-transplant validation checklist with exact commands/exit criteria, operational cautions, scaling behavior guidance, and reuse boundary statement based on verified runtime behavior.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T03:38:28+00:00 Started drafting deterministic reuse checklist and operational boundary summary for additional project transplants.",
      "outputs": "## Validation Checklist (Post-Paste Into New Repo)\n\n1. Step 1: Healthy no-op verification\n- Command:\n```bash\npython3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py \\\n  --file commscribe/communicate.md \\\n  --json commscribe/communicate.json \\\n  --failure-log commscribe/failure_log.json \\\n  consume\n```\n- Expected exit code: `0`\n- PASS criteria:\n  - stdout contains `No new INPUT PAD content. Nothing to do.`\n  - no new request block added\n  - `communicate.md` and `communicate.json` hashes unchanged\n\n2. Step 2: Markdown corruption + recovery probe\n- Commands:\n```bash\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncp commscribe/communicate.md \"$tmp/communicate.md\"\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"schema_version\":1,\"canonical_store\":\"communicate.json\",\"requests\":[]}' > \"$tmp/communicate.json\"\nperl -0pi -e 's/Paste request text here\\. One request at a time\\. Include files\\/paths if relevant\\./Probe markdown failure/' \"$tmp/communicate.md\"\nperl -0pi -e 's/<!-- REQUEST_QUEUE_END -->/<!-- REQUEST_QUEUE_END_BROKEN -->/' \"$tmp/communicate.md\"\npython3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py --file \"$tmp/communicate.md\" --json \"$tmp/communicate.json\" --failure-log \"$tmp/failure_log.json\" consume\nperl -0pi -e 's/<!-- REQUEST_QUEUE_END_BROKEN -->/<!-- REQUEST_QUEUE_END -->/' \"$tmp/communicate.md\"\npython3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py --file \"$tmp/communicate.md\" --json \"$tmp/communicate.json\" --failure-log \"$tmp/failure_log.json\" system-status\n```\n- Expected exit codes:\n  - first `consume`: non-zero (`1`)\n  - `system-status` after markdown repair: `0`\n- PASS criteria:\n  - first call surfaces `SYSTEM_BLOCKED`\n  - recovery succeeds after markdown-only repair\n  - no JSON mutation required during recovery validation\n\n3. Step 3: JSON corruption + recovery probe\n- Commands:\n```bash\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncp commscribe/communicate.md \"$tmp/communicate.md\"\nprintf '{bad json' > \"$tmp/communicate.json\"\npython3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py --file \"$tmp/communicate.md\" --json \"$tmp/communicate.json\" --failure-log \"$tmp/failure_log.json\" consume\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"schema_version\":1,\"canonical_store\":\"communicate.json\",\"requests\":[]}' > \"$tmp/communicate.json\"\npython3 commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py --file \"$tmp/communicate.md\" --json \"$tmp/communicate.json\" --failure-log \"$tmp/failure_log.json\" system-status\n```\n- Expected exit codes:\n  - first `consume`: non-zero (`1`)\n  - `system-status` after JSON repair: `0`\n- PASS criteria:\n  - first call surfaces `SYSTEM_BLOCKED`\n  - repaired JSON clears blocked state deterministically\n\n4. Step 4: Concurrent UI + scanner contention probe\n- Command:\n```bash\npython3 -m unittest commscribe.tests.test_communicate_ui.CommunicateUiTests.test_concurrent_set_input_and_consume_no_queue_clobber -v\n```\n- Expected exit code: `0`\n- PASS criteria:\n  - test reports `ok`\n  - no queue/index marker loss\n  - no stale overwrite in concurrent path\n\n5. Step 5: Confirm Makefile target integration (if used)\n- Command:\n```bash\nls -1 | rg '^[Mm]akefile$'\n```\n- Expected exit code:\n  - `0` if Makefile exists\n  - non-zero if absent\n- PASS criteria:\n  - If Makefile exists and you rely on make: ensure targets `communicate`, `communicate-ui`, `communicate-orchestrate` are present.\n  - If absent: direct `python3 commscribe/scripts/...` invocation is still valid.\n\n## Operational Cautions\n\n- Missing Makefile target matters only when your team expects `make` entrypoints; it does not affect runtime correctness.\n- Lock serialization becomes noticeable when many writes contend on the same lock file.\n- Contention behavior is correctness-safe (fail-closed with timeout), primarily performance-impacting.\n\n## Scaling Threshold Estimate\n\n- Low request volume: near-immediate operations; deterministic and stable.\n- Moderate request volume: occasional lock wait/retry; behavior remains deterministic.\n- Heavy concurrent UI use: increased contention/timeouts; degradation is graceful (explicit failures), not silent corruption.\n\n## Reuse Boundary Statement\n\n- Suitable for:\n  - solo developer projects\n  - small teams\n  - AI-heavy dev workflows with bounded concurrent writers\n- Not yet optimized for:\n  - high-concurrency multi-user server environments\n  - distributed deployments\n\n## Final Reuse Readiness\n\n- Safe with validation checklist\n- Confidence: High",
      "evidence": "Evidence basis:\n- Prior invariant and reproducibility probes in this host project remain passing.\n- Runtime test suite status: 15/15 passing.\n- Host Makefile check run in this project root returned no Makefile present, confirming the operational caution context.\n\nCommands referenced in checklist are the same validated scanner and test entrypoints used throughout commscribe verification.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "problem_type: descriptive"
