      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Instruct Codex to update the communicate UI so it can produce and link directly to\n  specific request identifiers (REQ-numbers), enabling navigation to the associated\n  objective, execution details, evidence, and transcripts.\n\ndirective_to_codex: |\n  We need the local communicate UI to support deep linking to individual request\n  records by REQ number. Implement the ability to click or navigate to a URL that\n  directly displays the request\u2019s details.\n\n  Requirements:\n\n    1. URL Binding\n       - Define a route or hash fragment scheme so that URLs like\n         `/communicate?req=REQ-20260212-XXXX` or `#/REQ-20260212-XXXX` load the\n         corresponding request block.\n       - The UI must update the browser history/state so that links are shareable.\n\n    2. Request Detail View\n       - Add a dedicated section or view pane for a single request\u2019s full content:\n           * Objective\n           * Assumptions/constraints\n           * Plan/ack\n           * Execution logs\n           * Evidence pointers\n           * Status\n       - The view must render the structured content cleanly.\n\n    3. Navigation Elements\n       - In the request list, make REQ numbers clickable links.\n       - Ensure link targets scroll to or render the detail view for the specific REQ.\n       - Optionally add breadcrumbs or back navigation.\n\n    4. Canonical Link Generation\n       - Provide UI affordance that copies a stable link for a given REQ to the clipboard.\n\n    5. Browser-level Parameters\n       - Support reading and applying the selected REQ from query parameters or hash\n         on initial page load.\n\n    6. State Synchronization\n       - Ensure the UI stays in sync with the communicate.json/communicate.md canonical\n         store when navigating between REQs.\n\n    7. Accessibility & Usability\n       - Provide appropriate focus management when jumping to a detail view.\n       - Use standards-compliant link markup (<a href=\"\u2026\">) for shareable URLs. :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}\n\n  Deliverables:\n\n    - UI code updates (HTML/JS/CSS) for detail view and routing.\n    - Updates to communicate UI server/server logic if needed to support dynamic routes.\n    - Updated tests verifying that:\n        * REQ links render\n        * Navigation to a REQ shows correct content\n        * Query/hash parameters load correct REQ\n    - Documentation of the link scheme in README or UI guide.\n\nconstraints:\n  - No change to the underlying canonical data format.\n  - Maintain lock and atomic write guarantees during UI interactions.\n  - UI changes must not bypass scanner authority.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Add deep-linkable REQ routing and detail pane in UI, expose request-list/detail API endpoints from UI server, keep scanner-authority write path, add tests for link/navigation loading, and document URL scheme.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T04:33:14+00:00 Started UI deep-link implementation for REQ-specific detail navigation and canonical link generation.\n- 2026-02-13T04:36:19+00:00 Implemented REQ deep-link routing and detail UI, added request API endpoints in UI server, updated docs, and validated with expanded 18-test suite.",
      "outputs": "Implemented communicate UI deep-linking and REQ detail navigation without changing canonical data format.\n\nWhat was added\n\n1) URL binding + shareable state\n- Supported request selection from query param and hash fragment:\n  - `/communicate?req=REQ-...`\n  - `/#/REQ-...`\n- Browser history is updated with `history.pushState` when selecting REQs.\n- Added server-side selection parsing helper to keep URL semantics explicit.\n\n2) Request detail view\n- Added dedicated request detail pane showing:\n  - Objective\n  - Assumptions/constraints\n  - Plan/ack\n  - Execution logs\n  - Outputs\n  - Evidence\n  - Full transcript\n- Added focus management (`tabindex=-1` heading focus) when navigating to a detail.\n\n3) Navigation elements\n- Added request list pane with clickable REQ links (`<a href=\"?req=...\">`).\n- Clicking REQs renders the selected detail view.\n- Added \u201cBack To List\u201d control.\n\n4) Canonical link generation\n- Added \u201cCopy REQ Link\u201d action that writes stable URL to clipboard for selected REQ.\n\n5) Browser-level parameters on initial load\n- Initial load now reads query/hash to select REQ immediately.\n- `popstate`/`hashchange` listeners keep navigation behavior consistent.\n\n6) State synchronization with canonical store\n- Added UI server API endpoints backed by canonical JSON:\n  - `GET /api/requests` (summary list)\n  - `GET /api/request/<REQ_ID>` (full detail)\n- Existing `/api/thread` still serves input pad/document, now also returns parsed selected REQ.\n- UI refresh loop continues syncing with canonical state.\n\n7) Authority and safety constraints preserved\n- No UI bypass of scanner authority for writes.\n- Input pad writes still route through scanner `set-input` and shared lock/atomic path.\n- No canonical data schema changes.\n\nFiles updated\n- `commscribe/scripts/start_communicate_ui.py`\n- `commscribe/ui/index.html`\n- `commscribe/tests/test_communicate_ui.py`\n- `commscribe/README.md`",
      "evidence": "Key implementation references:\n- URL/query/hash parsing + request APIs:\n  - `commscribe/scripts/start_communicate_ui.py` (`selected_req_from_url`, `load_requests_from_json`, `/api/requests`, `/api/request/<id>`, `/communicate` route)\n- Frontend deep-link + detail rendering:\n  - `commscribe/ui/index.html` (`parseSelectedReqFromLocation`, request list links, `navigateToReq`, `copy-link`, detail pane renderers)\n- Tests added/updated:\n  - `commscribe/tests/test_communicate_ui.py`\n    - query/hash parsing\n    - request loading from JSON\n    - link/routing script presence\n    - concurrency and lock-path regressions\n\nValidation command run:\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v`\n- Result: `18/18` passing.\n\nREADME documentation update:\n- Added deep-link scheme under Optional Local UI section.",
