      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Refine the communicate UI layout and styling so the INPUT PAD text area\n  aligns correctly within the main container column and uses a clearer,\n  more intentional visual color treatment.\n\ndirective_to_codex: |\n  The communicate UI needs minor visual refinement.\n\n  1. Layout Alignment\n     - The INPUT PAD textarea must align with the same container column\n       as the rest of the content.\n     - Remove any overflow, negative margins, or width mismatches.\n     - Ensure consistent horizontal padding.\n     - Ensure responsiveness across:\n         * Desktop\n         * Tablet\n         * Narrow viewport\n     - Textarea width must be constrained to container max-width\n       and not exceed it.\n\n  2. Spacing Consistency\n     - Ensure vertical spacing above and below INPUT PAD matches\n       section spacing elsewhere.\n     - Align label, textarea, and submit button cleanly.\n     - Avoid full-viewport width stretch if container is centered.\n\n  3. Visual Treatment\n     - Adjust color scheme for INPUT PAD section so it:\n         * Is visually distinct from request list\n         * Does not overpower the interface\n         * Remains readable\n     - Consider:\n         * Subtle background tint\n         * Border accent\n         * Soft shadow\n         * Status-aware accent color (optional)\n\n  4. Design Constraints\n     - Keep styling minimal and clean.\n     - No heavy frameworks.\n     - Preserve existing functionality.\n     - Avoid inline styles; use consistent CSS structure.\n\n  5. Validation\n     - Confirm:\n         * No layout shift on submission.\n         * No overflow scrollbars introduced.\n         * No regression in REQ detail view.\n         * No JS breakage.\n\ndeliverables:\n  - Updated HTML/CSS.\n  - Screenshot-ready layout consistency.\n  - No runtime behavior changes.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Refine communicate UI layout/styling for INPUT PAD alignment, spacing, and subtle visual distinction while preserving behavior and responsive rendering.",
