      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Add a table of contents (TOC) section to communicate.md that\n  generates internal anchor links to individual REQ blocks,\n  allowing navigation within the Markdown document itself.\n\ndirective_to_codex: |\n  We want communicate.md to include a navigable Table of Contents\n  that links to each REQ block within the same document.\n\n  Requirements:\n\n    1. Anchor Strategy\n       - Each REQ block must have a stable anchor ID.\n       - Format example:\n           ## REQ-20260212-123456\n         or\n           <a id=\"REQ-20260212-123456\"></a>\n           ## REQ-20260212-123456\n       - Anchor IDs must exactly match the REQ number.\n\n    2. TOC Section\n       - Add a section near the top of communicate.md:\n           ## Request Index\n       - Under it, generate a list:\n           - [REQ-20260212-123456](#REQ-20260212-123456) \u2014 DONE\n           - [REQ-20260212-123457](#REQ-20260212-123457) \u2014 BLOCKED\n       - Include:\n           * Status\n           * Short objective summary (first line of request)\n\n    3. Automation\n       - The TOC must be auto-generated or updated by communicate_scan.py.\n       - It must not require manual edits.\n       - Updating the TOC must not modify historical REQ content.\n\n    4. Idempotence\n       - Re-running communicate with no new changes must not reorder or rewrite the TOC unnecessarily.\n       - Preserve stable ordering (chronological by REQ id).\n\n    5. Integrity Constraints\n       - Do not break existing markdown rendering.\n       - Do not mutate canonical JSON.\n       - Do not alter REQ block content.\n       - Fail closed if anchor mismatch detected.\n\n    6. Test Coverage\n       - Add test ensuring:\n           * New REQ automatically appears in TOC.\n           * Status updates reflect in TOC.\n           * Internal links correctly match anchors.\n           * No duplicate entries appear on rerun.\n\ndeliverables:\n  - Updated communicate_scan.py logic for TOC rendering.\n  - Updated communicate.md template structure.\n  - Regression tests.\n  - Documentation note describing anchor and TOC format.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Add auto-generated Request Index section and stable per-REQ anchors in markdown sync, enforce anchor integrity checks, and add regression tests for TOC update/status/link/idempotence behavior.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T04:45:08+00:00 Implemented request-index markers, REQ anchor rendering, TOC generation logic, integrity checks, and regression coverage; validated with full test suite.",
      "outputs": "Implemented auto-generated in-document REQ navigation for `communicate.md`.\n\nWhat changed\n\n1) Anchor strategy\n- Each rendered REQ block now includes a stable anchor that exactly matches request id:\n  - `<a id=\"REQ-...\"></a>`\n- Anchor is generated by `communicate_scan.py` during queue rendering.\n\n2) TOC section\n- Added `## Request Index` near top of `communicate.md` with managed markers:\n  - `<!-- REQUEST_INDEX_START -->`\n  - `<!-- REQUEST_INDEX_END -->`\n- The section is auto-generated with entries:\n  - `[REQ-...](#REQ-...) \u2014 STATUS \u2014 <first non-empty request line>`\n\n3) Automation\n- `communicate_scan.py` now renders the Request Index during markdown sync.\n- No manual editing required; index refresh occurs on normal lifecycle mutations.\n\n4) Idempotence and ordering\n- Index ordering follows request list order (chronological append order).\n- No-op consume path does not rewrite markdown; index remains stable.\n\n5) Integrity constraints\n- Canonical JSON schema/format unchanged.\n- REQ field content is unchanged; only anchor line added at block start in markdown rendering.\n- Added fail-closed anchor mismatch detection while parsing markdown blocks.\n\n6) Test coverage\n- Added regression tests ensuring:\n  - new REQ appears in Request Index\n  - status updates reflected in index\n  - internal link target matches anchor id\n  - no duplicate index entries on no-op rerun\n\nDeliverables completed\n- Updated scanner TOC/anchor logic.\n- Updated `communicate.md` template structure with Request Index markers.\n- Added regression tests.\n- Added README note documenting anchor/index format.",
      "evidence": "Files updated:\n- `commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py`\n  - Added Request Index markers/constants\n  - Added anchor mismatch structural validation\n  - Added per-REQ anchor rendering\n  - Added request index renderer and markdown sync wiring\n- `commscribe/communicate.md`\n  - Added `## Request Index` section and managed markers\n- `commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py`\n  - Added `test_request_index_updates_with_request_status_and_anchor`\n  - Added `test_request_index_no_duplicates_on_noop_rerun`\n- `commscribe/README.md`\n  - Added markdown navigation format note\n\nValidation:\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v`\n- Result: `20/20` passing.",
