      "request_id": "REQ-20260212-230227",
      "status": "DONE",
      "author": "USER",
      "created_at": "2026-02-13T05:02:27+00:00",
      "last_updated_at": "2026-02-13T05:05:26+00:00",
      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Create a zero-modification structural inventory of the host repository and output\n  a polished interactive HTML report that categorizes the project\u2019s files/dirs,\n  highlights entropy/redundancy signals, and supports filtering, search, and basic\n  visualization\u2014without performing any cleanup actions.\n\ncommunicate_request_block_text: |\n  ## REQ: Project Structural Inventory + Interactive HTML Report (NO CHANGES)\n\n  ### Objective\n  Produce a complete, categorized inventory of this repository and generate an\n  interactive, polished HTML report for browsing and analysis. Do not modify,\n  move, rename, or delete any project files as part of this request.\n\n  ### Hard Constraints (Binding)\n  - NO cleanup actions: no moves/renames/deletes/content edits to existing project files.\n  - Read-only analysis: inventory and reporting only.\n  - Any generated artifacts must be written to a dedicated output directory\n    (e.g., `reports/` or `development_docs/reports/`) and must not affect runtime behavior.\n  - Do not add new CI gates or modify pipelines in this request.\n\n  ### Inventory Scope\n  Enumerate and classify files and directories into these categories:\n\n  1) Runtime Core\n  2) Product Logic (UI/business/data/alerts)\n  3) Infrastructure / CI\n  4) Tests (code)\n  5) Test Artifacts (generated outputs)\n  6) Audit / Compliance Artifacts (DRA, verification, phase docs)\n  7) Development Docs (handoffs, notes, session logs)\n  8) Operational Artifacts (logs, metrics dumps, generated operational reports)\n  9) Archive Candidates (duplicates, superseded, stale, experiments)\n\n  For each category, report:\n  - counts (files/dirs)\n  - size totals\n  - top subtrees by size and count\n  - naming/pattern signals (date-stamped docs, repeated \u201clatest/status\u201d, duplicates)\n  - ownership clarity (authoritative vs derived)\n  - redundancy risk (Low/Medium/High)\n  - cleanup priority candidate (Low/Medium/High) \u2014 advisory only (no actions)\n\n  ### \u201cEntropy Signals\u201d to Detect (Read-only)\n  - Root-level status/audit doc sprawl (multiple competing \u201clatest/status/phase\u201d docs)\n  - Large accumulation of generated artifacts under logs/test_results/etc\n  - Duplicate or near-duplicate docs by naming convention (date suffixes, copies)\n  - Mixed-purpose directories (runtime + docs + artifacts interleaved)\n  - Inconsistent naming schemes for audits/reports/tests\n\n  ### Interactive HTML Report Requirements\n  Output: a single entry HTML file (plus local assets) that is viewable offline.\n\n  Must include:\n  - A left navigation panel (directory tree + category filters)\n  - Search box (path/name substring)\n  - Filter controls:\n      * category\n      * file type/extension\n      * size ranges\n      * modified-time buckets\n      * \u201cderived vs authoritative\u201d tag\n  - Sortable tables:\n      * largest files\n      * largest directories\n      * most dense directories by file count\n      * top duplication candidates (by heuristic)\n  - Visuals (lightweight but useful):\n      * bar chart: counts by category\n      * bar chart: size by category\n      * treemap OR collapsible tree for subtree sizes (choose whichever is simplest offline)\n      * timeline histogram for modified times (coarse buckets)\n  - A \u201cFindings\u201d panel summarizing:\n      * major entropy hotspots\n      * likely consolidation targets\n      * advisory cleanup priorities (no execution)\n\n  UI quality constraints:\n  - Clean, modern styling (readable typography, consistent spacing).\n  - No external network dependencies (no CDN). Bundle any JS/CSS locally.\n  - Fast enough to open and interact with on a typical repo size.\n\n  ### Output Location (Binding)\n  Write artifacts only under:\n    - `reports/inventory/` (preferred)\n  with:\n    - `reports/inventory/index.html`\n    - `reports/inventory/data.json` (if needed)\n    - `reports/inventory/assets/*` (if needed)\n\n  Do not write anywhere else.\n\n  ### Implementation Guidance (Allowed)\n  - You may implement a small Python script to scan the repo and produce a JSON dataset.\n  - The HTML can load that JSON locally and render UI components.\n  - Prefer minimal dependencies; if you add any, justify and pin them.\n  - Provide a command to regenerate the report (e.g., `python scripts/generate_inventory_report.py`).\n\n  ### Evidence Requirements\n  In the request output/evidence, include:\n  - exact commands run\n  - output file paths created\n  - a brief description of data schema used for the report\n  - proof no project files were modified (e.g., write locations and a brief explanation)\n\n  ### Completion Criteria\n  - Inventory dataset generated.\n  - Offline interactive HTML report generated and opens correctly.\n  - Report includes filters, searchable tables, and basic visuals.\n  - No existing project files modified outside the report output directory.\n\nformat_notes:\n  - Paste the full block above into INPUT PAD as a single request.\n  - Run `communicate` once to process.\n\nconstraints:\n  - Do not conflate \u201cinventory\u201d with \u201ccleanup.\u201d This request is strictly read-only analysis.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Generate a zero-modification structural inventory and offline interactive HTML report under reports/inventory only, including category filters/search/sort/visual summaries and entropy findings, with reproducible command and evidence.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T05:02:49+00:00 Started read-only repository inventory/report implementation constrained to reports/inventory outputs only.\n- 2026-02-13T05:05:09+00:00 Generated offline structural inventory dataset and interactive HTML report under reports/inventory with no cleanup actions.",
      "outputs": "Created a zero-modification structural inventory report pipeline with offline interactive HTML browsing, written only under `reports/inventory/`.\n\nGenerated artifacts\n- `reports/inventory/index.html`\n- `reports/inventory/data.json`\n- `reports/inventory/generate_inventory_report.py` (regeneration script)\n\nRegeneration command\n```bash\npython3 reports/inventory/generate_inventory_report.py\n```\n\nWhat the interactive report includes\n- Left navigation panel:\n  - top-level directory tree buttons (prefix filter)\n  - search by path substring\n  - filters for category, extension, size range, modified-time bucket, ownership tag\n- Sortable tables:\n  - largest files\n  - largest directories\n  - most dense directories by file count\n  - duplication candidates (heuristic)\n- Visuals (offline, no CDN):\n  - bar chart: counts by category\n  - bar chart: size by category\n  - modified-time histogram\n  - top-level tree filter controls for subtree exploration\n- Findings panel:\n  - entropy hotspots\n  - likely consolidation targets\n  - advisory cleanup priorities (analysis only; no execution)\n\nCategory coverage in dataset\n1. Runtime Core\n2. Product Logic\n3. Infrastructure / CI\n4. Tests (code)\n5. Test Artifacts (generated outputs)\n6. Audit / Compliance Artifacts\n7. Development Docs\n8. Operational Artifacts\n9. Archive Candidates\n\nNotes on constraints\n- No cleanup actions were performed (no moves/renames/deletes).\n- No canonical runtime behavior was changed.\n- Inventory is read-only analysis; report generation writes only in `reports/inventory/`.",
      "evidence": "Commands run\n1) python3 reports/inventory/generate_inventory_report.py\n2) python3 - <<'PY'\n   import json\n   from pathlib import Path\n   d=json.loads(Path('reports/inventory/data.json').read_text())\n   print(sorted(d['summary'].keys()))\n   print(len(d['categories']), len(d['files']))\n   print(sorted(d['tables'].keys()))\n   print(sorted(d['charts'].keys()))\n   PY\n3) find reports/inventory -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort\n\nObserved outputs\n- reports/inventory/data.json\n- reports/inventory/index.html\n- reports/inventory/generate_inventory_report.py\n\nData schema summary\n- `summary`: file/dir counts and total bytes\n- `categories`: per-category counts/sizes/top subtrees/signals/risk/priority\n- `files`: path-level inventory records with size/ext/mtime/category/ownership\n- `tables`: precomputed largest-files, largest-dirs, dense-dirs, duplicate candidates\n- `charts`: count/size by category, modified-time buckets, top-level tree counts\n- `findings`: entropy hotspot summaries with severity labels\n\nProof boundary\n- All generated report artifacts are under `reports/inventory/`.\n- No cleanup operations were executed.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "problem_type: prescriptive"
