      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n    1) Propose generating a README for the inventory report that includes instructions on viewing the interactive HTML without double-clicking, and\n    2) Produces that README file as part of the request.\ncommunicate_request_block_text: |\n  ## REQ: Inventory Report Usage README for Interactive HTML Report\n\n  ### Objective\n  Produce a README for the inventory report that explains how to open\n  `reports/inventory/index.html` in a browser without relying on double-clicking,\n  including:\n    - How to serve the report via a simple local HTTP server\n    - How to configure static serving if necessary\n    - Any OS/browser considerations\n    - Recommended script/command to run\n\n  ### Deliverables\n  1. A file at:\n       reports/inventory/USAGE_README.md\n     that contains clear, step-by-step instructions for:\n       * Running a local HTTP server to serve the HTML\n       * Opening the report in a browser via HTTP\n       * Verifying that interactive charts/filters work\n       * Optional automated regenerate + serve script\n\n  ### Requirements\n  - The README must be written in Markdown.\n  - Include example commands (e.g., Python built-in HTTP server,\n    alternative tooling if preferred).\n  - All instructions must be clear and usable by another developer.\n  - Do not modify any existing source code or canonical inventory outputs.\n\n  ### Evidence\n  - Include the exact commands needed to serve and view the report.\n  - Include example output snippets showing how the server indicates\n    where to access the report.\n  - Include a note about avoiding double-click browser file access and\n    why serving over HTTP improves interactive behavior.\n\n  ### Constraints\n  - Only create `reports/inventory/USAGE_README.md`; do not add any\n    other files beyond this request\u2019s scope.\n\nformat_notes:\n  - Paste the entire block above into the INPUT PAD.\n  - Then run `communicate` to process.",
