      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T05:10:20+00:00 Started authoring inventory usage README with HTTP serving guidance and interaction verification steps.\n- 2026-02-13T05:10:50+00:00 Created reports/inventory/USAGE_README.md with HTTP serving workflow, verification steps, command examples, and troubleshooting notes.",
      "outputs": "Created `reports/inventory/USAGE_README.md` with step-by-step instructions for viewing the interactive inventory report over local HTTP.\n\nContents included:\n- Why HTTP serving is recommended over double-click `file://` opening\n- Python built-in server commands (`python3 -m http.server`)\n- Browser URL targets (`http://127.0.0.1:<port>/index.html`)\n- Interactivity verification checklist (filters/search/charts/sorting/tree filter)\n- Regenerate-then-serve command sequence\n- Optional Node static serving command (`npx serve`)\n- OS/browser notes and troubleshooting\n\nScope respected:\n- Only `reports/inventory/USAGE_README.md` was created.\n- No source code or canonical inventory outputs were modified.",
      "evidence": "Exact commands documented in README:\n1) cd reports/inventory\n2) python3 -m http.server 8765\n3) Open http://127.0.0.1:8765/index.html\n\nAlternative command documented:\n- npx serve reports/inventory -l 8765\n\nExample server output snippet documented:\n- Serving HTTP on 0.0.0.0 port 8765 (http://0.0.0.0:8765/) ...\n\nCreated file path:\n- reports/inventory/USAGE_README.md\n\nConstraint check:\n- Request scope honored by creating only the specified README file.",
