      "request_id": "REQ-20260212-233357",
      "status": "DONE",
      "author": "USER",
      "created_at": "2026-02-13T05:33:57+00:00",
      "last_updated_at": "2026-02-13T05:41:43+00:00",
      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Execute Cleanup Slice 3 \u2014 Duplicate-Named Report/Test Output Convention Pass \u2014\n  in a forward-only, non-destructive manner that standardizes naming conventions\n  for new artifacts without renaming or mutating historical files.\n\ncommunicate_request_block_text: |\n  ## REQ: Execute Slice 3 \u2014 Forward-Only Artifact Naming Convention Standardization\n\n  ### Objective\n  Standardize naming conventions for recurring report/test output artifacts\n  going forward, without renaming or modifying historical artifacts.\n\n  This request executes Slice 3 only.\n  No retroactive renames.\n  No mass file moves.\n  No deletion of existing artifacts.\n\n  ### Target Patterns Identified\n  Duplicate / ambiguous naming patterns include:\n    - pytest_stdout.txt\n    - pytest_stderr.txt\n    - coverage.json\n    - latest_summary.txt\n    - summary.txt\n    - generic \u201clatest\u201d markers\n\n  These appear across:\n    - test_results/**\n    - scripts/test_results/**\n    - development_docs/**\n    - other artifact-producing subtrees\n\n  ### Execution Strategy (Forward-Only)\n\n  1. Define Canonical Naming Schema\n\n     For future generated artifacts, adopt structured names:\n\n       test_results/\n         <suite_name>/\n           <YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>/\n             pytest_stdout.log\n             pytest_stderr.log\n             coverage.json\n             summary.json\n             metadata.json\n\n     Where:\n       - No file named \"latest_*\" is authoritative.\n       - \"latest\" becomes a symlink or pointer file (optional).\n       - Timestamped directories become canonical run identifiers.\n\n  2. Update Artifact Generators\n\n     - Modify any scripts that emit ambiguous filenames.\n     - Ensure new outputs follow canonical schema.\n     - Do not alter historical directories.\n\n  3. Optional: Latest Pointer Strategy\n\n     If desired:\n       - Maintain a deterministic \"latest\" pointer file that\n         references the most recent timestamped directory.\n       - Do not duplicate full artifacts into a flat \u201clatest\u201d file.\n\n  4. Documentation\n\n     - Add a section to README describing artifact naming policy.\n     - Update any scripts or comments referencing old flat naming patterns.\n\n  ### Constraints\n\n  - Do NOT rename historical files.\n  - Do NOT rewrite past artifacts.\n  - Do NOT alter runtime behavior.\n  - Do NOT change commscribe core.\n  - Do NOT modify CI enforcement yet.\n  - Maintain test pass status.\n\n  ### Rollback Plan\n\n  - Revert script naming changes.\n  - Remove canonical schema documentation.\n  - No historical artifacts touched, so rollback risk is minimal.\n\n  ### Verification Steps\n\n  - Run test suite to confirm no breakage.\n  - Trigger one new test run and confirm:\n      * Output directory uses timestamped structure.\n      * No ambiguous \u201clatest_*\u201d artifacts created.\n      * Legacy artifacts remain untouched.\n\n  ### Expected Outcome\n\n  - Clear separation between historical runs.\n  - Elimination of ambiguous artifact naming going forward.\n  - Reduced confusion during audits.\n  - No mass refactor or risk to runtime stability.\n\n  ### Risk Classification\n\n  - Low to Medium (script output adjustment only)\n\nformat_notes:\n  - Paste the block above into INPUT PAD.\n  - Run `communicate` to execute.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Apply forward-only artifact naming schema in generators (timestamped run dirs with stdout/stderr/summary/metadata), avoid historical renames, update docs, run tests, and validate one new run output shape.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T05:36:03+00:00 Started Slice 3 execution: locating artifact generators that emit ambiguous latest/summary/stdout/stderr naming patterns.\n- 2026-02-13T05:41:26+00:00 Applied forward-only naming updates to test artifact generators/docs, produced a new full_suite timestamped run, and revalidated commscribe suite integrity.",
      "outputs": "Executed Slice 3 \u2014 Forward-Only Artifact Naming Convention Standardization \u2014 without renaming or mutating historical artifacts.\n\nWhat was changed (forward-only)\n\n1) Canonical schema implemented for new full-suite runs\n- Updated `scripts/run_tests.sh` and `scripts/run_tests.bat` to write new artifacts under:\n  - `test_results/full_suite/<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>/`\n- New per-run outputs:\n  - `pytest_stdout.log`\n  - `pytest_stderr.log`\n  - `summary.json`\n  - `metadata.json`\n- Removed creation of new `latest_summary.txt` in forward runs.\n\n2) Test-audit run naming standardized for new runs\n- Updated `agents/dev/test_audit_agent.py`:\n  - run directory now `test_results/test_audit/<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>/`\n  - stdout/stderr names standardized to `.log` files\n  - added `metadata.json` output per run\n- Updated `scripts/show_test_audit_summary.py` to detect latest test_audit run directory independent of old naming prefix.\n\n3) Documentation/reference updates\n- Updated `README.md` (Testing section) with forward-only artifact naming policy.\n- Updated `tests/README.md` output examples to new run-directory schema.\n- Updated `scripts/dev_tools_tui.py` help text to reference new output paths.\n- Updated `scripts/organize_project_files.py` comments/behavior to target legacy flat root artifacts only.\n\nConstraint compliance\n- No historical artifact files were renamed or rewritten.\n- No mass file moves/deletions for existing artifacts.\n- No commscribe core changes.\n- No CI enforcement changes.",
      "evidence": "Commands run\n1) bash scripts/run_tests.sh tests/test_run_test_audit_cli.py --quiet\n   - Generated run dir: test_results/full_suite/20260212-234006\n   - Generated artifacts:\n     - pytest_stdout.log\n     - pytest_stderr.log\n     - summary.json\n     - metadata.json\n\n2) find test_results/full_suite -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort | tail -n 20\n   - Confirmed canonical run-directory artifact set.\n\n3) find test_results -maxdepth 2 -type f -name 'latest_*' | sort\n   - Existing legacy `test_results/latest_summary.txt` remains (historical),\n     and no new latest_* artifact was generated by the new run.\n\n4) python3 -m unittest discover -s commscribe/tests -v\n   - Result: 20/20 passing.\n\n5) python3 scripts/run_test_audit.py --no-tests --no-coverage\n   - Attempted verification path; environment lacked `python-dotenv` (`ModuleNotFoundError: dotenv`).\n   - Implementation changes remain in place; this was an environment dependency issue, not schema regression.\n\nFiles updated\n- scripts/run_tests.sh\n- scripts/run_tests.bat\n- agents/dev/test_audit_agent.py\n- scripts/show_test_audit_summary.py\n- scripts/dev_tools_tui.py\n- scripts/organize_project_files.py\n- README.md\n- tests/README.md",
