      "last_updated_at": "2026-02-13T16:11:14+00:00",
      "request_text": "problem_type: descriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Diagnose why a manual trade was allowed when:\n    1) daily trade limit was already reached, and\n    2) max open positions limit was already reached.\n\ndirective_to_codex: |\n  We need a strict diagnostic analysis of why a manual trade was permitted\n  despite configured risk constraints:\n\n    - Daily trade limit reached\n    - Max open positions limit reached\n\n  Do not assume the constraint system is working.\n  Trace the full execution path.\n\n  Investigation Requirements:\n\n    1. Constraint Enforcement Location\n       - Where are daily trade limits enforced?\n       - Where are max position limits enforced?\n       - Are these checks in:\n           * strategy layer?\n           * order execution layer?\n           * API wrapper?\n           * UI layer?\n       - Are they enforced before or after order submission?\n\n    2. Manual vs Automated Path\n       - Is manual trade submission routed through the same validation\n         pipeline as automated trades?\n       - If not, identify divergence point.\n       - Identify whether manual UI bypasses risk engine.\n\n    3. Source of Truth\n       - What component calculates:\n           * daily trade count?\n           * open positions count?\n       - Is it reading from:\n           * internal state?\n           * broker API?\n           * cached memory?\n       - Could state have been stale?\n\n    4. Enforcement Mode\n       - Are limits:\n           * soft (warn only)?\n           * hard (block order submission)?\n       - Is there a flag like `override=True` or admin bypass?\n\n    5. Timing / Race Conditions\n       - Was the daily limit incremented after execution instead of before?\n       - Is position count checked before fills settle?\n       - Could asynchronous update timing allow one extra order?\n\n    6. Broker-Level Behavior\n       - Is this enforced internally only?\n       - Does the broker itself enforce max position constraints?\n       - If broker doesn\u2019t enforce, internal guard must.\n\n  Required Output:\n\n    - Exact code paths involved in manual order submission.\n    - Where limit checks are invoked (or not invoked).\n    - Whether the constraint system is bypassed for manual trades.\n    - Whether this is:\n        * design gap\n        * logic bug\n        * state sync issue\n        * race condition\n    - Severity classification.\n    - Recommended fix path (no implementation yet).\n\n  Constraints:\n    - No speculative answers.\n    - Cite file names and functions.\n    - Distinguish verified vs inferred behavior.\n    - Do not modify code during this diagnostic phase.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Trace manual trade submission path and risk limit enforcement locations for daily trade/open-position constraints, compare manual vs automated pipelines, classify root cause and severity, and provide fix path recommendations without code changes.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T16:02:55+00:00 Started code-path diagnostic for manual trade constraint bypass investigation.\n- 2026-02-13T16:11:05+00:00 Diagnostic findings (no code changes made):\n\n1) Root cause (confirmed): manual trade path bypasses RiskAgent guardrails.\n- API route /trade/manual directly delegates to coordinator manual_trade:\n  - server/routers/trading.py:38-43\n  - agents/coordinator.py:214-217\n- Coordinator manual_trade delegates to ExecutionAgent.execute_manual_trade:\n  - agents/coordinator.py:216\n- ExecutionAgent.execute_manual_trade explicitly documents bypass behavior and submits directly to broker without any RiskCheckPassed gate:\n  - agents/execution_agent.py:89-90 (\"bypasses risk checks\")\n  - agents/execution_agent.py:97-113 (manual buy submit)\n  - agents/execution_agent.py:129-134 (manual sell submit)\n\n2) Where daily/open-position limits are actually enforced.\n- These limits are enforced only inside RiskAgent._handle_signal (automated signal path):\n  - daily trade limit check: agents/risk_agent.py:108-111\n  - max open positions check (buy): agents/risk_agent.py:125-131 and 263-265\n- Execution of automated trades is subscribed to RiskCheckPassed events:\n  - agents/execution_agent.py:39 (subscribe)\n  - agents/execution_agent.py:46-88 (_handle_approved_trade)\n\n3) Source-of-truth and soft/hard enforcement characterization.\n- Current source-of-truth for MAX_DAILY_TRADES and MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS enforcement is RiskAgent logic, not broker.\n- AlpacaBroker/FakeBroker do not enforce these strategy limits:\n  - broker submit path: broker.py:163-197 (no daily/open-position policy checks)\n  - fake broker submit path: fake_broker.py:222-303 (checks buying power/available shares only)\n- Therefore these are hard-enforced only on automated path, soft/non-enforced on manual path.\n\n4) Timing/race observations.\n- Trade count increments after successful execution in both auto/manual paths:\n  - auto increment: agents/execution_agent.py:79-80\n  - manual increment: agents/execution_agent.py:148-149\n- Because manual path never performs pre-trade RiskAgent limit checks, limit violation can occur deterministically even without concurrency.\n- Additional timing risk exists generally if approvals/executions overlap because check and increment are not a single atomic operation at RiskAgent boundary; event bus publishes handlers sequentially per publish call, but separate events can still interleave over time:\n  - event publish behavior: agents/event_bus.py:66-107\n\n5) Broker behavior under limit breach.\n- Broker will accept/reject based on broker-side constraints (buying power, holdings, venue/account rules), not app-level MAX_DAILY_TRADES/MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS. Thus manual orders can execute despite internal policy limits.\n\nSeverity: HIGH\n- Policy controls can be bypassed via first-class API route (/trade/manual), causing deterministic non-compliance with configured risk limits.\n\nRecommended fix path (diagnostic only, not implemented):\nA) Route manual trades through same risk gate as automated trades (single policy authority).\n- Option 1: Create a manual-signal path that invokes RiskAgent checks before any submit.\n- Option 2: Extract shared risk validation into reusable method/service and invoke from both _handle_signal and execute_manual_trade.\nB) Keep broker as execution backend only; do not rely on broker for internal policy controls.\nC) Make check+reserve semantics explicit for daily trade count/open-position limit to minimize race window (atomic pre-commit or serialized execution queue).\nD) Add regression tests:\n- manual buy blocked when MAX_DAILY_TRADES reached\n- manual buy blocked when MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS reached\n- parity test: same input -> same allow/deny decision for manual vs auto path\n- concurrent manual+auto attempts around limit boundary",
      "outputs": "Completed diagnostic: manual trade risk-bypass confirmed with code-path evidence and remediation plan (no implementation).",
      "evidence": "Verified references: server/routers/trading.py:38-43; agents/coordinator.py:214-217; agents/execution_agent.py:89-90,97-113,129-134,148-149; agents/risk_agent.py:108-111,125-131,263-265; agents/event_bus.py:66-107; broker.py:163-197; fake_broker.py:222-303.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "problem_type: descriptive"
    },
