      "request_text": "problem_type: prescriptive\n\nobjective: >\n  Verify that request ordering has been updated so that:\n    - communicate.md lists requests in **descending (most-recent first)** order\n    - the Communicate UI displays requests in descending order by default\n\ncommunicate_request_block_text: |\n  ## REQ: Verify Descending Order for communicate.md and Communicate UI\n\n  ### Objective\n  Confirm that request ordering in both:\n    1) communicate.md (the canonical Markdown)\n    2) the Communicate UI list view\n  uses descending order (most recent at the top) by default.\n\n  This is a **verification only** request. Do not change sorting\n  behavior in this request.\n\n  ### Verification Steps\n\n  1. communicate.md\n     - Inspect the first several request blocks.\n     - Confirm that their timestamps and REQ identifiers decrease\n       from top to bottom.\n     - Confirm that the TOC Request Index lists entries in descending order.\n\n  2. Communicate UI\n     - Load the UI.\n     - Confirm that:\n         * Most recent requests appear at the top.\n         * No filter or toggle is required to see descending order by default.\n\n  3. Edge Cases\n     - Confirm that sorting holds when:\n         * There are more than 10 requests\n         * There are mixed DONE/BLOCKED/IN_PROGRESS statuses\n         * There are many archived older requests\n\n  4. Evidence Requirements\n     - For communicate.md: sample of the first 5 REQ IDs with timestamps\n     - For UI: screenshot/log of the visible ordering with 5 entries\n     - Explicit PASS/FAIL for each verification step\n\n  ### Success Criteria\n  - communicate.md is confirmed to be descending most-recent first\n  - UI default list is confirmed descending\n  - TOC respects descending order\n  - No behavioral change occurs\n\n  ### Constraints\n  - Verification only; no sorting logic modifications in this request.\n  - Do not alter any files.\n  - This request reports only.\n\nformat_notes:\n  - Paste