      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-13T17:17:08+00:00 Implemented descending-order behavior without mutating canonical JSON semantics.\n\nCode changes:\n1) Markdown render ordering (newest-first, deterministic)\n- Updated `commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py`:\n  - added `_request_sort_key` and `_render_ordered_requests`\n  - `_render_queue` now renders `_render_ordered_requests(requests)`\n  - `_render_request_index` now renders `_render_ordered_requests(requests)`\n  - `_render_index` now renders `_render_ordered_requests(requests)`\n- Canonical JSON `requests` array write path unchanged (append + state machine unchanged).\n\n2) UI default descending order + optional toggle\n- Updated `commscribe/ui/index.html`:\n  - added `sortMode` with default `newest`\n  - added `parseReqTimestamp` and `sortRequestList`\n  - `loadRequests` now applies sorted view order before rendering\n  - added optional `toggle-sort` button (`Sort: Newest` / `Sort: Oldest`)\n- UI sorting is view-only and does not mutate JSON.\n\n3) Regression tests added/updated\n- `commscribe/tests/test_communicate_scan.py`\n  - added `test_markdown_queue_and_index_render_newest_first_without_mutating_json_order`\n- `commscribe/tests/test_communicate_ui.py`\n  - extended UI structure checks for sort toggle and sort function wiring.",
