      "request_text": "Problem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nCreate a repeatable \u201cstakeholder demo path\u201d for the Market-Watch project using Cloudflare, such that non-technical stakeholders can access a stable demo URL (optionally Access-protected), while the demo remains isolated from production and can be rebuilt consistently.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n\nA single demo URL works end-to-end and is documented.\n\nDemo environment is isolated from production (separate hostname and/or separate env vars, secrets, and data).\n\nAccess control (if enabled) reliably gates the demo to an allowlist.\n\nSetup is reproducible from repo instructions with minimal manual steps.\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate (this sprint). Optimize for fastest reliable stakeholder demo with clean rollback.\n\nScope / Stakeholders:\n\nScope: Cloudflare configuration + repo changes needed to stand up a demo entry point.\n\nStakeholders: internal dev team + business stakeholders viewing the demo.\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n\nProduce a \u201cdemo path\u201d that is stable (not a random preview hash URL).\n\nKeep production and demo separated (hostnames, env vars, secrets, and data).\n\nAdd documentation and a quick-start checklist for maintainers.\n\nPrefer Cloudflare-native primitives (Pages/Workers/Access/Tunnel) over extra vendors.\nSoft:\n\nInfrastructure-as-code preferred if time permits (Terraform or wrangler-based scripts).\n\nUse path-based routing if feasible (e.g., /demo) but hostname-based demo is acceptable and usually simpler.\nIgnored (justified):\n\nFull SSO/IdP integration beyond Cloudflare Access defaults, unless already in use (keeps scope minimal).\n\nAssumptions:\n\n\u201cMarket-Watch\u201d is an existing app in this repo or deployable artifact (frontend and/or API).\n\nA domain is available in Cloudflare DNS (e.g., market-watch.example.com), or Pages project can be created.\n\nStakeholder access can be gated by email allowlist (Cloudflare Access).\n\nModel Frame:\nCloudflare deployment + routing + access gating + repo docs and scripts.\n\nComparisons Required:\nImplement one primary approach, but include a brief \u201cAlternatives\u201d section in docs comparing:\n\nPages + custom domain (recommended for frontend)\n\nWorkers-only app (if no frontend build)\n\nTunnel to private origin (if demo must hit internal services)\n\nUncertainty Requirements:\n\nClearly mark any placeholders requiring operator input (domain name, zone id, account id, allowed emails).\n\nDo not guess secrets or production endpoints; require explicit config.\n\nOut of Scope:\n\nProduct feature work inside Market-Watch unrelated to demo access.\n\nLarge redesign of CI/CD unless required for demo deploy.\n\nDeliverables:\n\ndocs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md\n\nWhat the demo is\n\nDemo URL(s)\n\nAccess policy behavior (who can get in)\n\nHow to deploy/update demo\n\nHow to disable demo fast\n\nTroubleshooting\n\nCloudflare deployment implementation (choose the simplest that fits this repo):\nA) If frontend/static site:\n\nCloudflare Pages project configuration\n\nCustom domain like demo.market-watch.<domain> OR staging.market-watch.<domain>\n\nOptional branch alias (e.g., \u201cdemo\u201d branch \u2192 demo hostname)\nB) If server/API:\n\nCloudflare Workers (wrangler) deployment\n\nRoute bound to demo hostname and/or /demo path\nC) If origin is private:\n\nCloudflare Tunnel config + public hostname route\n\nAccess app in front of hostname\n\nAccess control (if enabled):\n\nCloudflare Zero Trust Access application\n\nPath or hostname protection (prefer hostname demo.market-watch.<domain>; path-based allowed if required)\n\nAllow policy: email allowlist (config file placeholder)\n\nDeny by default\n\nRepo scripts/config:\n\n./scripts/demo/setup_cloudflare_demo.(sh|js) OR Makefile targets:\n\ndemo:setup\n\ndemo:deploy\n\ndemo:verify\n\nStore non-secret config in repo; secrets via Cloudflare env vars / secrets.\n\nImplementation Steps (execute):\n\nInspect repo to determine app shape:\n\nIs there a frontend build (e.g., Vite/Next/React) suitable for Pages?\n\nIs there a backend API needing Workers or Tunnel?\n\nIdentify current deploy method, if any.\n\nDecide primary demo topology (pick minimal viable):\n\nPreferred: demo hostname (demo.market-watch.<domain>) \u2192 Pages (frontend) and/or Workers (API).\n\nOnly use /demo path routing if hostname cannot be created.\n\nConfigure deployment:\n\nPages: create/update Pages config, set build command/output dir, set environment vars for demo.\n\nWorkers: create wrangler.toml with demo env, bind route to demo hostname and/or /demo path.\n\nConfigure Access (if enabled):\n\nCreate Access application protecting demo hostname/path.\n\nAdd allow policy (email allowlist).\n\nDocument how to update allowlist.\n\nVerification:\n\ndemo:verify script that checks:\n\nDNS resolves (if custom domain)\n\nHTTP returns expected gating (302 to Access or 200 if Access disabled)\n\nAfter auth (manual step), page loads and key endpoint health is OK\n\nAdd a small verification checklist in docs.\n\nProduce a \u201cfast disable\u201d plan:\n\nRemove Access app or disable policy\n\nRemove route or unbind custom domain\n\nRoll back Pages/Workers deployment to prior commit\n\nVerification Outcomes / Test Results (must produce):\n\nOutput results from demo:verify (command + observed status codes).\n\nIf Access enabled, show:\n\nunauthenticated request result (expected redirect/forbidden)\n\nauthenticated access confirmation (manual note)\n\nConfirm demo config is isolated (distinct env vars, no production secrets referenced).\n\nFiles to Create/Modify (expected):\n\ndocs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md\n\nscripts/demo/* (setup/deploy/verify)\n\nwrangler.toml and/or Pages config notes (as appropriate)\n\nAny minimal app config needed for demo env (e.g., .env.demo.example; no secrets committed)",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Assess repo deployment shape (frontend/backend), choose minimal Cloudflare-native demo topology, add demo docs + scripts + make targets with explicit placeholders and isolation controls, provide verification command flow and fast-disable plan.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-14T00:21:47+00:00 Implemented Cloudflare-based stakeholder demo path with reproducible repo assets (Tunnel + Access primary), isolated from production.\n\nCreated files:\n- docs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md\n- scripts/demo/setup_cloudflare_demo.sh\n- scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh\n- scripts/demo/verify_cloudflare_demo.sh\n- scripts/demo/disable_cloudflare_demo.sh\n- scripts/demo/cloudflare_demo.env.example\n- scripts/demo/access_allowlist_emails.txt.example\n- .env.demo.example\n\nPrimary topology selected:\n- C) Cloudflare Tunnel to private demo origin + optional Access allowlist gate.\n- Rationale: current project is FastAPI/server-backed; tunnel path requires minimal app change and supports full stack demo with stable hostname.\n\nWhat implementation provides:\n- Stable demo URL pattern (`demo.<domain>`) with explicit placeholders.\n- Isolation controls documented and templated:\n  - separate hostname\n  - separate `.env.demo`\n  - separate config/log paths under `data/demo` and `logs/demo`\n  - demo-only credentials expectation (paper/non-prod)\n- Access policy automation path in deploy script (if `CF_API_TOKEN`/account inputs provided).\n- Reproducible setup/deploy/verify/disable flow.\n- Fast-disable operational path and command.\n- Alternatives section in docs:\n  - Pages + custom domain\n  - Workers-only\n  - Tunnel (selected)\n\nVerification command outputs (executed):\n1) setup script\n- Command: `scripts/demo/setup_cloudflare_demo.sh`\n- Observed: template files created and next-step checklist emitted.\n\n2) verify script (local env probe)\n- Command: `scripts/demo/verify_cloudflare_demo.sh /tmp/cloudflare-demo-local.env`\n- Observed output:\n  - `DNS: PASS`\n  - `Unauthenticated status code: 000`\n  - `Unauthenticated gate check: FAIL`\n  - `Service-token authenticated status code: SKIPPED`\n  - `Overall: FAIL`\n- Interpretation: expected in current environment because no demo origin server is running on `127.0.0.1:18000` and no live Cloudflare route is configured here.\n\nEnvironment constraints encountered:\n- Cloudflare credentials/token/domain not available in this environment.\n- `uvicorn` not installed in this shell, so local origin app could not be started for a 200 health response check.\n\nNo production endpoints, secrets, or canonical runtime lifecycle semantics were changed.",
      "outputs": "Implemented a reproducible Cloudflare stakeholder demo path (Tunnel + optional Access), with isolation templates, setup/deploy/verify/disable scripts, and maintainer documentation.",
      "evidence": "Artifacts created: docs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md, scripts/demo/{setup_cloudflare_demo.sh,deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh,verify_cloudflare_demo.sh,disable_cloudflare_demo.sh,cloudflare_demo.env.example,access_allowlist_emails.txt.example}, .env.demo.example. Script sanity check: bash -n on all demo scripts passed. Verification run captured via scripts/demo/verify_cloudflare_demo.sh /tmp/cloudflare-demo-local.env: DNS PASS, unauth status 000, gate FAIL, auth SKIPPED, overall FAIL (no live origin/tunnel in this environment).",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
