      "created_at": "2026-02-14T02:48:53+00:00",
      "last_updated_at": "2026-02-14T02:51:30+00:00",
      "request_text": "codex> Diagnose and fix Cloudflare Tunnel error for Market-Watch demo\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nIdentify the root cause of the Cloudflare Tunnel failure and produce a minimal, deterministic fix so the Market-Watch app is reachable via the trycloudflare URL.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n\ncloudflared starts without DNS resolver errors.\n\nNo \u201cUnable to reach the origin service\u201d errors.\n\nVisiting the trycloudflare URL returns HTTP 200 from the Market-Watch app.\n\nLocal app reachable directly at its origin port before tunnel starts.\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate (debug + restore demo access).\n\nScope / Stakeholders:\n\nScope: Local dev machine, cloudflared config, and Market-Watch local server.\n\nStakeholders: Developer running demo + stakeholders waiting for link.\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n\nDo not modify production infrastructure.\n\nFix must work with temporary trycloudflare tunnel.\n\nMust verify local origin server is actually listening.\nSoft:\n\nKeep changes minimal.\nIgnored (justified):\n\nPermanent named tunnel setup (out of scope for immediate recovery).\n\nAssumptions:\n\nMarket-Watch app is expected to run locally on port 18000.\n\ncloudflared was started with origin http://127.0.0.1:18000.\n\nNo reverse proxy already bound to that port.\n\nModel Frame:\nRoot cause analysis: separate into DNS resolution failure vs origin connectivity failure.\n\nComparisons Required:\nCheck both:\n\nLocal origin not running\n\nWrong port binding\n\nFirewall / DNS failure\n\ncloudflared binary / network issue\n\nUncertainty Requirements:\n\nValidate each layer before moving on.\n\nDo not assume the app is running.\n\nOut of Scope:\n\nRefactoring Market-Watch.\n\nConverting to Pages/Workers deployment.\n\nRoot Cause Analysis (Based on Error)\n\nYou have two independent failures:\n\nDNS resolver failure\nlookup region1.v2.argotunnel.com: i/o timeout\n\u2192 Your machine cannot resolve Cloudflare\u2019s tunnel endpoint.\n\nOrigin connection refused\ndial tcp 127.0.0.1:18000: connectex: No connection could be made because the target machine actively refused it.\n\u2192 Nothing is listening on port 18000 locally.\n\nThe second error alone would break the tunnel even if DNS worked.\n\nStep 1 \u2014 Verify Local App Is Actually Running\n\nRun:\n\nWindows:\n\nnetstat -ano | findstr :18000\n\n\nMac/Linux:\n\nlsof -i :18000\n\n\nIf nothing is listening:\n\u2192 Your Market-Watch app is not running on port 18000.\n\nStart the app explicitly and confirm:\n\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:18000\n\n\nIf curl fails:\n\nWrong port\n\nApp crashed\n\nApp bound to different interface (e.g. 0.0.0.0:3000)\n\nIf your app runs on another port (e.g. 3000), start tunnel correctly:\n\ncloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:3000\n\n\nDo not assume 18000 unless verified.\n\nStep 2 \u2014 Fix DNS Resolver Error\n\nThe DNS error suggests one of:\n\nNo internet connectivity\n\nCorporate firewall blocking outbound\n\nLocal DNS resolver misconfigured\n\nVPN interference\n\nTest DNS:\n\nnslookup region1.v2.argotunnel.com\n\n\nIf that fails:\n\nSwitch DNS to 1.1.1.1 temporarily\n\nDisable VPN\n\nCheck firewall\n\nQuick Windows fix:\nSet adapter DNS to:\nPrimary: 1.1.1.1\nSecondary: 8.8.8.8\n\nRetry:\n\ncloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:PORT\n\nStep 3 \u2014 Minimal Working Command\n\nOnce origin is confirmed working:\n\ncloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:PORT\n\n\nWhere PORT = actual running port.\n\nYou should see:\n\nINF +------------------------------------------------------------+\nINF |  Your quick Tunnel has been created! Visit it:            |\nINF |  https://random-name.trycloudflare.com                    |\nINF +------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n\nNo repeated originService errors.\n\nStep 4 \u2014 Verification\n\nMust confirm all three:\n\nLocal:\n\ncurl http://localhost:PORT\n\n\n\u2192 returns app HTML/JSON\n\nTunnel logs:\nNo connectex or Unable to reach origin errors.\n\nBrowser:\nVisit trycloudflare URL\n\u2192 loads Market-Watch\n\nLikely Actual Cause (Most Probable)\n\nThe error strongly indicates:\n\nMarket-Watch was not running when cloudflared started.\n\nCloudflared does not start the origin server. It only forwards traffic.\n\nFastest Fix Summary\n\nStart Market-Watch.\n\nConfirm correct port.\n\nRestart cloudflared with correct port.\n\nEnsure DNS works (switch to 1.1.1.1 if needed).",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Validate root cause in sequence: (1) check local origin listener on 18000, (2) curl origin, (3) DNS lookup for argotunnel endpoint, (4) cloudflared behavior in this shell, then produce minimal deterministic recovery commands and constraints.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-14T02:50:42+00:00 Root-cause diagnosis and minimal deterministic fix completed.\n\nVerified root causes (in this environment):\n1) Origin connectivity failure (confirmed)\n- Command: `curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://127.0.0.1:18000`\n- Result: `000` / connection refused\n- Meaning: Market-Watch origin is not running on expected port, so tunnel cannot proxy.\n\n2) cloudflared runtime mode failure from WSL using Windows .exe (confirmed)\n- Command: `\"/mnt/c/Program Files (x86)/cloudflared/cloudflared.exe\" tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:18000 --no-autoupdate`\n- Result: `WSL ... UtilBindVsockAnyPort ... socket failed 1`\n- Meaning: invoking Windows cloudflared.exe directly from WSL fails in this host mode; run from PowerShell.\n\n3) DNS check from this shell was not conclusive due tool/network constraints\n- `nslookup` unavailable here; `getent hosts` lookup failed in sandbox context.\n- Not needed to prove immediate blocker because origin refusal alone is fatal.\n\nImplemented fixes:\n- Updated `scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh`:\n  a) Added deterministic origin preflight before tunnel launch.\n     - If origin unreachable, script exits with explicit start-server command.\n  b) Added WSL + `.exe` guard with explicit PowerShell tunnel command.\n     - Prevents opaque vsock failure path.\n  c) Redirects process output to `.demo/cloudflared.log` for clearer diagnostics.\n- Updated troubleshooting note in `docs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md` for WSL/PowerShell behavior.\n\nPost-fix behavior evidence:\n- Command: `CLOUDFLARED_BIN=\"/mnt/c/Program Files (x86)/cloudflared/cloudflared.exe\" ./scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh`\n- Output now deterministically reports:\n  - `Origin preflight failed: http://127.0.0.1:18000 is not reachable.`\n  - `Start Market-Watch first, then rerun deploy.`\n\nDeterministic recovery path:\n1) Start app on origin port (18000).\n2) If running from WSL with Windows cloudflared, execute tunnel from PowerShell:\n   & \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\cloudflared\\cloudflared.exe\" tunnel --url \"http://127.0.0.1:18000\" --no-autoupdate\n3) Verify URL returns 200 and `/api/health` returns 200.\n- 2026-02-14T02:50:54+00:00 Root-cause diagnosis and minimal deterministic fix completed.\n\nVerified root causes (in this environment):\n1) Origin connectivity failure (confirmed)\n- Command: curl http://127.0.0.1:18000\n- Result: connection refused / HTTP 000\n- Meaning: Market-Watch origin is not running on expected port, so tunnel cannot proxy.\n\n2) cloudflared runtime mode failure from WSL using Windows exe (confirmed)\n- Direct tunnel run from WSL with Windows cloudflared produced vsock socket failure.\n- Meaning: invoking Windows cloudflared.exe directly from WSL fails in this host mode; run from PowerShell.\n\nImplemented fixes:\n- Updated scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh:\n  a) Added deterministic origin preflight before tunnel launch.\n  b) Added WSL + .exe guard with explicit PowerShell tunnel guidance.\n  c) Redirects process output to .demo/cloudflared.log for clearer diagnostics.\n- Updated docs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md troubleshooting note for WSL/PowerShell behavior.\n\nPost-fix behavior evidence:\n- Command: CLOUDFLARED_BIN=\"/mnt/c/Program Files (x86)/cloudflared/cloudflared.exe\" ./scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh\n- Output now deterministically reports:\n  - Origin preflight failed: http://127.0.0.1:18000 is not reachable.\n  - Start Market-Watch first, then rerun deploy.\n\nDeterministic recovery path:\n1) Start app on origin port 18000.\n2) If using WSL + Windows cloudflared binary, run tunnel from PowerShell.\n3) Verify trycloudflare URL and /api/health return HTTP 200.\n- 2026-02-14T02:51:21+00:00 Root-cause diagnosis completed. Confirmed origin on 127.0.0.1:18000 is not reachable (HTTP 000), and Windows cloudflared.exe invoked from WSL produced vsock socket failure. Applied deterministic fix in scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh: origin preflight check, explicit WSL+exe PowerShell guidance, and improved log capture. Updated docs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md troubleshooting accordingly.",
      "outputs": "Implemented minimal deterministic tunnel-recovery fix: deploy now fails fast when origin is down, and explicitly directs WSL users with Windows cloudflared.exe to run tunnel from PowerShell.",
      "evidence": "Verified pre-fix failures: curl http://127.0.0.1:18000 -> HTTP 000 (origin down); direct WSL launch of Windows cloudflared.exe -> vsock socket failure. Applied changes in scripts/demo/deploy_cloudflare_demo.sh and docs/demo/STAKEHOLDER_DEMO.md. Post-fix deploy output now gives clear origin preflight failure and exact recovery instruction.",
