      "request_text": "codex> Add remote access protection to nginx for production demo\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nModify the nginx configuration so that the publicly reachable demo site is protected by basic HTTP authentication. Stakeholders must provide a username and password to access any URL (including WebSockets and /health). Do not expose broker secrets or remove core functionality.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n- nginx returns 401 Unauthorized until correct credentials are supplied\n- Credentials configurable in a secure store (htpasswd)\n- WebSockets and API proxy continue working after authentication\n- No public unauthenticated access allowed\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate\n\nScope / Stakeholders:\n- nginx config in /etc/nginx/sites-available/marketwatch\n- Protected routes: all\n- Stakeholders: internal devs + stakeholder viewers\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do not remove existing proxy_pass logic\n- Ensure WebSocket upgrades still function\n- Use standard htpasswd for auth\nSoft:\n- Use a single credential pair for demo viewers initially\nIgnored:\n- Full SSO integration\n\nAssumptions:\n- nginx is currently proxying correctly\n- You have shell access to create htpasswd\n\nDeliverables:\n\n1) Generate htpasswd entry for username (e.g., stakeholder) and a strong password\n2) Update nginx server block:\n   - Add `auth_basic \"Restricted Demo\";`\n   - Add `auth_basic_user_file /etc/nginx/.htpasswd;`\n   inside the root `location /` handling both HTTP and ws\n   Add necessary proxy headers (`proxy_http_version 1.1` etc.)\n3) Test both HTTP and WebSocket under auth\n4) Verification steps:\n   - Accessing https://yourdomain/health without creds \u2192 401\n   - With basic auth \u2192 200\n   - /ws connects only after credentials\n   - No broker secrets leak\n\nExample commit message:",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Inspect current /etc/nginx/sites-available/marketwatch, generate htpasswd credential, provide exact auth-enabled nginx server block preserving proxy/websocket behavior, and supply verification commands. Apply directly if permissions allow; otherwise provide root-exec steps.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-14T23:57:04+00:00 Inspected live nginx config at /etc/nginx/sites-available/marketwatch and prepared auth-enabled replacement preserving proxy/websocket headers. Direct write failed due host permission boundary (cannot write /etc in this environment).",
      "outputs": "BLOCKED: Cannot modify /etc/nginx/sites-available/marketwatch or /etc/nginx/.htpasswd from this workspace due OS permission boundary (write to /etc denied).",
      "evidence": "",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "Run the following as a privileged user on the VPS: 1) Create htpasswd file: printf 'stakeholder:.kWFkOwWZuhVQDCOL1/\\n' | sudo tee /etc/nginx/.htpasswd >/dev/null && sudo chmod 640 /etc/nginx/.htpasswd && sudo chown root:www-data /etc/nginx/.htpasswd. 2) Replace /etc/nginx/sites-available/marketwatch with: server { listen 80 default_server; server_name _; location / { auth_basic \"Restricted Demo\"; auth_basic_user_file /etc/nginx/.htpasswd; proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000; proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Upgrade ; proxy_set_header Connection \"upgrade\"; proxy_set_header Host ; proxy_set_header X-Real-IP ; proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For ; proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto ; } }. 3) Validate/reload: sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx. 4) Verify auth: curl -i http://<host>/health (expect 401), curl -i -u stakeholder:'Gw_B+KPDARG0zIzO0^wFSh' http://<host>/health (expect 200), and test websocket with basic auth headers.",
      "objective": "codex> Add remote access protection to nginx for production demo"
    },
