      "request_text": "codex> Improve Communicate UI usability: copy output button + clickable request links\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nEnhance the Communicate UI to improve reliability of copying outputs and navigation within communicate.md.\n\nThere are three issues to address:\n\n1) Add a dedicated \u201cCopy Output\u201d button in the top navigation section.\n2) Mitigate refresh-related copy/selection problems.\n3) Make request links in communicate.md clickable for TOC-style navigation.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n- Users can copy the full output of the currently selected request with one click.\n- Copy action works even if auto-refresh is enabled.\n- No reliance on manual Ctrl+A selection.\n- Request IDs in communicate.md become clickable anchors.\n- Navigation does not break existing rendering behavior.\n\nScope:\n- Communicate UI frontend\n- communicate.md rendering logic\n- No backend runtime changes unless strictly required\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do not alter runtime invariants.\n- Do not change request execution semantics.\n- Preserve existing \u201cCopy Req Link\u201d behavior.\n- Keep implementation minimal and isolated to UI layer.\n\nSoft:\n- Improve usability without introducing state instability.\n- Avoid large refactors.\n\nIgnored:\n- Styling redesign beyond necessary UI adjustments.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n1) Copy Output Button\n   - Add a button labeled \u201cCopy Output\u201d in the top navigation section (next to Copy Req Link).\n   - When clicked:\n       - Copy the entire rendered output block of the currently selected request.\n       - Use navigator.clipboard API.\n       - Provide temporary visual confirmation (e.g., \u201cCopied \u2713\u201d for 1\u20132 seconds).\n   - Must work even if auto-refresh is enabled.\n\n2) Refresh-Safe Copy Handling\n   - Ensure auto-refresh does not interrupt clipboard copying.\n   - If necessary:\n       - Temporarily suspend refresh during copy action.\n       - Or snapshot the current output DOM before copying.\n   - Document chosen approach in comments.\n\n3) Clickable Request Links in communicate.md\n   - Convert request identifiers (e.g., REQ-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS) into anchor links.\n   - Each request block should have an id attribute.\n   - Clicking a request ID in the list should:\n       - Scroll to the corresponding block.\n       - Highlight briefly for orientation (optional but preferred).\n   - Must not break markdown rendering.\n\n4) Verification Steps\n   - Select a request \u2192 click \u201cCopy Output\u201d \u2192 paste into text editor \u2192 full output appears.\n   - Trigger auto-refresh \u2192 ensure copy still works.\n   - Click a request ID link \u2192 page scrolls to correct request.\n   - No console errors.\n\nOutput:\n- Minimal diff summary\n- Files modified\n- Short explanation of refresh handling strategy",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Add Copy Output control in UI toolbar, implement refresh-safe copy strategy using in-memory snapshot + temporary refresh pause, and make REQ identifiers clickable in rendered request content with navigation + brief highlight.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-15T01:00:15+00:00 Reviewed commscribe UI code paths; implementing minimal frontend-only changes in commscribe/ui/index.html (and CSS if needed) without runtime semantic changes.",
      "outputs": "Implemented the requested Communicate UI usability improvements with minimal UI-only changes.\n\nFiles modified\n- `commscribe/ui/index.html`\n- `commscribe/ui/theme.css`\n\nMinimal diff summary\n1) Added toolbar button\n- Added `Copy Output` button next to existing `Copy REQ Link`.\n\n2) Refresh-safe copy handling\n- Added `selectedRequestData` snapshot state and `refreshPauseUntil` guard.\n- Copy action reads from in-memory selected request snapshot (`selectedRequestData.outputs`) instead of manual selection/DOM scraping.\n- During copy, refresh is temporarily paused for 2 seconds to avoid refresh races.\n- Button shows temporary confirmation (`Copied \u2713`) or failure (`Copy failed`).\n\n3) Clickable request links in rendered request content\n- Added REQ linkification helper that converts `REQ-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS` text to clickable anchors in detail blocks.\n- Added navigation handler for inline REQ links (`data-req-nav`) to open target request.\n- Added brief jump highlight and scroll-to-detail behavior for orientation.\n\n4) Styling support\n- Added `.req-inline-link` styles for clickable REQ ids.\n- Added `.req-jump-highlight` animation for brief visual focus after navigation.\n\nRefresh handling strategy (short)\n- Strategy used: snapshot + temporary refresh pause.\n- Copy reads `selectedRequestData.outputs` (stable in-memory data), and `refresh()` returns early while `Date.now() < refreshPauseUntil`.\n- This prevents auto-refresh from interrupting copy operations while preserving periodic refresh behavior.",
      "evidence": "Verification performed\n- Ran UI tests:\n  - `python3 -m unittest commscribe.tests.test_communicate_ui -v`\n  - Result: 8 tests passed.\n\nManual verification steps\n1) Select a request in UI.\n2) Click `Copy Output`.\n3) Paste into a text editor; confirm full Outputs block text is copied.\n4) Wait during auto-refresh interval; repeat copy and confirm it still succeeds.\n5) Click a REQ id shown inside rendered detail text; confirm navigation updates selection, scrolls to detail area, and briefly highlights orientation target.\n6) Confirm no browser console errors during these actions.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "codex> Improve Communicate UI usability: copy output button + clickable request links"
    },
