      "request_text": "codex> Generate actionable implementation plan for strengthening governance metrics and maturity\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nProduce a concrete implementation plan that turns the previously generated governance recommendations (SLIs/SLOs, MTTR, CFR, defect escape, release KPIs, runbooks, PIRs, API contracts, versioning) into executable engineering tasks with tools, scripts, integration steps, and verification commands.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n- Each recommendation must specify:\n  - Tools or libraries to use (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, CI engines)\n  - Code/configuration artifacts to add\n  - Where to integrate in the repo\n  - How to measure success objectively\n  - Exact commands or scripts for setup and verification\n- Must preserve existing architecture and runtime invariants\n- Must produce repeatable, automatable steps\n\nTime Horizon:\nIncremental: 30-day execution plan\n\nScope:\n- Quantification & evaluability (SLIs/SLOs, error budgets, dashboards)\n- Operational discipline (incident reviews, runbooks, release gates)\n- Productization readiness (API contracts, versioning, packaging)\n- Observability minimum bar (logs, metrics, alerts)\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do not assume external closed source tools; use open source or managed tools compatible with FastAPI/nginx ecosystem\n- Do not degrade existing system stability\nSoft:\n- Prefer incremental integration over big-bang rewrites\nIgnored:\n- UI/UX aesthetic improvements outside governance signals\n\nDeliverables:\n\n1) **SLI/SLO Monitoring Setup**\n   - Specify a metrics pipeline (e.g., Prometheus + exporters)\n   - Provide config for request success rate, latency, error rate SLIs\n   - Define SLO targets and alert rules\n   - Generate dashboards (Grafana)\n\n2) **Operational Tracking**\n   - Incident template artifacts (YAML/MD)\n   - PIR automation (scripts to collect logs, annotations)\n   - Runbook templates\n   - Integrate incident timeline automation\n\n3) **Release Quality Metrics**\n   - Scripts or CI config to calculate:\n     - Deployment lead time\n     - Change Failure Rate\n     - Defect escape rate\n   - Store metrics in a visible dashboard\n\n4) **API Contract and Versioning**\n   - Integrate OpenAPI publishing (versioned)\n   - GitHub/GitLab CI step to fail on contract breaking\n   - Script to auto-publish compatibility matrix\n\n5) **Verification and Alerts**\n   - Test commands for each metric\n   - Example thresholds and alert definitions\n   - Smoke scripts to validate metric collection\n\n6) **Verification Plan**\n   - Checklist of success criteria for each subtask\n   - Expected outputs and commands to verify them\n\nExample commit message at end:",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Create a 30-day executable governance implementation plan mapping each recommendation to concrete tools, repo artifacts, CI integrations, alert rules, and verification commands while preserving current runtime invariants.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-15T01:12:03+00:00 Preparing phased implementation plan covering SLI/SLO monitoring, operational discipline automation, release quality KPIs, API contract/versioning gates, and verification checklist.",
      "outputs": "30-Day Actionable Implementation Plan: Governance Metrics + Maturity\n\nGuiding constraints\n- Preserve runtime invariants and existing request lifecycle semantics.\n- Add observability/governance in parallel, not via core-logic rewrites.\n- Keep all additions opt-in and verifiable via CI and scripts.\n\nProposed repo structure additions\n- `monitoring/prometheus/prometheus.yml`\n- `monitoring/prometheus/alert_rules.yml`\n- `monitoring/grafana/dashboards/governance_overview.json`\n- `monitoring/loki/loki-config.yml` (optional if Loki chosen)\n- `reports/governance/` (generated KPI JSON/HTML)\n- `scripts/governance/collect_sli_snapshot.py`\n- `scripts/governance/calc_release_kpis.py`\n- `scripts/governance/calc_defect_escape.py`\n- `scripts/governance/publish_openapi.py`\n- `scripts/governance/check_openapi_breaking.py`\n- `scripts/governance/generate_compat_matrix.py`\n- `docs/operations/RUNBOOK_TEMPLATE.md`\n- `docs/operations/INCIDENT_TEMPLATE.md`\n- `docs/operations/PIR_TEMPLATE.md`\n- `docs/operations/SLO_POLICY.md`\n- `.github/workflows/governance-metrics.yml` (if GitHub Actions)\n\n1) SLI/SLO Monitoring Setup\n\nTooling\n- Metrics: `prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator` for FastAPI request metrics.\n- Scraping/alerting: Prometheus + Alertmanager.\n- Dashboards: Grafana.\n- Edge metrics: nginx stub_status exporter or nginx log parsing pipeline.\n\nImplementation tasks\n1. Add FastAPI metrics endpoint (non-invasive):\n   - Integrate instrumentation in app startup path with `/metrics` endpoint.\n   - Keep existing API behavior unchanged.\n2. Add Prometheus scrape config:\n   - `monitoring/prometheus/prometheus.yml` with jobs for app + optional nginx exporter.\n3. Add alert rules:\n   - `monitoring/prometheus/alert_rules.yml` for 5xx rate, latency SLO, availability burn.\n4. Add Grafana dashboard JSON:\n   - Track request success rate, p95 latency, error budget burn, health endpoint status.\n\nSLO definitions (initial)\n- Availability SLO: >= 99.5% (30-day) for `/health`, `/api/health`, and top 3 critical API routes.\n- Latency SLO: p95 <= 500ms for critical routes.\n- Error budget: 0.5% monthly failure budget.\n\nAlert thresholds (initial)\n- Critical: 5xx ratio > 2% over 10m.\n- Warning: p95 latency > 800ms over 15m.\n- Burn alert: projected error budget exhaustion in < 7 days.\n\nSetup commands\n- `pip install prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator`\n- `docker run -d --name prometheus -p 9090:9090 -v $PWD/monitoring/prometheus/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml prom/prometheus`\n- `docker run -d --name grafana -p 3000:3000 grafana/grafana`\n\nVerification commands\n- `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/metrics | head`\n- `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/rules`\n- `curl -s \"http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/query?query=rate(http_requests_total[5m])\"`\n\nSuccess criteria\n- `/metrics` exposed and scraped.\n- Dashboard panels populated.\n- At least one synthetic alert rule can be tested end-to-end.\n\n2) Operational Tracking (Incidents, PIRs, Runbooks)\n\nTooling\n- Templates + scripts (Markdown/YAML + Python).\n- Optional issue tracker integration via GitHub CLI (`gh`) or API.\n\nImplementation tasks\n1. Add incident/runbook templates:\n   - `docs/operations/INCIDENT_TEMPLATE.md`\n   - `docs/operations/PIR_TEMPLATE.md`\n   - `docs/operations/RUNBOOK_TEMPLATE.md`\n2. Add timeline collector script:\n   - `scripts/governance/collect_incident_timeline.py`\n   - Inputs: start/end time, request_id/service tags.\n   - Outputs: structured timeline JSON under `reports/governance/incidents/`.\n3. Add PIR enforcement check in CI:\n   - For incidents labeled `sev1|sev2`, require PIR artifact path.\n\nTemplate fields (minimum)\n- Incident: severity, start/end UTC, detection source, impacted routes, mitigation, recovery time.\n- PIR: root cause, contributing factors, corrective actions, owners, due dates.\n- Runbook: trigger conditions, diagnostics, rollback steps, validation checks.\n\nVerification commands\n- `python3 scripts/governance/collect_incident_timeline.py --from 2026-02-01T00:00:00Z --to 2026-02-01T02:00:00Z --out reports/governance/incidents/sample.json`\n- `test -f docs/operations/PIR_TEMPLATE.md && echo OK`\n\nSuccess criteria\n- Top 5 incident classes mapped to runbooks.\n- PIR template adopted and referenced in incident workflow.\n- Timeline script produces reproducible output.\n\n3) Release Quality Metrics (Lead Time, CFR, Defect Escape)\n\nTooling\n- Git metadata + CI deploy metadata + issue labels.\n- Python aggregation scripts writing JSON/CSV for dashboards.\n\nImplementation tasks\n1. Add lead time calculator:\n   - `scripts/governance/calc_release_kpis.py`\n   - Calculate merge->deploy duration (p50/p90).\n2. Add CFR calculator:\n   - Same script or separate module reading release and incident/hotfix labels.\n3. Add defect escape script:\n   - `scripts/governance/calc_defect_escape.py` consuming issue metadata (`found_in`).\n4. Persist generated metrics:\n   - `reports/governance/release_kpis.json`.\n\nKPI targets\n- Lead time: p50 <= 1 day, p90 <= 3 days.\n- CFR: <= 15% per release window.\n- Defect escape: <= 10% prod-found defects.\n\nCI integration\n- Nightly job generates KPI artifacts.\n- PR check warns when trailing windows exceed thresholds.\n\nVerification commands\n- `python3 scripts/governance/calc_release_kpis.py --since 30d --out reports/governance/release_kpis.json`\n- `python3 scripts/governance/calc_defect_escape.py --since 30d --out reports/governance/defect_escape.json`\n- `cat reports/governance/release_kpis.json | jq .`\n\nSuccess criteria\n- KPI JSON generated on schedule.\n- Threshold breaches visible in CI output and dashboard.\n\n4) API Contract + Versioning + Compatibility Matrix\n\nTooling\n- OpenAPI export from FastAPI.\n- Contract diff checker (`openapi-diff` or Python comparator).\n- SemVer policy in release workflow.\n\nImplementation tasks\n1. Publish versioned OpenAPI snapshots:\n   - `scripts/governance/publish_openapi.py`\n   - Output path: `contracts/openapi/v1/openapi-<date>.json` + `contracts/openapi/latest.json`.\n2. Add breaking-change check:\n   - `scripts/governance/check_openapi_breaking.py --base contracts/openapi/latest.json --candidate <new>`\n   - Fail CI on breaking change unless explicit override label.\n3. Add version policy docs:\n   - `docs/operations/VERSIONING_POLICY.md` (SemVer + support window).\n4. Add compatibility matrix generator:\n   - `scripts/governance/generate_compat_matrix.py`\n   - Output `reports/governance/compatibility_matrix.md`.\n\nVerification commands\n- `python3 scripts/governance/publish_openapi.py --out contracts/openapi/latest.json`\n- `python3 scripts/governance/check_openapi_breaking.py --base contracts/openapi/latest.json --candidate contracts/openapi/latest.json`\n- `python3 scripts/governance/generate_compat_matrix.py --out reports/governance/compatibility_matrix.md`\n\nSuccess criteria\n- Contract snapshot generated per release.\n- CI blocks undocumented breaking contracts.\n- Compatibility matrix published and updated monthly.\n\n5) Verification + Alerts (Smoke validations)\n\nAdd smoke script\n- `scripts/governance/smoke_governance.sh` running:\n  - health and metrics endpoint checks\n  - Prometheus rule API checks\n  - existence/format checks for KPI and contract artifacts\n\nExample smoke commands\n- `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/health`\n- `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/metrics | grep -E \"http_.*requests\"`\n- `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/rules >/dev/null`\n- `test -f reports/governance/release_kpis.json`\n- `test -f contracts/openapi/latest.json`\n\nAlert examples\n- Availability burn > 2x budget over 1h -> warning.\n- Availability burn > 5x budget over 15m -> critical.\n- CFR trailing 30d > 20% -> operational warning (non-paging).\n\n6) 30-Day phased execution timeline\n\nDays 1-5\n- Add SLO policy doc + incident/PIR/runbook templates.\n- Enable FastAPI metrics endpoint and Prometheus scrape.\n- Stand up baseline Grafana dashboard.\n\nDays 6-12\n- Add alert rules + alert routing.\n- Implement release KPI scripts and scheduled CI generation.\n- Publish initial KPI baseline report.\n\nDays 13-20\n- Implement OpenAPI publishing and contract break checks in CI.\n- Publish versioning policy and compatibility matrix generator.\n\nDays 21-30\n- Add governance smoke script and enforce in CI.\n- Run first operational review against collected data.\n- Tune thresholds/alerts based on first two weeks of telemetry.\n\nVerification Plan (checklist)\n\nSLI/SLO\n- [ ] `/metrics` endpoint present.\n- [ ] Prometheus scrape target UP.\n- [ ] Dashboard shows request rate/error/latency.\n- [ ] Alert rule test triggers notification path.\n\nOperational discipline\n- [ ] Incident/PIR/runbook templates in repo.\n- [ ] Timeline script outputs valid JSON.\n- [ ] Sev1/2 workflow includes PIR completion gate.\n\nRelease quality\n- [ ] KPI scripts produce JSON artifacts.\n- [ ] CI publishes artifacts and flags threshold breaches.\n\nProductization readiness\n- [ ] Versioned OpenAPI artifact published.\n- [ ] Contract-breaking check active in CI.\n- [ ] Compatibility matrix generated.\n\nGlobal success criterion\n- Governance artifacts regenerate from scripts/CI without manual editing.\n- No core runtime behavior or invariants changed to enable governance metrics.",
      "evidence": "No runtime code modifications executed for this request.\nDeliverable is an implementation-ready plan with:\n- tool selections\n- target repo artifact paths\n- integration points\n- setup/verification commands\n- phased 30-day milestones and objective success criteria.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
