      "request_text": "codex> Audit existing scripts for virtual environment setup and provide a definitive venv helper\n\nProblem Type:\ndescriptive + prescriptive\n\nObjective:\nReview all existing shell and Python helper scripts in the repository to determine whether:\n1) A script exists to create and activate a Python virtual environment.\n2) It is robust (works on fresh environments, idempotent, documented).\n3) If none exists or it is insufficient, generate a definitive venv setup script with instructions.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n- Script must:\n  - Create a virtual environment if not existing\n  - Activate it correctly in bash/sh\n  - Install dependencies (from requirements.txt) into that venv\n  - Fail with clear error if prerequisites are missing\n  - Be runnable from project root\n- If multiple scripts exist, produce a summary of each:\n  - Path\n  - Purpose\n  - Whether it handles venv\n  - Quality gaps\n- If missing or insufficient, produce a new script with:\n  - Self-contained logic\n  - Clear usage instructions\n  - Safety checks (e.g., `which python3`, existing venv)\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate diagnostic + script generation\n\nScope:\n- Scripts directory: `scripts/`\n- Root helpers (e.g., `serve.py`, other helpers)\n- Dev config files that may contain venv logic\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do not alter existing runtime behavior outside script generation\n- Do not assume nonstandard tools installed\n\nSoft:\n- Use standard tools only (`python3`, `venv`, `pip`)\n- Provide simple, clear UX\n\nIgnored:\n- CI workflows (unless they contain venv logic that can be reused)\n\nDeliverables:\n\n1) **Audit Report**\n   - List of scripts examined\n   - Which scripts set up/activate venv\n   - Quality rating for each\n\n2) **Definitive venv Helper Script**\n   - Example: `scripts/setup_venv.sh`\n   - Creates and activates venv\n   - Installs dependencies\n   - Prints usage instructions\n\n3) **Usage Instructions**\n   - How to run (e.g., `bash scripts