      "codex_ack_plan": "Audit repository scripts for venv setup/activation robustness, summarize quality gaps, and add a definitive scripts/setup_venv.sh helper with safety checks, dry-run mode, and usage guidance if needed.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-15T01:45:58+00:00 Starting script audit across scripts/ and root helpers for venv creation/activation/install logic and idempotency.\n- 2026-02-15T01:46:55+00:00 Completed venv audit and added scripts/setup_venv.sh as definitive helper (idempotent, prerequisite checks, dry-run, dependency install, root-run compatible).",
      "outputs": "Audit Report\n\nScripts examined for venv setup/activation\n- `start_app.sh`\n  - Purpose: local app startup helper.\n  - Handles venv: yes (creates `venv`, activates, conditionally installs deps).\n  - Quality rating: **Medium**.\n  - Gaps:\n    - No dry-run mode.\n    - Bash-specific (`source`) and hardcoded to `venv` only.\n    - Mixed concerns (env bootstrap + app launch), not a dedicated reusable setup tool.\n\n- `scripts/run_tests.sh`\n  - Purpose: run tests with artifact logging.\n  - Handles venv: partial (activates existing envs in priority order).\n  - Quality rating: **Medium**.\n  - Gaps:\n    - Does not create missing venv.\n    - Geared to test execution, not first-time environment bootstrap.\n\n- `scripts/run_tests.bat`\n  - Purpose: Windows test runner.\n  - Handles venv: partial (activates existing `venv`).\n  - Quality rating: **Low-Medium**.\n  - Gaps:\n    - No venv creation path.\n    - Windows-only and test-specific.\n\n- `scripts/setup_cron.sh`\n  - Purpose: schedule post-market tasks.\n  - Handles venv: references fixed `.venv-wsl` path only.\n  - Quality rating: **Low** for generic setup.\n  - Gaps:\n    - No creation/installation logic.\n    - Environment-specific assumption.\n\n- `scripts/serve.py` and most other `scripts/*`\n  - Purpose: runtime/task operations.\n  - Handles venv: no setup logic (expected).\n  - Quality rating for venv setup: **N/A**.\n\nConclusion\n- No existing script provides a definitive, reusable, idempotent venv bootstrap for fresh environments.\n- Added a dedicated helper to close this gap.\n\nDefinitive venv helper script\n- Added: `scripts/setup_venv.sh`\n- Capabilities:\n  - Creates virtual environment if missing.\n  - Works from project root automatically (script resolves root).\n  - Checks prerequisites (`python3`, `venv` module, `requirements.txt`).\n  - Installs dependencies into that venv (`pip install -r requirements.txt`).\n  - Supports idempotent reruns.\n  - Supports `--dry-run` for non-destructive validation.\n  - Supports `--venv-dir <path>` and `--no-upgrade-pip`.\n\nUsage instructions\n- Standard run:\n  - `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh`\n- Dry run:\n  - `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh --dry-run`\n- Custom venv path:\n  - `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh --venv-dir .venv`\n- Activate after setup:\n  - `source venv/bin/activate`\n\nCI integration snippet\n- Example step:\n```yaml\n- name: Setup Python environment\n  run: |\n    bash scripts/setup_venv.sh --venv-dir .venv\n    . .venv/bin/activate\n    python -V\n```\n\nVerification plan\n1) Dry-run path\n- `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh --dry-run`\n- Expected: prints planned create/install actions without modifying environment.\n\n2) Real setup path\n- `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh`\n- `source venv/bin/activate`\n- `python -V`\n- `pip list | grep prometheus-client`\n- Expected: package present and no prerequisite errors.\n\n3) Idempotency\n- Re-run `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh`\n- Expected: reports existing venv and completes dependency install safely.\n\nFiles modified\n- `scripts/setup_venv.sh` (new)",
      "evidence": "Validation executed\n- `bash scripts/setup_venv.sh --dry-run` completed and printed planned commands.\n- `git status --short` confirms only new file in scope: `scripts/setup_venv.sh`.\n\nObserved dry-run output includes:\n- pip/setuptools/wheel upgrade command\n- requirements installation command\n- activation instructions",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "codex> Audit existing scripts for virtual environment setup and provide a definitive venv helper"
    },
