      "request_text": "codex> Refactor metrics to use registry injection for test safety\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nRefactor the existing Prometheus metrics instrumentation so that metric objects are created via a factory and bound to a custom CollectorRegistry. Avoid global metric registration in module scope to eliminate duplicate timeseries in test environments. Update the /metrics endpoint to use the injected registry. Update tests accordingly.\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n- No global metric registration.\n- Each invocation of create_metrics returns a fresh registry and metric instances.\n- The /metrics endpoint uses the correct instance registry.\n- Tests do not cause duplicated timeseries errors.\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate.\n\nScope:\n- server/main.py (or wherever metrics are defined)\n- tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py\n- Any module that currently imports global metrics\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do not remove metric names or labels.\n- Do not change metric semantics (counter/histogram shape).\n- Preserve existing endpoint behavior.\n\nSoft:\n- Keep API surface simple.\n\nIgnored:\n- Integration with external monitoring systems.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n1) **create_metrics Factory**\n   - Add a function that takes an optional registry and returns:\n       - registry\n       - instrumented metrics: request counter, error counter, latency histogram\n\n2) **App Initialization Update**\n   - In server startup, call create_metrics to initialize registry\n   - Update /metrics endpoint to use generate_latest(registry)\n\n3) **Test Updates**\n   - Modify tests to create isolated registry via create_metrics\n   - Test metrics endpoint using test client and isolated registry\n\n4) **Minimal Diff Summary**\n   - Show only lines changed/added/removed in patch form\n\n5) **Verification**\n   - pytest tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py must pass with no duplicate timeseries errors\n   - Manual curl to /metrics must still return expected metrics\n\nExample commit message:",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Replace module-level Prometheus metric objects with create_metrics(registry) factory + app-bound registry instance, wire middleware and /metrics endpoint to injected registry, and update governance metrics tests for isolated registries.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-15T01:55:39+00:00 Starting metrics refactor: registry-injected metric factory in server/main.py and tests updated to avoid duplicate timeseries in reload scenarios.\n- 2026-02-15T02:05:20+00:00 Refactor complete: removed module-scope metric registration, introduced create_metrics(registry) factory, bound metrics to app.state, switched /metrics to generate_latest(app registry), and updated metrics tests for isolated registry injection.",
      "outputs": "Implemented registry-injection refactor for Prometheus metrics with test-safe isolation.\n\nFiles changed\n- `server/main.py`\n- `tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py`\n\n1) create_metrics factory\n- Added `create_metrics(registry: CollectorRegistry | None = None)` in `server/main.py`.\n- Factory returns a fresh bundle each call:\n  - `registry`\n  - `request_count` (`http_requests_total`)\n  - `request_error_count` (`http_request_errors_total`)\n  - `request_latency` (`http_request_duration_seconds`)\n- Metric names/labels unchanged.\n\n2) App initialization update\n- Removed module-scope global metric registration.\n- App now initializes metrics via:\n  - `app.state.metrics = create_metrics()`\n- Middleware uses app-bound metrics instance (`app.state.metrics[...]`).\n- `/metrics` endpoint now uses injected registry:\n  - `generate_latest(app.state.metrics[\"registry\"])`\n\n3) Test updates\n- Updated `tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py`:\n  - Injects isolated metrics bundle into app state per test load:\n    - `app.state.metrics = module.create_metrics()`\n  - Added factory isolation assertion:\n    - two `create_metrics()` calls return distinct registry/metric objects.\n  - Existing endpoint assertions retained.\n\n4) Minimal diff summary\n- `server/main.py`\n  - Added `CollectorRegistry` import.\n  - Added `create_metrics(...)` factory.\n  - Replaced global metric objects with `app.state.metrics` usage.\n  - Updated `/metrics` endpoint to `generate_latest(app.state.metrics[\"registry\"])`.\n- `tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py`\n  - Helper returns `(app, module)` and injects fresh metrics.\n  - Added `test_create_metrics_returns_isolated_registries`.\n  - Updated existing tests to use helper tuple.\n\n5) Verification\n- Pytest target command:\n  - `python3 -m pytest tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py -q`\n- Expected:\n  - tests pass\n  - no duplicate timeseries errors\n- Manual check:\n  - `curl http://localhost:8000/metrics`\n  - expected: `http_requests_total`, `http_request_errors_total`, `http_request_duration_seconds` still present.",
      "evidence": "Validation run in this shell:\n- `python3 -m py_compile server/main.py tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py` passed.\n\nEnvironment limitation:\n- Runtime import-based verification for FastAPI tests could not be executed here because `fastapi` is not installed in this shell.\n- Provided pytest and curl commands above for full verification in project runtime environment.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
      "objective": "codex> Refactor metrics to use registry injection for test safety"
    },
