      "request_text": "codex> Reassess current CI coverage state and implement an actionable coverage improvement plan\n\nProblem Type:\ndescriptive + prescriptive\n\nObjective:\n1) Reassess the repo\u2019s current test/coverage state in CI and locally.\n2) Identify coverage gaps by module and by critical path (governance, startup/lifespan, routers, broker integration boundaries).\n3) Implement the minimal changes needed to make coverage \u201ccomplete\u201d in CI:\n   - deterministic coverage reporting (line + branch)\n   - stored artifacts (xml + html or term-missing)\n   - coverage threshold gating with pragmatic floors\n   - a staged plan to raise coverage safely over time\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\n- CI runs pytest with coverage and produces:\n  - terminal report with missing lines (term-missing)\n  - coverage.xml (Cobertura) for tooling\n  - optional HTML report as artifact\n- CI enforces a coverage floor (overall + at least one targeted package/module floor) and fails when below.\n- A coverage gap report is produced:\n  - top 20 files by missed lines\n  - \u201ccritical modules\u201d list with current % and target %\n- A prioritized test plan is produced with LOE and expected coverage delta.\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate (baseline + CI completeness) + staged improvements (2\u20134 iterations)\n\nScope:\n- Test runner: pytest\n- Coverage: coverage.py / pytest-cov\n- CI workflows (GitHub Actions)\n- Existing tests under tests/, including governance suite\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do not introduce flaky tests.\n- Do not chase 100% coverage; prioritize risk-reduction and critical paths.\n- Do not change business logic; add tests and minimal harness seams only when required.\n- Keep thresholds realistic: start with baseline floor + incremental increases.\n\nDeliverables:\n\nA) Reassessment Report (write into communicate record)\n- Current test command(s) and whether they run in CI today\n- Whether pytest-cov is installed/used\n- Current coverage % (line + branch) for:\n  - overall\n  - server/ (or main package)\n  - tests/governance focus modules\n- Identify what \u201cincomplete\u201d currently means (missing tooling, missing artifacts, no gates, etc.)\n\nB) Coverage Tooling Implementation\n1) Add/ensure dependencies:\n   - pytest\n   - pytest-cov\n   - coverage (if needed)\n2) Add configuration:\n   - pyproject.toml [tool.pytest.ini_options] / [tool.coverage.*] OR setup.cfg/.coveragerc\n   - include/exclude rules (ignore venv, generated reports/, etc.)\n   - enable branch coverage\n3) Add CI workflow updates:\n   - run: pytest --cov=<primary_package_or_server_dir> --cov-branch --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=xml --cov-report=html\n   - upload artifacts: coverage.xml (+ htmlcov/)\n   - enforce floor: --cov-fail-under=<baseline_or_baseline_minus_small_buffer>\n   - add per-module gate if practical (or staged plan)\n\nC) Actionable Coverage Improvement Plan\n- List top coverage gaps by risk:\n  1) startup/lifespan + flags\n  2) router endpoints (health/config/observability)\n  3) governance scripts threshold paths\n  4) broker wiring boundaries (mocked)\n- For each item:\n  - tests to add (file names, test cases)\n  - fixtures/mocks approach\n  - expected coverage increase\n  - estimated effort\n- Provide an ordered execution plan in 3 batches:\n  - Batch 1: stabilize coverage infra + add 3\u20135 high-leverage tests\n  - Batch 2: expand critical route coverage + failure modes\n  - Batch 3: raise thresholds and add contract-ish checks\n\nD) Verification\n- Local:\n  - python3 -m pytest -q\n  - python3 -m pytest --cov ... (show sample output)\n- CI:\n  - workflow passes and stores artifacts\n  - coverage floor enforced (demonstrate fail behavior by temporarily lowering floor or using a sample)\n\nOutput:\n- Minimal diff summary\n- Commands run (py_compile/pytest/coverage) and results\n- New coverage baseline and chosen thresholds\n- Next-step checklist\n\nExample commit messages:\n- ci: add pytest coverage reporting and enforce baseline gate\n- test: increase coverage for startup/lifespan and core routers",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Reassess current coverage tooling/CI + local viability, establish baseline (overall/critical modules), implement deterministic branch coverage artifacts and enforceable gates in CI, and add an actionable staged coverage improvement plan with risk-prioritized test targets.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-15T02:33:02+00:00 Auditing current coverage setup: workflow commands, coverage config, local executability, and baseline metrics extraction for overall/server/governance paths.\n- 2026-02-15T02:52:17+00:00 Added CI-enforced coverage gates (line+branch+server module floor), deterministic report artifacts (term-missing/xml/html/json), and automated top-gap report generation with critical-module targets.",
      "outputs": "A) Reassessment Report\n\nCurrent CI coverage state (before patch)\n- Workflow: `.github/workflows/tests.yml`\n- Existing test command used coverage but was incomplete for enforcement:\n  - `python -m pytest ... --cov --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=json --cov-report=html`\n- Gaps identified:\n  - No `--cov-branch` in pytest command (branch not deterministically enforced by CI command).\n  - No `coverage.xml` artifact for external tooling.\n  - No hard fail gate (`--cov-fail-under` absent).\n  - No targeted module floor gate (e.g., `server/`).\n  - No automated top-missed-lines report artifact.\n\nTooling presence\n- `pytest`, `pytest-cov`, `coverage` are present in `requirements.txt`.\n- `.coveragerc` exists and already enables branch coverage in coverage settings.\n\nCoverage baseline used for gating (from current coverage artifact)\n- Source artifact: existing `coverage.json` in repo.\n- Overall line coverage: **79.63%**\n- Overall branch coverage: **69.75%**\n- `server/` line coverage: **67.00%**\n- `server/` branch coverage: **43.60%**\n\nCritical-path gap highlights (top missed lines)\n- `fake_broker.py` (150 missed)\n- `backtest/data.py` (121)\n- `broker.py` (98)\n- `server/routers/analytics.py` (87)\n- `backtest/cli.py` (59)\n- `server/routers/trading.py` (55)\n- `server/lifespan.py` (54)\n- `server/routers/observability.py` (40)\n\nWhat \u201cincomplete\u201d meant\n- Coverage was reported but not truly governance-complete because CI did not fail on coverage regression, had no module-specific floor, and did not produce actionable ranked gap outputs.\n\nB) Coverage Tooling Implementation\n\nImplemented changes\n1) CI workflow hardening (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`)\n- Updated pytest coverage run to deterministic outputs + branch + fail gate:\n  - `--cov=. --cov-branch`\n  - `--cov-report=term-missing`\n  - `--cov-report=json:coverage.json`\n  - `--cov-report=xml:coverage.xml`\n  - `--cov-report=html:htmlcov`\n  - `--cov-fail-under=75`\n- Added automated gap report generation step:\n  - `python scripts/governance/coverage_gap_report.py ... --top 20`\n- Added enforced module threshold gate step:\n  - `python scripts/governance/check_coverage_thresholds.py --min-line 75 --min-branch 65 --min-server-line 60`\n- Artifact upload now includes:\n  - `coverage.xml`\n  - `reports/coverage/gap_report.json`\n  - `reports/coverage/gap_report.md`\n  - existing `coverage.json`, `htmlcov/`, `.coverage`\n\n2) Added coverage governance scripts\n- `scripts/governance/check_coverage_thresholds.py`\n  - Enforces:\n    - overall line floor\n    - overall branch floor\n    - `server/` line floor\n  - Fails build with exit code 1 on threshold breach.\n- `scripts/governance/coverage_gap_report.py`\n  - Generates top-20 missed files report and critical-module table.\n  - Outputs:\n    - `reports/coverage/gap_report.json`\n    - `reports/coverage/gap_report.md`\n\n3) Generated baseline gap artifacts\n- `reports/coverage/gap_report.json`\n- `reports/coverage/gap_report.md`\n\nChosen pragmatic thresholds (enforced now)\n- Overall line: **>= 75%**\n- Overall branch: **>= 65%**\n- `server/` line: **>= 60%**\n\nRationale\n- Floors are below current baseline but close enough to prevent regressions while allowing incremental test expansion.\n\nC) Actionable Coverage Improvement Plan (Prioritized)\n\nBatch 1 (high leverage, infra stabilization) \u2014 3 to 5 tests\n1) Startup/lifespan + flags\n- Add tests:\n  - `tests/server/test_startup_flags.py`\n  - cases for `MARKET_WATCH_DEMO_MODE` and `FASTAPI_DISABLE_LIFESPAN` combinations.\n- Approach: import/reload with env overrides; assert selected lifespan path and safe behavior.\n- Expected delta: +2 to +4% `server/main.py` line coverage.\n- LOE: S\n\n2) Router safety/failure modes\n- Add tests:\n  - `tests/server/test_router_resilience.py`\n  - `/api/config`, `/api/observability/logs` in both initialized and degraded states.\n- Approach: TestClient + controlled state/mocks.\n- Expected delta: +3 to +6% across `server/routers/*`.\n- LOE: M\n\n3) Governance script thresholds\n- Expand tests in `tests/governance/test_kpi_script.py`:\n  - boundary equality tests for threshold script (exactly equal to floor should pass).\n- Expected delta: +5 to +10% in `scripts/governance/*`.\n- LOE: S\n\nBatch 2 (critical routes + failure paths)\n1) `server/lifespan.py` failure and recovery paths\n- Add tests with mocked dependencies for broker/coordinator startup failures.\n- Expected delta: +8 to +12% in lifespan-related modules.\n- LOE: M\n\n2) `server/routers/analytics.py` + `server/routers/trading.py`\n- Add route-level tests for success + validation failure + backend unavailable.\n- Expected delta: +6 to +10% in those routers.\n- LOE: M\n\nBatch 3 (threshold raise + contract-ish checks)\n1) Raise floors once Batch 1+2 are stable:\n- Proposed next gates:\n  - overall line 78%\n  - overall branch 68%\n  - server line 65%\n2) Add contract-ish API checks:\n- smoke tests ensuring response shape consistency for critical endpoints.\n- LOE: M\n\nD) Verification\n\nLocal commands\n1) Baseline tests:\n- `python3 -m pytest -q`\n2) Coverage run (CI-equivalent):\n- `python3 -m pytest tests/ --ignore=tests/test_backtest_data.py --cov=. --cov-branch --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=json:coverage.json --cov-report=xml:coverage.xml --cov-report=html:htmlcov --cov-fail-under=75`\n3) Gap report generation:\n- `python3 scripts/governance/coverage_gap_report.py --input coverage.json --json-out reports/coverage/gap_report.json --md-out reports/coverage/gap_report.md --top 20`\n4) Threshold gate:\n- `python3 scripts/governance/check_coverage_thresholds.py --input coverage.json --min-line 75 --min-branch 65 --min-server-line 60`\n\nCI expected behavior\n- Workflow fails if:\n  - overall line < 75\n  - overall branch < 65\n  - `server/` line < 60\n- Workflow uploads `coverage.xml`, `htmlcov/`, and gap report artifacts.\n\nMinimal diff summary\n- `M .github/workflows/tests.yml`\n- `A scripts/governance/check_coverage_thresholds.py`\n- `A scripts/governance/coverage_gap_report.py`\n- `A reports/coverage/gap_report.json`\n- `A reports/coverage/gap_report.md`\n\nNext-step checklist\n- [ ] Add Batch 1 tests (startup flags + router degraded paths + governance boundaries)\n- [ ] Re-run CI and capture new baseline\n- [ ] Raise thresholds in small increments after two stable CI cycles\n- [ ] Track top-20 missed files trend in weekly engineering review",
      "evidence": "Commands run and results\n- `python3 scripts/governance/coverage_gap_report.py ... --top 20`\n  - Result: wrote `reports/coverage/gap_report.json` and `.md`\n- `python3 scripts/governance/check_coverage_thresholds.py --input coverage.json --min-line 75 --min-branch 65 --min-server-line 60`\n  - Result: PASS (overall_line=79.63, overall_branch=69.75, server_line=67.00)\n- Synthetic fail behavior check:\n  - Result: exit code 1 with FAIL lines for all breached thresholds\n- Static checks:\n  - `python3 -m py_compile scripts/governance/check_coverage_thresholds.py scripts/governance/coverage_gap_report.py` passed\n\nLocal execution limitation observed in this shell\n- Long-running pytest+coverage invocations timed out in this environment (exit 124) before completion, so baseline percentages were taken from current coverage artifact (`coverage.json`) and then enforced via deterministic gate scripts.",
      "next_steps_if_blocked": "",
