      "request_text": "codex> Perform full production hygiene and legacy operations audit\n\nProblem Type:\ndescriptive + prescriptive\n\nObjective:\nAudit the entire repository to identify temporary, transitional, demo-only, legacy, redundant, or unsafe operations now that the application is live on a VPS with systemd + nginx.\n\nClassify all findings into:\n- Required production logic\n- Transitional scaffolding\n- Legacy or redundant logic\n- Unsafe or publicly exposed artifacts\n- Dev-only tooling that should not exist in production runtime\n\nMetric / Evaluative Standard:\nThe audit must:\n- Enumerate exact file paths\n- Reference specific functions/flags/env vars\n- Identify whether code is reachable in production\n- State risk level (Low / Moderate / High)\n- Recommend: Keep / Remove / Refactor\n- Provide minimal removal/refactor plan\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate audit (no code changes yet)\n\nScope:\nEntire repository including:\n- server/\n- scripts/\n- monitoring/\n- CI workflows\n- runtime/\n- routers/\n- backtest/\n- Dockerfiles\n- legacy deployment configs\n- environment variables\n- demo hardening layer\n- fake broker\n- Fly.io / Cloudflare remnants\n- any orphaned scripts\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n- Do NOT modify code yet\n- Do NOT delete files\n- Only analyze and classify\n- Must assume system is deployed via:\n    systemd \u2192 uvicorn \u2192 nginx \u2192 VPS\n\nSoft:\n- Flag performance inefficiencies if obvious\n- Flag duplicate startup paths\n- Flag unreachable code branches\n\nIgnored:\n- Minor formatting inconsistencies\n- Documentation tone\n\nDeliverables:\n\n1) Startup Path Analysis\n   - All possible ways the app can start\n   - Whether scripts/serve.py is still required\n   - Lifespan override logic still reachable?\n   - Demo mode logic still necessary?\n\n2) Environment Variable Audit\n   - List all referenced env vars\n   - Mark as:\n       Production required\n       Dev-only\n       Transitional\n       Unused\n\n3) Broker & Data Layer Audit\n   - fake_broker references\n   - conditional broker factory logic\n   - demo shortcuts\n   - unreachable branches\n\n4) Demo Hardening Layer Audit\n   - server/runtime/demo_hardening.py\n   - Identify if guards are now redundant\n   - Identify if any logic masks real errors\n\n5) Observability & Logging Audit\n   - File-based logs\n   - Log path assumptions\n   - /metrics exposure\n   - Public endpoints\n   - Debug or test-only routes\n\n6) Infrastructure Remnants\n   - Fly.io configs\n   - Cloudflare artifacts\n   - Dockerfile usage\n   - Orphaned deployment files\n   - .env.demo or test env files\n\n7) CI & Coverage Artifacts\n   - Sample JSON files\n   - Generated reports accidentally committed\n   - Redundant workflow files\n\n8) Risk Matrix Summary\n   Table format:\n\n   | File | Category | Risk | Reachable in Prod | Recommendation |\n\n9) Cleanup Execution Plan\n   - Phase 1: Safe removals\n   - Phase 2: Refactors\n   - Phase 3: Optional hardening\n   - Phase 4: Verification steps\n\nVerification:\n- No production behavior changed\n- After cleanup, systemd restart must succeed\n- nginx proxy must remain functional\n- /health must return 200\n- /metrics must return expected series\n\nOutput:\n- Structured audit report\n- Categorized findings\n- Actionable cleanup roadmap\n- No narrative fluff",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Read request, execute exactly requested command/output path, validate results, then complete or block with concrete evidence.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-15T16:32:47+00:00 Completed full read-only production hygiene/legacy ops audit across startup, env vars, broker/data layer, demo hardening, observability exposure, infra remnants, and CI artifacts. Prepared structured risk matrix and phased cleanup roadmap.",
      "outputs": "## 1) Startup Path Analysis\n\nObserved startup paths:\n- `deploy/market-watch.service` -> `ExecStart=/opt/market-watch/.venv/bin/uvicorn server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`\n  - Reachable in prod: Yes (matches stated VPS systemd + nginx model)\n  - Classification: Required production logic\n- `server.py` shim -> `from server import app`\n  - Reachable in prod: Yes (indirectly via `uvicorn server:app`)\n  - Classification: Transitional scaffolding (thin compatibility entrypoint)\n- `scripts/serve.py`\n  - Reachable in prod: Typically No (dev launcher with safety keyword and optional `--reload`/`--no-lifespan`)\n  - Classification: Dev/transitional tooling\n- `start_app.sh`\n  - Reachable in prod: No (dev convenience bootstrap with `--reload`)\n  - Classification: Dev-only tooling\n\nLifespan / demo overrides:\n- `server/main.py` uses:\n  - `MARKET_WATCH_DEMO_MODE`\n  - `FASTAPI_DISABLE_LIFESPAN`\n  - `SELECTED_LIFESPAN = full_lifespan if DEMO_MODE else (noop_lifespan if USE_NOOP_LIFESPAN else full_lifespan)`\n- Reachable in prod: Yes if env vars are set in service environment; otherwise full lifespan path is used.\n- Assessment:\n  - `FASTAPI_DISABLE_LIFESPAN` is transitional and unsafe for production runtime if set.\n  - `MARKET_WATCH_DEMO_MODE` is demo/transitional and should not be enabled in production.\n\nWhether `scripts/serve.py` is still required:\n- For systemd-managed production: No.\n- For local/dev safety-start convenience: Yes (optional).\n\n## 2) Environment Variable Audit\n\nProduction required (runtime-critical):\n- `ALPACA_API_KEY`, `ALPACA_SECRET_KEY`, `TRADING_MODE`, `API_HOST`, `API_PORT`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`\n\nProduction strongly recommended (security/control):\n- `API_TOKEN` (currently not enforced by live router wiring), `AUTO_TRADE`, `TRADE_INTERVAL_MINUTES`, `MAX_DAILY_TRADES`, `MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS`, `MAX_POSITION_PCT`, `STOP_LOSS_PCT`, `DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT_PCT`, `MAX_DRAWDOWN_PCT`, `MAX_SECTOR_EXPOSURE_PCT`, `MAX_CORRELATED_EXPOSURE_PCT`, `CORRELATION_THRESHOLD`, `CORRELATION_LOOKBACK_DAYS`, `RVOL_THRESHOLD`, `MARKET_TIMEZONE`, `DATA_FEED`\n\nFeature flags / optional production:\n- `ANALYTICS_ENABLED`, `OBSERVABILITY_ENABLED`, `OBSERVABILITY_MAX_LOG_MB`, `ALERTS_ENABLED`, `ALERT_EMAIL_ENABLED`, `ALERT_WEBHOOK_ENABLED`, `ALERT_EMAIL_SMTP_HOST`, `ALERT_EMAIL_SMTP_PORT`, `ALERT_EMAIL_SMTP_USER`, `ALERT_EMAIL_SMTP_PASSWORD`, `ALERT_EMAIL_FROM`, `ALERT_EMAIL_TO`, `ALERT_EMAIL_USE_TLS`, `ALERT_EMAIL_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`, `ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL`, `ALERT_WEBHOOK_TYPE`, `ALERT_WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, `ALERT_WEBHOOK_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`\n\nDev-only / transitional:\n- `FASTAPI_DISABLE_LIFESPAN`, `MARKET_WATCH_DEMO_MODE`, `UVICORN_LOG_LEVEL`, `UI_PORT`, `UI_CHECK_ENABLED`, `UI_CHECK_INTERVAL_MINUTES`, `UI_CHECK_URL`, `UI_CHECK_LOG_PATH`, `TEST_AGENT_ENABLED`, `TEST_AGENT_INTERVAL_MINUTES`, `TEST_AGENT_LOG_PATH`, `REPLAY_RECORDER_ENABLED`, `REPLAY_RECORDER_INTERVAL_MINUTES`, `REPLAY_RECORDER_SYMBOLS`, `REPLAY_RECORDER_DIR`, `SIM_REPLAY_ENABLED`, `SIM_REPLAY_DATE`, `SIMULATION_JIGGLE_FACTOR`, `FMP_API_KEY`, `FMP_BASE_URL`\n\nLikely unused or stale in current runtime path:\n- `WEBHOOK_URL` (legacy/duplicate with alert webhook vars)\n- `REQUIRE_APPROVAL` (not used in server runtime path)\n- `ANALYTICS_DATA_PATH` (commented/legacy)\n\nConfig/state pathing vars (keep but validate):\n- `CONFIG_STATE_PATH`, `SECTOR_MAP_PATH`, `SECTOR_MAP_JSON`, `WATCHLIST_MODE`, `TOP_GAINERS_COUNT`, `TOP_GAINERS_UNIVERSE`, `TOP_GAINERS_MIN_PRICE`, `TOP_GAINERS_MIN_VOLUME`, `STRATEGY`, `MOMENTUM_THRESHOLD`, `SELL_THRESHOLD`, `POSITION_SIZER_SCALE_BY_STRENGTH`, `POSITION_SIZER_MIN_STRENGTH`, `POSITION_SIZER_MAX_STRENGTH`\n\n## 3) Broker & Data Layer Audit\n\n- `server/lifespan.py` broker factory:\n  - `FakeBroker` for `Universe.SIMULATION`\n  - `AlpacaBroker` for `PAPER/LIVE`\n  - Reachable in prod: Yes (depends on `TRADING_MODE`)\n  - Recommendation: Keep; enforce `TRADING_MODE` policy externally (prod should be `paper` or `live` only).\n- `fake_broker.py`\n  - Reachable in prod: Only if `TRADING_MODE=simulation`\n  - Risk: Moderate (accidental simulation mode in production gives false confidence/no real brokerage)\n  - Recommendation: Keep but add deployment guard to reject simulation mode in production service.\n- `server/state.py::rebuild_for_universe`\n  - Reachable in prod: Yes\n  - Quality: Good guardrails (universe mismatch assertions)\n  - Recommendation: Keep\n\n## 4) Demo Hardening Layer Audit (`server/runtime/demo_hardening.py`)\n\n- What it does:\n  - Adds `/health` readiness route\n  - Rewrites dependency calls to safe 503 wrappers\n  - Adds startup probe warning when lifespan disabled\n- Reachable in prod: Yes (always applied via `build_demo_hardening(app)` in `server/main.py`)\n- Risks:\n  - Moderate: can mask initialization defects with controlled 503 behavior instead of failing hard at startup.\n  - Moderate: runtime dependency substitution is operationally complex and harder to reason about in stable production.\n- Recommendation:\n  - Refactor: gate this layer behind explicit demo/dev mode; default to strict production failure semantics.\n\n## 5) Observability & Logging Audit\n\n- Public endpoints currently exposed from app:\n  - `/metrics` (no auth in app)\n  - `/api/logs`\n  - `/api/observability/logs`\n  - `/docs`, `/redoc`\n- Reachable in prod: Yes unless nginx restricts them.\n- Risks:\n  - High: metrics/log endpoints can leak internals if internet-reachable.\n  - Moderate: docs UIs expose API surface in production.\n- Recommendation:\n  - Keep functionality, but restrict at nginx and/or app auth dependency.\n\n## 6) Infrastructure Remnants\n\n- Fly.io artifacts:\n  - `Dockerfile`, `fly.toml`, `.dockerignore`: not present (already removed)\n- Cloudflare demo artifacts:\n  - `scripts/demo/` and `docs/demo/`: not present\n- Remaining transitional env files:\n  - `.env.demo`, `.env.demo.example` (transitional)\n- Legacy/alternate deployment content in docs:\n  - `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` includes Docker/Heroku/cloud sections not aligned with current VPS+systemd target.\n\n## 7) CI & Coverage Artifacts Audit\n\nPotentially committed generated artifacts:\n- `reports/coverage/gap_report.json`\n- `reports/coverage/gap_report.md`\n- `reports/governance/release_quality.json`\n\nSample/static artifacts (acceptable if intentional):\n- `reports/governance/deployments.sample.json`\n- `reports/inventory/*` outputs\n\nRecommendation:\n- Refactor CI to publish generated artifacts only via CI uploads, not committed files, unless explicitly versioned as baseline fixtures.\n\n## 8) Risk Matrix Summary\n\n| File | Category | Risk | Reachable in Prod | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `server/main.py` (`/metrics`, `/docs`, `/redoc`) | Required production logic + exposure | High | Yes | Refactor (protect endpoints, docs off in prod) |\n| `server/__init__.py` (`require_api_access`) | Legacy/redundant security logic (unwired) | High | No (function), impact Yes | Refactor (wire auth middleware/dependency or remove dead helper) |\n| `server/runtime/demo_hardening.py` | Transitional scaffolding | Moderate | Yes | Refactor (gate to demo/dev only) |\n| `server/lifespan.py` (`FakeBroker` branch) | Required logic with simulation branch | Moderate | Yes | Keep + enforce prod mode policy |\n| `fake_broker.py` | Dev/simulation runtime | Moderate | Conditional | Keep (non-prod only), guard usage |\n| `scripts/serve.py` | Dev tooling | Low | No | Keep (dev), exclude from prod ops docs |\n| `start_app.sh` | Dev-only tooling | Low | No | Keep or remove from prod docs |\n| `.env.demo`, `.env.demo.example` | Transitional/demo artifacts | Moderate | Possible misconfig | Remove from prod deployment package |\n| `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` (multi-target legacy sections) | Legacy/redundant docs | Moderate | Operational | Refactor to single authoritative VPS runbook |\n| `reports/coverage/gap_report.*` | Generated artifacts in repo | Low-Moderate | N/A | Remove from source control or mark as intentional baselines |\n| `reports/governance/release_quality.json` | Generated artifact | Low-Moderate | N/A | Same as above |\n| `scripts/dev_tools_tui.py` + dev audit scripts | Dev-only tooling | Low | No | Keep but isolate from runtime package |\n| `server/routers/status.py` (`/api/logs`) | Required + potentially sensitive output | Moderate-High | Yes | Restrict access; keep endpoint |\n| `server/routers/observability.py` (`/api/observability/logs`) | Required + potentially sensitive output | Moderate-High | Yes | Restrict access; keep endpoint |\n| `deploy/market-watch.service` | Required production logic | Low | Yes | Keep; make this canonical startup path |\n\n## 9) Cleanup Execution Plan\n\nPhase 1: Safe removals\n- Remove demo-only env templates from production deployment bundle (`.env.demo*`).\n- Remove or relocate committed generated reports (`reports/coverage/*`, `reports/governance/release_quality.json`) if not intentional fixtures.\n- Prune stale multi-platform deployment fragments from primary prod runbook.\n\nPhase 2: Refactors\n- Implement actual API auth enforcement in live app path (currently legacy helper is not wired).\n- Gate `build_demo_hardening(app)` to explicit non-prod mode.\n- Disable `/docs` and `/redoc` by default in production.\n\nPhase 3: Optional hardening\n- Restrict `/metrics`, `/api/logs`, `/api/observability/logs` at nginx allowlist/auth layer.\n- Add startup guard: reject `TRADING_MODE=simulation` in production service environment.\n- Consolidate startup to one blessed path (`systemd -> uvicorn server:app`).\n\nPhase 4: Verification steps\n- `systemctl restart marketwatch` succeeds.\n- `curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` returns expected healthy status under full init.\n- `curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/metrics` returns expected series and is externally restricted.\n- `curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/config` and observability routes enforce intended access control.\n- Confirm no remaining service references to demo flags (`MARKET_WATCH_DEMO_MODE`, `FASTAPI_DISABLE_LIFESPAN`).\n\n## Classification Summary\n\nRequired production logic:\n- `deploy/market-watch.service`, `server/main.py`, `server/lifespan.py`, core routers, `server/state.py`, `config.py`\n\nTransitional scaffolding:\n- `server/runtime/demo_hardening.py`, `server.py` shim, `.env.demo*`, parts of `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`\n\nLegacy/redundant logic:\n- Unwired security helper in `server/__init__.py` (`require_api_access`)\n- Multi-target deployment/doc pathways no longer used for VPS production\n\nUnsafe/publicly exposed artifacts:\n- Public API docs endpoints and telemetry/log endpoints if not nginx-restricted\n- Unenforced API token path in current runtime wiring\n\nDev-only tooling that should not exist in production runtime package:\n- `scripts/dev_tools_tui.py`, `scripts/run_*audit.py`, `scripts/organize_*`, `scripts/fix_tests.py`, `scripts/dev_server_control.py`, `start_app.sh`",
