/failure feedback.\n\nPhase 5 \u2014 State Integrity & Edge Cases\n1. Prevent:\n   - Partial imports.\n   - Duplicate residual data.\n   - Silent failures.\n2. Test cases:\n   - Import valid file into empty system.\n   - Import valid file over existing data (confirm replacement).\n   - Import malformed file (ensure no data loss).\n   - Import empty file.\n   - Import wrong format.\n\nPhase 6 \u2014 Verification\n1. Confirm:\n   - No static/demo data remains in codebase.\n   - All displayed data originates from imported file.\n   - System handles empty state gracefully.\n2. Provide summary of:\n   - Files modified.\n   - Logic removed.\n   - Logic added.\n   - Risks introduced.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do not change UI unless required for file import.\n- Do not introduce new frameworks.\n- Keep implementation minimal and consistent with current architecture.\n- Preserve local-only operation.\n\nSuccess Criteria:\n- Application contains zero demo/static data.\n- A new imported file completely replaces prior dataset.\n- System remains stable under empty or malformed input conditions.",
