      "request_text": "Title:\nIsolate and Resolve Hanging Governance Metrics Test\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nIdentify the root cause of the deterministic hang in tests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py during coverage runs and implement a minimal, test-safe fix that ensures full suite completion under pytest with coverage enabled.\n\nScope:\nIncluded:\n\ntests/governance/test_metrics_endpoint.py\n\nserver/main.py\n\nserver/runtime/demo_hardening.py\n\nAny app factory or lifespan logic invoked during tests\n\npytest configuration (pytest.ini)\n\ncoverage configuration\nExcluded:\n\nBusiness logic changes\n\nBroker logic changes\n\nNon-governance test files unless directly implicated\n\nCI workflow modifications (unless required for deterministic test execution)\n\nTime Horizon:\nImmediate root-cause isolation and one-pass fix\n\nConstraints:\nBinding:\n\nNo modification of production business logic\n\nNo removal of governance metrics functionality\n\nNo disabling of coverage instrumentation\n\nNo skipping or xfail of hanging test\n\nAll tests must pass with:\n\npytest\n\npytest --cov=server --cov-branch\nSoft:\n\nPrefer fixture-based isolation\n\nPrefer lifespan=\"off\" or controlled startup in test context\nIgnored:\n\nDeprecation warnings unless causal\n\nEnvironment Context:\n\nFastAPI application using lifespan logic\n\nMixed use of @app.on_event(\"startup\") and lifespan handlers\n\nTests use httpx.AsyncClient with ASGITransport\n\nsystemd/nginx production path irrelevant for test isolation\n\npytest + pytest-cov enabled\n\nTasks:\n\nReproduce Hang Deterministically\n\nRun:\npytest --cov=server --cov-branch -vv\n\nIdentify exact test and line where execution stalls.\n\nConfirm whether hang occurs:\na) During importlib.reload(server.main)\nb) During TestClient(app)\nc) During AsyncClient(ASGITransport)\nd) During coverage finalization\n\nInspect test_metrics_endpoint.py\n\nVerify:\n\nWhether global app is imported\n\nWhether app is reused across tests\n\nWhether lifespan is invoked implicitly\n\nWhether CollectorRegistry is isolated per test\n\nConfirm whether ASGITransport is closed explicitly.\n\nConfirm no background tasks remain pending.\n\nAudit server/main.py\n\nConfirm if app instance is global.\n\nConfirm if metrics factory is executed at import time.\n\nConfirm if demo_hardening registers @app.on_event(\"startup\").\n\nConfirm whether multiple startup handlers are registered on reload.\n\nIdentify Root Cause Category\nClassify into one:\n\nGlobal app reuse across tests\n\nLifespan double-registration\n\nStartup handler not terminating\n\nCoverage instrumentation interaction\n\nAsync transport not closing\n\nEvent loop reuse conflict\n\nImplement Minimal Fix\nIf app reuse issue:\n\nIntroduce create_app() factory.\n\nEnsure tests instantiate fresh app per test.\nIf lifespan conflict:\n\nDisable lifespan in test context via:\nASGITransport(app=app, lifespan=\"off\")\nOR\ncreate_app(testing=True) that bypasses startup hooks.\nIf startup double-registration:\n\nRemove @app.on_event usage and consolidate into lifespan.\nIf transport closure issue:\n\nExplicitly close transport after client context.\nFix must:\n\nPreserve production behavior.\n\nPreserve metrics registry injection.\n\nNot alter endpoint semantics.\n\nValidate Deterministic Completion\nRun:\npytest -q\npytest --cov=server --cov-branch -q\nConfirm:\n\nNo hangs\n\nAll tests pass\n\nCoverage summary completes\n\nNo open event loop warnings\n\nDeliverables:\n\nRoot Cause Summary:\n\nFile\n\nFunction\n\nExact failure mechanism\n\nWhy coverage exposed it\n\nMinimal Diff Summary:\n\nFile paths modified\n\nExact changes (before/after)\n\nJustification\n\nValidation Output:\n\npytest summary\n\npytest --cov summary\n\nExit codes\n\nConfirmation:\n\nHanging behavior eliminated\n\nCoverage suite completes under 60 seconds\n\nNo production startup path altered\n\nVerification:\nCompletion is validated when:\n\npytest --cov=server --cov-branch exits cleanly (exit 0)\n\nNo test exceeds 10 seconds execution\n\nNo background task warnings remain\n\nNo lifecycle double-registration occurs\n\nMetrics endpoint tests still validate expected series\n\nOutput Requirements:\n\nStructured sections only\n\nNo narrative commentary\n\nExplicit file references\n\nExplicit diff explanation\n\nExplicit confirmation of deterministic resolution",
