      "request_text": "se_agent>\n\nTitle:\nImplement AI Runtime Enforcement Layer (PROJECT_RUNTIME + STARTUP_PROTOCOL)\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nEmbed a deterministic AI Runtime Enforcement Layer into the repository so that every terminal LLM session must execute a standardized startup handshake and operate under enforced commscribe lifecycle rules.\n\nThis implementation must:\n\n* Add PROJECT_RUNTIME.md\n* Add STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md\n* Create ai_runtime/ directory\n* Integrate enforcement references into README (non-invasive)\n* Not modify business logic\n* Not alter existing commscribe schema\n* Not break current tests\n* Be production-safe\n\nScope:\n\nIncluded:\n\n* Create directory: ai_runtime/\n* Add:\n\n  * ai_runtime/PROJECT_RUNTIME.md\n  * ai_runtime/STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md\n* Add minimal README section referencing startup requirement\n* Optional: add lightweight startup_check script (non-blocking)\n* No runtime behavior change\n\nExcluded:\n\n* Backend logic changes\n* Test suite changes\n* Governance threshold changes\n* CI pipeline changes\n* Web UI changes\n\nTime Horizon:\nSingle structured patch\n\nConstraints:\n\nBinding:\n\n* Files must match enforcement templates exactly.\n* No paraphrasing or summarization.\n* Must include:\n  \"PROJECT RUNTIME ACTIVE \u2014 ENFORCED MODE\"\n* Must include:\n  communicate\n  communicate_scan\n  governance_check\n  startup_check\n* Must not alter commscribe behavior.\n* Must not auto-execute startup in code (human-triggered).\n\nSoft:\n\n* Add README section:\n  \u201cTerminal LLM Startup Requirement\u201d\n* Keep diff minimal and isolated.\n\nIgnored:\n\n* Cosmetic formatting differences.\n* License headers.\n\n---\n\n## TASKS\n\n1. Create directory:\n\n   ai_runtime/\n\n2. Create file:\n\n   ai_runtime/PROJECT_RUNTIME.md\n\nUse exact enforcement template including:\n\n* Operating Mode\n* Authorized Commands\n* Startup Handshake Requirements\n* Lifecycle Rules\n* Code Modification Rules\n* Workspace Boundaries\n* Governance Enforcement\n* Security Constraints\n* Session Acknowledgment section\n\nMust contain:\n\n```\nPROJECT RUNTIME ACTIVE \u2014 ENFORCED MODE\n```\n\n3) Create file:\n\n```\nai_runtime/STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md\n```\n\nMust include:\n\n* Phase 0\u20135 structure\n* Mandatory contract ingestion\n* communicate_scan system-status\n* git status validation\n* Governance check phase\n* Emergency override\n* Failure conditions\n* \u201cStartup protocol complete.\u201d message\n\n4. Update README.md\n\nAppend section:\n\n---\n\n## Terminal LLM Startup Requirement\n\nAll terminal LLM sessions must begin by reviewing:\n\n```\nai_runtime/STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md\n```\n\nNo development work should begin until startup protocol completes successfully.\n\n---\n\nDo not modify other README sections.\n\n5. (Optional but recommended)\n\nAdd lightweight script:\n\n```\nscripts/ai_runtime/startup_check.sh\n```\n\nPurpose:\n\n* Echo required startup steps.\n* Not enforce.\n* Informational only.\n\nContent:\n\n* Print reminder to review STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md\n* Print enforcement phrase\n\nDo not auto-run script.\n\n---\n\n## DELIVERABLES\n\n1. File list created/modified.\n\n2. Minimal diff summary.\n\n3. Confirmation:\n\n   * No business logic changed.\n   * No commscribe logic altered.\n   * No test regressions expected.\n\n4. Confirm directory structure:\n\n   ai_runtime/\n   PROJECT_RUNTIME.md\n   STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md\n\n5. Confirm enforcement phrase present in PROJECT_RUNTIME.md.\n\n---\n\n## VERIFICATION CRITERIA\n\n* Repository builds unchanged.\n* Tests remain unaffected.\n* commscribe behavior unchanged.\n* Runtime contract readable.\n* Startup protocol readable.\n* No accidental side effects.\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nStructured only.\n\nSections:\n\n* Files Created\n* Files Modified\n* Diff Summary\n* Validation Confirmation\n\nNo narrative commentary.\n\nEnd.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Run startup protocol phases 0-5: ingest runtime contracts, validate communicate_scan health, validate git working tree, execute governance equivalent checks, then publish completion signal.",
