      "request_text": "se_agent>\n\nTitle:\nAutomated Intelligent Documentation Restructure (Non-Breaking, Dependency-Safe)\n\nProblem Type:\nprescriptive\n\nObjective:\nRestructure repository documentation into a clean, typed, hierarchical `docs/` architecture while ensuring:\n\n* No functional dependencies are broken.\n* No referenced documents are orphaned.\n* No relative paths in code, CI, or README break.\n* No runtime or governance scripts depend on moved file paths without update.\n* All moved files are traceable.\n* No content is deleted.\n\nScope:\n\nIncluded:\n\n* Root-level `.md` files (excluding README.md)\n* Existing `docs/` directory\n* Governance docs\n* Architecture docs\n* Spec files\n* Reports and analysis files\n* ADR-like documents\n* Deployment docs\n\nExcluded:\n\n* LICENSE\n* README.md (except minimal link update)\n* ai_runtime/ directory\n* commscribe core files\n* Code comments\n* Non-markdown assets\n* Files referenced explicitly by CI workflows unless updated safely\n\nTime Horizon:\nSingle-pass restructure with dependency validation phase.\n\nConstraints:\n\nBinding:\n\n* Do not delete any files.\n* Do not modify content unless updating broken internal links.\n* Before moving any file:\n\n  * Search entire repo for references.\n  * Update references if necessary.\n* Maintain git history (use move, not delete + recreate).\n* Produce full move map.\n* If any ambiguity exists about classification, do not move file \u2014 mark for review.\n\nSoft:\n\n* Prefer deterministic classification rules.\n* Preserve logical grouping.\n* Avoid deep nesting beyond 3 levels.\n\nIgnored:\n\n* Cosmetic markdown formatting changes.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1 \u2014 INVENTORY & DEPENDENCY SCAN\n\n1. Enumerate all markdown files in repository:\n\n   * Root-level\n   * Nested folders\n   * Exclude:\n\n     * ai_runtime/\n     * commscribe/\n     * node_modules/\n     * venv/\n     * .git/\n\n2. For each markdown file:\n\n   * Search for references using:\n\n     * grep across repo\n     * README links\n     * CI workflow references\n     * Script references\n     * Relative path usage\n   * Build dependency graph:\n\n     * file \u2192 referenced_by\n\n3. Output classification report:\n\n   * File path\n   * Reference count\n   * Referenced by\n   * Suggested doc type\n\nIf file referenced by:\n- CI workflow\n- Script execution\n- Runtime contract\n\u2192 Mark as PROTECTED\n\u2192 Do not move without updating references.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2 \u2014 CLASSIFICATION RULES\n\nClassify markdown files into types:\n\nIf filename contains:\n- spec \u2192 docs/specs/\n- roadmap \u2192 docs/specs/\n- realism \u2192 docs/specs/\n- governance \u2192 docs/governance/\n- coverage \u2192 docs/governance/\n- deployment | vps | ssl \u2192 docs/operations/\n- architecture \u2192 docs/architecture/\n- adr \u2192 docs/architecture/adr/\n- report \u2192 docs/archive/YYYY-MM/\n- audit \u2192 docs/archive/YYYY-MM/\n- draft \u2192 docs/specs/draft/\n- notes \u2192 docs/archive/YYYY-MM/\n\nIf ambiguous:\n- Leave in place.\n- Mark for manual review.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3 \u2014 STRUCTURE CREATION\n\nEnsure directory structure exists:\n\ndocs/\n00_index.md\nspecs/\ndraft/\ngovernance/\narchitecture/\nadr/\noperations/\narchive/\nYYYY-MM/\n\nCreate directories if missing.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4 \u2014 SAFE MOVE EXECUTION\n\nFor each non-protected markdown file:\n\n1. Compute new path.\n2. Verify no name collision.\n3. Move file using git mv.\n4. Update all references across repo.\n5. Re-scan for broken links.\n6. Confirm zero unresolved references.\n\nIf any reference cannot be updated deterministically:\n- Abort move for that file.\n- Log as BLOCKED.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 5 \u2014 INDEX GENERATION\n\nCreate docs/00_index.md:\n\nInclude:\n\nActive Specifications:\n\n* List docs/specs/*.md (excluding draft)\n\nGovernance:\n\n* docs/governance/*.md\n\nArchitecture:\n\n* docs/architecture/*.md\n\nOperations:\n\n* docs/operations/*.md\n\nArchive:\n\n* docs/archive/\n\nEnsure:\n\n* Only ACTIVE docs listed.\n* ARCHIVED docs excluded from main list.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 6 \u2014 STATUS HEADER STANDARDIZATION\n\nFor files moved to docs/specs or docs/governance:\n\nIf missing header block:\n\nPrepend:\n\n# <Title>\n\nVersion: 1.0\nStatus: ACTIVE\nLast Updated: <today>\nReplaces:\nDepends On:\n\nIf file moved to archive:\n\nPrepend:\n\nStatus: ARCHIVED\n\nDo not alter original content below header.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 7 \u2014 VALIDATION\n\nAfter restructure:\n\n1. Run:\n\n   * grep for broken .md references.\n2. Run:\n\n   * CI workflow dry validation (if possible).\n3. Ensure:\n\n   * No README broken links.\n   * No script path failures.\n4. Confirm:\n\n   * git status clean except intentional moves.\n5. Output:\n\n   * Files moved\n   * Files unchanged (protected)\n   * Files flagged ambiguous\n   * Any blocked moves\n\n---\n\n## DELIVERABLES\n\n1. Move Map:\n\n   * Old path \u2192 New path\n\n2. Protected Files List:\n\n   * Reason for protection\n\n3. Ambiguous Files List:\n\n   * Reason for manual review\n\n4. Updated docs/00_index.md content\n\n5. Confirmation:\n\n   * No functional dependency broken\n   * No CI references invalid\n   * No runtime contract references broken\n   * No commscribe dependency broken\n\n---\n\n## FAILSAFE\n\nIf any move risks breaking:\n\n* CI workflow\n* Runtime contract\n* Governance scripts\n* README primary navigation\n\nThen:\n- Abort that move.\n- Log as BLOCKED.\n- Do not proceed silently.\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nStructured only:\n\n* Inventory Summary\n* Dependency Report\n* Move Plan\n* Move Execution Results\n* Validation Results\n* Final Confirmation\n\nNo narrative commentary.\n\nEnd.",
