mance.py, tests/domain/test_phase1_integration.py |\n| TaxModel using realized gains | PARTIAL | server/domain/tax.py, server/domain/performance.py |\n| ComplianceModel settlement dependency | PARTIAL | server/domain/compliance.py, server/domain/performance.py |\n| Config toggles | COMPLETE | config.py (ENABLE_CORPORATE_ACTIONS, ENABLE_COST_BASIS_ENGINE, ENABLE_SETTLEMENT_ENFORCEMENT, DEFAULT_SETTLEMENT_CYCLE) |\n| Migration artifacts | COMPLETE | scripts/migrations/20260217_phase1_structural_accuracy.sql |\n| Runtime integration into existing trading pipeline | MISSING | No imports/usages outside tests/domain (search shows domain layer currently isolated) |\n| International/FX/margin Tier B logic | MISSING | No dedicated modules or integration paths in server/domain or runtime wiring |\n\nCompletion Percentages\n- Tier A completion (CorporateActionModel + CostBasisEngine + SettlementEngine): 88.7%\n- Tier B completion (Enhanced MarginModel + FX timing refinement): 9.2%\n- Tier C completion (excluded scope by spec decision): 0.0% implementation (expected excluded)\n- Overall realism spec completion (weighted domain coverage): 44.1%\n\nGap List\n- Missing runtime wiring from existing execution flow to server/domain/PerformanceEngine.\n- Cost model lacks componentized fees (commission/exchange/regulatory/borrow/fx spread/margin interest/session slippage decomposition).\n- Tax model lacks jurisdiction adapters/profile rules/foreign tax credit placeholders in executable path.\n- Compliance rules missing PDT/international entitlement checks specified in spec.\n- No dedicated margin model implementation (Tier B) beyond settlement engine margin bypass check.\n- No FX timing model implementation (Tier B).\n- International support scaffolding incomplete (currency conversion, transaction taxes, custody costs not implemented).\n- Migration artifact is SQL-only; no applied migration runner integration verified.\n\nRisk Classification (High / Medium / Low)\n- High: Domain layer not wired to live/paper execution path -> realism calculations may not affect actual trades.\n- High: Fee/tax component simplification can materially misstate net/after-tax results.\n- Medium: Settlement + cost basis modules are tested but isolated; integration regressions remain untested.\n- Medium: Margin/FX/international gaps limit cross-market realism claims.\n- Low: Tier C excluded items are explicitly documented as out of scope.\n\nDeterministic Next 3 Actions (ranked by structural impact)\n1. Integrate server/domain/PerformanceEngine into the existing trade execution pipeline and route all executed trades through compliance -> cost basis -> tax -> settlement ordering.\n2. Replace single cost_rate with componentized CostModel interfaces and persist fee breakdown fields in trade analytics outputs.\n3. Add Tier B skeleton modules (MarginModel, FX timing mode) with config gates and minimal deterministic tests to convert current missing areas into explicit partial implementations.",
