ed runtime/governance work has evolved outside this roadmap document lineage.\n- CI/governance maturity is higher than many roadmap sections imply (coverage gate + release-quality thresholds already present).\n\nEstimated Roadmap Completion %\n- Phase-average completion (using declared phase status percentages A-M): 37.7%\n- Foundation subset (A-H only): 48.8%\n- Realism-track alignment in roadmap document: 20.0% (low visibility of current realism implementation work)\n\nObsolete Items\n- Root-level canonical reference ROADMAP.md (obsolete location; file not present)\n- Any process expecting single mutable roadmap file at repo root (superseded by dated snapshot model in development_docs/roadmap)\n\nMissing Strategic Items\n- Explicit roadmap phase for Multi-Market Realism Spec execution tracking (Tier A/B/C milestones)\n- Explicit roadmap mapping for server/domain realism integration into live/paper runtime paths\n- Explicit roadmap milestone for fee/tax model production wiring and validation\n- Explicit roadmap section linking governance runtime enforcement and commscribe contracts as first-class deliverables\n\nRisk Classification (High / Medium / Low)\n- High: Canonical roadmap path drift (missing root ROADMAP.md while still referenced) can mislead planning and completion claims.\n- High: Realism implementation exists but roadmap does not track it, causing status-reporting mismatch.\n- Medium: Partial integration of realism modules into production flow may overstate implementation readiness if roadmap consumers rely on module existence only.\n- Low: systemd/nginx deployment references remain present and consistent in docs/artifacts.",
