      "outputs": "Roadmap Phase Snapshot\n- Phase E\n  - Status: Not started (0/5)\n  - Dependencies: Phase C\n- Phase F\n  - Status: In progress (2/4)\n  - Dependencies: Not explicitly declared\n- Phase H\n  - Status: 40% complete\n  - Dependencies: Phase D complete, Phase F helpful\n- Phase L\n  - Status: Not started (0/6)\n  - Dependencies: all previous phases complete\n- Phase M\n  - Status: Not started (0/5)\n  - Dependencies: Phase L complete\n\nRealism Phase Snapshot\n- Phase 1 \u2014 Structural Accuracy Layer\n  - Scope: CorporateActionModel, CostBasisEngine, SettlementEngine\n  - Status: COMPLETE at module level; runtime integration progressed into analytics path with gate\n- Phase 2 \u2014 Enhanced Financial Realism\n  - Scope: Enhanced MarginModel, FX timing refinement\n  - Status: PARTIAL (skeleton modules + gates + tests present; not fully operationalized)\n- Phase 3 \u2014 Advanced Tax Extensions\n  - Scope: wash-sale modeling, dividend qualification, foreign tax credit placeholder\n  - Status: PARTIAL (foreign tax credit placeholder scaffolding present; wash-sale/dividend qualification not implemented)\n- Phase 4 \u2014 Broker-Grade Replay Hardening\n  - Scope: broker fill ingestion hardening, broker fee ingestion hardening, reconciliation-only mode\n  - Status: NOT STARTED (no dedicated replay hardening/reconciliation mode implementation)\n- Acceptance Criteria Snapshot\n  - CostBasisEngine defined: YES\n  - SettlementEngine defined: YES\n  - TaxModel depends on CostBasisEngine outputs: YES\n  - ComplianceModel references SettlementEngine for funds availability: YES\n  - PerformanceEngine references corporate action adjustments: YES\n  - Phased roadmap updated with logical progression: PARTIAL (Phase R exists; canonical roadmap lineage still split)\n\nAlignment Matrix\n| Realism Phase | Roadmap Phase Candidate | Implementation Status | Integration Status | Gap Type |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Phase 1 Structural Accuracy | Phase H (closest current execution surface) | Implemented (module set complete) | Partial-to-High (analytics runtime path wired under gate; not all legacy upstream flows replaced) | Runtime integration missing |\n| Phase 2 Enhanced Financial Realism | New Phase R (or sub-track under H) | Partial (Margin/FX skeletons only) | Low | Phase misclassified |\n| Phase 3 Advanced Tax Extensions | New Phase R (or Phase M later for compliance overlays) | Partial (profile + placeholder fields) | Partial | Testing gap |\n| Phase 4 Replay Hardening | Phase H | Not implemented | Not implemented | Feature not started |\n| Cross-phase governance alignment | Phase F + Phase M | Implemented in CI/runtime governance layer | Medium | Documentation drift |\n\nDrift Summary\n- Roadmap E/F/H/L/M structure does not explicitly encode realism spec phases 1\u20134 as first-class milestones.\n- Realism module implementation progressed faster than roadmap phase narrative.\n- Runtime integration currently exists in analytics pipeline gate path, but roadmap does not distinctly represent this integration state.\n- Compliance/audit dependencies in roadmap (Phase M after L) conflict with already-present governance/audit runtime infrastructure.\n\nDeterministic Next Phase\n- Authoritative next milestone: Phase R2 \u2014 Runtime Integration Closure and Replay-Parity Hardening\n- Classification: New Phase R (not Phase H alone, not Phase M alone)\n- Rationale basis (deterministic factors):\n  - Architectural leverage: highest (turns module-level realism into operational realism)\n  - Dependency order: Phase 1 modules already available, enabling direct integration closure\n  - Risk reduction: highest immediate reduction of status/reporting drift and PnL source ambiguity\n  - Acceptance criteria closure: unlocks credible completion claims for realism phases 1\u20133\n\nExecution Contract\n- Title:\n  - Phase R2 \u2014 Runtime Integration Closure and Replay-Parity Hardening\n- Problem Type:\n  - prescriptive\n- Objective:\n  - Make realism pipeline authoritative across executed-trade runtime paths and align replay/fee/tax parity outputs for deterministic analytics.\n- Scope:\n  - Included:\n    - unify executed trade processing through PerformanceEngine in all active runtime trade recording paths\n    - ensure fee/tax/settlement outputs persist consistently to analytics store\n    - add replay-oriented integration seam for broker fill/fee ingestion stubs\n    - finalize roadmap phase mapping entry for R2 completion criteria\n  - Excluded:\n    - ML strategy work\n    - UI redesign\n    - full international execution semantics\n- Constraints:\n  - preserve backward compatibility with feature gates\n  - no silent endpoint schema breakage\n  - deterministic tests for each new integration seam\n- Required Integration Points:\n  - agents/execution_agent.py\n  - agents/analytics_agent.py\n  - server/domain/performance.py\n  - analytics/store.py\n  - replay/broker ingestion seam (new or existing adapter path)\n- Tests Required:\n  - end-to-end runtime path test: executed buy/sell with realism gate on/off parity checks\n  - replay ingestion test: broker fee/fill payload consumption path\n  - regression tests for legacy fallback path\n- Verification Requirements:\n  - command-grounded evidence of tests passing\n  - explicit gate-on/gate-off output comparison\n  - persistence field verification for gross/net/after-tax/fees/settlement\n- Deliverables:\n  - integration code updates\n  - deterministic tests\n  - roadmap phase status update artifact for R2",
