      "outputs": "SECTION 1 \u2014 Phase R2 Task Breakdown\n1. Define runtime authority boundary for realism pipeline.\n- Output: explicit gate-on authoritative source definition for gross/net/after-tax/settlement fields.\n\n2. Wire executed-trade processing to unified realism path under gate.\n- Output: one canonical transformation path for executed trades with legacy fallback retained.\n\n3. Add replay ingestion seam for fill/fee payload normalization.\n- Output: adapter contract mapping replay payloads to realism pipeline input shape.\n\n4. Standardize persisted analytics output fields for parity reporting.\n- Output: deterministic field set (gross_pnl, net_pnl, after_tax_pnl, fee_breakdown, settlement_date, realism_pipeline_enabled).\n\n5. Implement gate-on/gate-off parity comparator utility for test assertions.\n- Output: deterministic diff report for output deltas and field presence.\n\n6. Add regression guards for legacy path invariants.\n- Output: tests proving legacy behavior unchanged when gate is off.\n\n7. Add roadmap normalization artifact update for R2 lifecycle state.\n- Output: Phase R2 status entry + H-vs-R2 boundary rule text.\n\nSECTION 2 \u2014 Dependency-Ordered Execution Plan\n1. Task 1 (authority boundary)\n- Justification: prevents ambiguous dual-source outputs before integration work.\n\n2. Task 4 (target field contract)\n- Justification: establishes stable output schema before wiring and tests.\n\n3. Task 2 (runtime wiring under gate)\n- Justification: core integration step; depends on authority and field contract.\n\n4. Task 3 (replay ingestion seam)\n- Justification: uses same canonical input/output contract as runtime wiring.\n\n5. Task 5 (parity comparator)\n- Justification: requires gate and output contracts in place.\n\n6. Task 6 (regression guards)\n- Justification: validates no fallback regression after integration changes.\n\n7. Task 7 (roadmap normalization update)\n- Justification: finalize classification and reporting after execution semantics are fixed.\n\nSECTION 3 \u2014 Integration Touchpoints\n- Runtime execution/events:\n  - `agents/execution_agent.py`\n  - `agents/analytics_agent.py`\n  - `agents/events.py`\n- Realism pipeline domain:\n  - `server/domain/performance.py`\n  - `server/domain/cost_model.py`\n  - `server/domain/tax.py`\n  - `server/domain/settlement.py`\n  - `server/domain/cost_basis.py`\n- Persistence/reporting:\n  - `analytics/store.py`\n- Replay seam:\n  - `scripts/replay_recorder.py` and/or replay ingestion adapter module boundary\n- Config/gates:\n  - `config.py`\n- Roadmap normalization:\n  - canonical roadmap artifact (root entrypoint + canonical dated snapshot)\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 Test Specification\n1. Runtime gate parity test (on/off)\n- Case: identical executed trade sequence under gate=false then gate=true.\n- Expected outputs:\n  - gate=false preserves legacy fields/values.\n  - gate=true includes realism fields and deterministic computed values.\n\n2. Runtime buy/split/sell realism chain test\n- Case: buy -> corporate action split -> sell.\n- Expected outputs:\n  - realized gain from lot accounting,\n  - non-zero fee component aggregation,\n  - tax estimate present,\n  - settlement date populated.\n\n3. Replay ingestion normalization test\n- Case: replay payload with fill + fee attributes.\n- Expected outputs:\n  - normalized payload accepted by realism path,\n  - parity fields persisted,\n  - no schema-breaking output.\n\n4. Legacy regression test (gate off)\n- Case: existing analytics trade capture scenario set.\n- Expected outputs:\n  - unchanged pass behavior for legacy path,\n  - no mandatory new-field failures.\n\n5. Determinism test\n- Case: same input trade stream run twice.\n- Expected outputs:\n  - identical computed fee/tax/settlement outputs,\n  - no stochastic variance.\n\nSECTION 5 \u2014 Verification Requirements\nRequired Commands\n1. `python3 -m pytest -q tests/domain tests/test_analytics_agent_trade_capture.py`\n2. Targeted replay seam tests (new test module command)\n3. Optional focused regression suite for existing analytics/trade flow tests\n\nRequired Observable Outputs\n- All required tests pass.\n- Gate on/off parity report artifact generated (text/JSON diff summary).\n- Evidence of persisted fields in trade records:\n  - `gross_pnl`, `net_pnl`, `after_tax_pnl`, `fee_breakdown`, `settlement_date`, `realism_pipeline_enabled`.\n\nRequired Artifacts\n- Test report lines with pass counts.\n- Parity diff artifact path.\n- Updated roadmap normalization entry with explicit R2 status and H boundary.\n\nSECTION 6 \u2014 Roadmap Normalization Entry\nPhase R2 \u2014 Runtime Integration Closure and Replay-Parity Hardening\n- Status: IN_PROGRESS (until gate-on authoritative path + replay seam + regression tests pass)\n- Scope Boundaries:\n  - Includes runtime executed-trade realism authority, replay parity seam, gate parity verification, legacy fallback regression protection.\n  - Excludes UI redesign, ML phases, full international execution semantics.\n- Phase H Boundary Rule:\n  - Phase H remains backtesting-focused (simulation/backtest UX/optimization).\n  - Phase R2 owns operational realism runtime authority and replay parity for live/paper execution outputs.\n- Completion Criteria:\n  1. Authoritative runtime realism path active under gate.\n  2. Replay normalization seam validated.\n  3. Gate on/off deterministic parity evidence produced.\n  4. Legacy fallback regression suite passes.",
