      "outputs": "SECTION 1 \u2014 Requirement Extraction\n1. Include boolean `realism_pipeline_enabled` when persisting trade records.\n2. Field value must reflect gate state at trade-record time.\n3. Gate OFF must persist `realism_pipeline_enabled=False`.\n4. Gate ON must persist `realism_pipeline_enabled=True`.\n5. Legacy behavior unchanged except adding this field.\n6. Modify `analytics/store.py` for persistence logic.\n7. Modify trade schema/model only if needed.\n8. Add tests validating persistence behavior.\n9. Test A (Gate Off): set gate False, persist trade, assert field exists, value False, other fields unchanged.\n10. Test B (Gate On): set gate True, persist trade, assert field exists, value True.\n11. Ensure no other logic changes introduced.\n12. Run verification command (or equivalent minimal invocation).\n13. Provide Section 1 output: unified diffs of every modified file.\n14. Provide Section 2 output: full content of new/changed test files.\n15. Provide Section 3 output: full pytest summary and pass count.\n16. Provide Section 4 output: example persisted trade record proving new field + required existing fields.\n17. Do not expand scope.\n18. Do not modify unrelated modules.\n19. Do not introduce architectural changes.\n20. Do not implement additional Phase R2 tasks.\n21. Stop after this slice is complete.\n\nSECTION 2 \u2014 Requirement Compliance Matrix\nR1 | SATISFIED | Evidence: `analytics/store.py` diff adds `trade[\"realism_pipeline_enabled\"] = bool(...)` | Persistence field explicitly added.\nR2 | SATISFIED | Evidence: expression falls back to `config.ENABLE_REALISM_PIPELINE` and preserves passed value | Captures gate state at write time.\nR3 | SATISFIED | Evidence: proof record shows AAPL trade with `realism_pipeline_enabled: false` | Gate-off persistence shown.\nR4 | SATISFIED | Evidence: proof record shows MSFT trade with `realism_pipeline_enabled: true` | Gate-on persistence shown.\nR5 | PARTIALLY SATISFIED | Evidence: no explicit regression diff beyond target logic; pytest passed | Behavioral non-regression is inferred from tests, not exhaustively proven.\nR6 | SATISFIED | Evidence: `analytics/store.py` modified | Required file changed.\nR7 | SATISFIED | Evidence: no schema/model redesign shown | Constraint respected.\nR8 | SATISFIED | Evidence: added gate-off/gate-on persistence tests in `tests/test_analytics_store.py` | Persistence behavior covered.\nR9 | PARTIALLY SATISFIED | Evidence: Gate-off test asserts existence + False; does not explicitly assert every other field unchanged | Main assertions present; \"no other field values changed\" not explicitly asserted.\nR10 | SATISFIED | Evidence: Gate-on test asserts existence + True | Required assertions present.\nR11 | SATISFIED | Evidence: logic change limited to store defaulting; additional edits are tests | No extra production logic beyond scope observed.\nR12 | SATISFIED | Evidence: pytest run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/domain tests/test_analytics_agent_trade_capture.py tests/test_analytics_store.py` -> `52 passed` | Equivalent minimal invocation with relevant added test module.\nR13 | SATISFIED | Evidence: output Section 1 includes unified diffs for all modified files | Deliverable present.\nR14 | SATISFIED | Evidence: output Section 2 includes full changed test files | Deliverable present.\nR15 | SATISFIED | Evidence: output Section 3 includes full summary and pass count (`52 passed`) | Deliverable present.\nR16 | SATISFIED | Evidence: output Section 4 includes JSON persisted trade records with required fields and new flag | Deliverable present.\nR17 | SATISFIED | Evidence: changes limited to store + tests for this slice | No clear scope overrun.\nR18 | SATISFIED | Evidence: modified files are directly related to persistence/test verification | No unrelated module change evidenced.\nR19 | SATISFIED | Evidence: no new abstractions/refactor architecture in diff | Constraint respected.\nR20 | SATISFIED | Evidence: no replay/comparator