      "request_text": "TITLE\nREQ Log Normalization and Objective Field Enforcement\n\nPROBLEM TYPE\nprescriptive (log structure enforcement + deterministic parsing update)\n\nOBJECTIVE\nNormalize the REQ log structure so that the `OBJECTIVE` field contains only the concise mission statement and never captures the full request body or additional sections.\n\nSCOPE\n\n* Update REQ logging logic/parser.\n* Enforce strict OBJECTIVE extraction rules.\n* Normalize existing malformed REQ entries.\n* Do not modify unrelated logging systems.\n\nINPUTS\n\n* Current REQ log file(s).\n* Current request parsing or logging implementation.\n\nREQUIRED ACTIONS\n\n1. Define Canonical REQ Entry Structure\n\nEach REQ entry must follow:\n\nREQ ENTRY\nID:\nDATE:\nTITLE:\nOBJECTIVE:\nSTATUS:\nARTIFACTS:\n\nNo additional sections allowed inside OBJECTIVE.\n\n2. Implement Deterministic OBJECTIVE Extraction Rule\n\nWhen parsing a new request:\n\nA. Locate exact header token:\n`OBJECTIVE`\n\nB. Capture only the text that:\n\n* Begins immediately after `OBJECTIVE`\n* Stops at the first:\n\n  * Blank line\n  * ALL-CAPS section header\n  * Line matching regex: `^[A-Z _-]+:$`\n  * Markdown header (`#` prefix)\n\nC. Trim whitespace.\n\nD. Enforce constraints:\n\n* Maximum 500 characters.\n* Maximum 3 sentences.\n* Must not contain:\n\n  * \u201cSECTION\u201d\n  * \u201cREQUIRED ACTIONS\u201d\n  * bullet markers (`- `, `* `)\n  * numbered lists (`1.`, `2.`)\n  * code blocks (```)\n\nE. If constraint violated:\n\n* Reject entry.\n* Emit error:\n  `OBJECTIVE field invalid \u2014 contains non-objective content.`\n\nF. If no OBJECTIVE token found:\n\n* Reject log write.\n* Emit error:\n  `OBJECTIVE section missing \u2014 REQ entry not recorded.`\n\n3. Remove Fallback-to-Full-Request Behavior\n\nIf OBJECTIVE extraction fails:\n\n* Do NOT default to full request body.\n* Do NOT attempt heuristic summary.\n* Hard fail.\n\n4. Normalize Existing REQ Log Entries\n\nScan existing REQ log:\n\nFor each entry:\n\n* If OBJECTIVE exceeds constraints:\n\n  * Re-parse original request source if available.\n  * Otherwise:\n\n    * Truncate at first blank line.\n    * Remove any lines containing section markers.\n    * Trim to first 3 sentences.\n* Record normalization action in:\n  `REQ_LOG_NORMALIZATION_REPORT.md`\n\n5. Add Validation Guard\n\nBefore writing a REQ entry:\n\n* Run validation function `validate_objective(text)`\n* If invalid, abort write.\n\n6. Add Unit Tests\n\nAdd tests validating:\n\nTest 1 \u2014 Proper Extraction\n\n* Given valid multi-section request, only objective sentence stored.\n\nTest 2 \u2014 Reject Full-Body Capture\n\n* Given OBJECTIVE followed by REQUIRED ACTIONS block, ensure extraction stops before that.\n\nTest 3 \u2014 Reject Missing OBJECTIVE\n\n* Ensure log write fails.\n\nTest 4 \u2014 Reject Overlength Objective\n\n* Ensure >500 chars fails.\n\nTest 5 \u2014 Reject Bullet/Section Contamination\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n\n* Do not modify unrelated logging behavior.\n* Do not alter REQ ID generation.\n* Do not redesign log storage backend.\n* Only enforce OBJECTIVE isolation and normalization.\n* Maintain backward compatibility for other REQ fields.\n\nVERIFICATION COMMAND\n\nRun:\n\n```\npython3 -m pytest -q tests/test_req_log_normalization.py\n```\n\nREQUIRED OUTPUT\n\nSECTION 1 \u2014 Files Modified\n\n* List modified/added files.\n\nSECTION 2 \u2014 Extraction Logic Summary\n\n* Short description of parsing and validation implementation.\n\nSECTION 3 \u2014 Normalization Report\n\n* Count of malformed entries fixed.\n* Example before/after (concise).\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 Pytest Summary\n\n* Full summary line.\n* Total tests passed.\n\nStop after completion.",
      "codex_ack_plan": "Read request, execute exactly the requested scope, run required verification commands, and complete with the specified output format only.",
      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-18T03:48:18+00:00 Implemented objective extraction/validation hard-fail path, legacy objective normalization/reporting, and targeted unit tests; verification command executed and passing.",
      "outputs": "SECTION 1 \u2014 Files Modified\n- `commscribe/scripts/communicate_scan.py`\n- `tests/test_req_log_normalization.py` (added)\n- `REQ_LOG_NORMALIZATION_REPORT.md` (generated)\n- `commscribe/communicate.json` (normalized objective fields on existing entries)\n- `commscribe/communicate.md` (synced normalized objective fields)\n\nSECTION 2 \u2014 Extraction Logic Summary\n- Added deterministic `extract_objective(request_text)` that:\n  - finds exact `OBJECTIVE` / `OBJECTIVE:` token,\n  - captures text immediately after token,\n  - stops on first blank line, ALL-CAPS header, `^[A-Z _-]+:$`, or markdown header (`#`).\n- Added `validate_objective(text)` guard enforcing:\n  - max 500 chars,\n  - max 3 sentences,\n  - rejects section/bullet/numbered-list/code-block contamination.\n- Added hard-fail behavior in `consume`:\n  - missing objective -> `OBJECTIVE section missing \u2014 REQ entry not recorded.`\n  - invalid objective -> `OBJECTIVE field invalid \u2014 contains non-objective content.`\n- Removed fallback-to-full-request behavior by requiring objective extraction success for new writes.\n- Added normalization pass for existing entries with report emission.\n\nSECTION 3 \u2014 Normalization Report\n- Malformed entries fixed: `82`\n- Report file: `REQ_LOG_NORMALIZATION_REPORT.md`\n- Example before/after:\n  - REQ `REQ-20260217-213804`\n  - before: `(empty)`\n  - after: `Eliminate identified compliance deficiencies by strengthening regression guarantees for legacy field invariance when persisting realism_pipeline_enabled.`\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 Pytest Summary\n- `.....                                                                    [100%]`\n- Total tests passed: `5 passed in 2.65s`",
      "evidence": "Verification command run: .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_req_log_normalization.py; result: 5 passed in 2.65s. Normalization artifact: REQ_LOG_NORMALIZATION_REPORT.md (82 entries fixed).",
