      "execution_log": "- 2026-02-18T03:56:24+00:00 Completed roadmap/spec/runtime reconciliation and produced deterministic phase alignment, drift classification, and next-phase execution contract (analysis-only).",
      "outputs": "Roadmap Phase Snapshot\n- Phase E (Market Awareness): Not started, 0/5 done.\n- Phase F (Testing & CI): In progress, 2/4 done; blockers include coverage gate and missing broker-failure/backtest-regression tests.\n- Phase H (Backtesting Enhancement): 40% complete (foundation complete; UI/optimizer/validation work pending).\n- Phase L (Production Readiness): Not started, 0/6 done.\n- Phase M (Compliance & Auditability): Not started, 0/5 done.\n- Phase R (Multi-Market Realism Track):\n  - R1: ~90% module-level complete.\n  - R2: NOT COMPLETE.\n  - R3: PARTIAL.\n  - R4: NOT STARTED.\n  - R5: NOT STARTED.\n\nRealism Phase Snapshot\n- Phase 1 (Structural Accuracy Layer):\n  - Scope: CorporateActionModel, CostBasisEngine, SettlementEngine.\n  - Repository state: Implemented in `server/domain/*`; integration test exists (`tests/domain/test_phase1_integration.py`).\n  - Runtime integration status: Partial (wired through analytics path; not yet authoritative execution-path integration).\n- Phase 2 (Enhanced Financial Realism):\n  - Scope: Enhanced MarginModel, FX timing refinement.\n  - Repository state: Models/toggles exist (`server/domain/performance.py`, `server/domain/fx_timing.py`, `server/domain/margin.py`, Tier-B skeleton tests).\n  - Runtime integration status: Partial-to-limited (available in performance path, but invocation surface is still constrained).\n- Phase 3 (Advanced Tax Extensions):\n  - Scope: Wash-sale modeling, dividend qualification, foreign tax credit placeholder.\n  - Repository state: Basic tax profile + foreign credit fields present; wash-sale/dividend-qualification logic not present.\n  - Runtime integration status: Partial (tax estimate present, advanced extensions incomplete).\n- Phase 4 (Broker-Grade Replay Hardening):\n  - Scope: Broker fill ingestion hardening, broker fee ingestion hardening, reconciliation-only realism mode.\n  - Repository state: Not evidenced as implemented.\n  - Runtime integration status: Not started.\n- Acceptance criteria status:\n  - Structural modules + core dependencies: substantially present.\n  - \"Phased roadmap updated\" criterion: present via Roadmap Phase R.\n  - Full operational integration criterion: not complete (R2 still open).\n\nAlignment Matrix\n| Realism Phase | Roadmap Phase Candidate | Implementation Status | Integration Status | Gap Type |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Phase 1 (Structural Accuracy) | R1 primary, R2 for authoritative wiring | Mostly implemented (domain modules + tests) | Partial (analytics-driven wiring, not full authoritative execution-plane wiring) | Runtime integration missing |\n| Phase 2 (Margin/FX) | R4 primary | Partial (engines/toggles exist) | Limited/partial invocation | Documentation drift |\n| Phase 3 (Advanced Tax Extensions) | R3 primary, M secondary for audit-facing compliance outputs | Partial (basic tax + placeholder fields; major extensions absent) | Partial | Feature not started |\n| Phase 4 (Broker-Grade Replay Hardening) | R2 + H intersection; M adjacency for reconciliation evidence | Not evidenced | Not started | Phase misclassified |\n\nDrift Summary\n- Structural drift 1: Roadmap marks R4 \"NOT STARTED\" while repository contains Tier-B code surfaces (margin/fx models and toggles) -> implementation/docs mismatch.\n- Structural drift 2: Realism pipeline invocation is concentrated in analytics/post-execution handling (`agents/analytics_agent.py`), while authoritative execution-path integration remains incomplete -> confirms R2 status gap.\n- Structural drift 3: Spec Phase 4 (broker-grade replay hardening) has no clear executed mapping in current runtime; roadmap alignment exists conceptually in R2 but operational artifacts are not evidenced.\n- Structural drift 4: Phase H contains backtest realism subitems (transaction cost modeling, realistic execution), creating overlap with Realism R-track unless explicitly split by ownership boundary.\n\nDeterministic Next Phase\n- Authoritative next milestone: Phase R2 \u2014 Authoritative runtime integration of realism pipeline in execution-critical flow.\n- Placement decision: New Phase R (existing realism track), not Phase H/F/M.\n- Deterministic rationale:\n  - Dependency order: R2 unblocks trustworthy use of Phase 1 assets and makes R3/R4 outcomes operationally meaningful.\n  - Architectural leverage: Converts module-level realism into runtime truth path.\n  - Risk: Current partial wiring can produce analytics enrichment without full execution-governed realism guarantees.\n  - Acceptance alignment: Directly addresses spec/roadmap requirement that module completion is insufficient without runtime wiring.\n\nExecution Contract\n- Title: Phase R2 \u2014 Authoritative Runtime Realism Integration\n- Problem Type: prescriptive (integration contract)\n- Objective: Route executed trades through a single authoritative realism pipeline path before persistence/reporting so cost/tax/settlement outputs are deterministically produced and auditable.\n- Scope:\n  - Included:\n    - Define and enforce one runtime invocation boundary for `PerformanceEngine.process_trade` on executed trades.\n    - Ensure persistence includes realism provenance flag and computed realism outputs when enabled.\n    - Preserve gate-off behavior with deterministic fallback fields.\n    - Align analytics outputs to same authoritative trade record.\n  - Excluded:\n    - New Tier-B/Tier-C feature expansion.\n    - Roadmap document edits.\n    - UI redesign.\n- Constraints:\n  - No backend architecture redesign.\n  - No REQ ID / logging backend changes.\n  - Maintain backward compatibility for non-realism trade flow.\n- Required integration points:\n  - Execution event emission path (`agents/execution_agent.py` -> `OrderExecuted`).\n  - Realism processing boundary (`server/domain/performance.py`).\n  - Persistence sink (`analytics/store.py`) and trade schema continuity.\n  - Config gates (`ENABLE_REALISM_PIPELINE`, settlement/cost/tax toggles).\n- Tests required:\n  - Integration: executed buy/sell lifecycle with realism ON/OFF across event->processing->persistence.\n  - Regression: no mutation of legacy required fields when realism metadata added.\n  - Determinism: same input event stream yields identical realism outputs under fixed config.\n  - Negative path: processing failure sets explicit provenance/error flags without breaking trade recording.\n- Verification requirements:\n  - Targeted pytest suite for domain + analytics capture + persistence assertions.\n  - Evidence artifact: persisted trade examples for gate OFF/ON with required legacy fields intact.\n  - Explicit pass/fail matrix for R2 acceptance checks.\n- Deliverables:\n  - R2 implementation diff (scoped integration only).\n  - Test additions and passing summaries.\n  - Runtime evidence samples proving authoritative wiring and fallback behavior.",
