      "request_text": "REQ ENTRY\nID: REQ-COMMSCRIBE-LOG-STRUCTURE-AUDIT-AND-DEPRECATION\nDATE: 2026-02-17\nTITLE: Audit communicate.md / communicate.json Structure and Fully Deprecate File-Based Storage\nOBJECTIVE:\n1) Determine whether communicate.md can be deterministically parsed into a formal schema.\n2) Extract required entry structure into a normalized table/schema definition.\n3) Decide whether communicate.md, communicate.json, and outputs.md are still active storage mechanisms.\n4) If file-based storage is deprecated and DB-backed engine is authoritative, complete 100% removal of file-based REQ storage.\n5) If not fully deprecated, outline exact migration steps and then execute.\n\nSTATUS: IN_PROGRESS\n\nARTIFACTS:\n- commscribe/docs/COMMUNICATE_SCHEMA.md\n- commscribe/db/schema.sql (if updated)\n- commscribe/scripts/audit_communicate_files.py\n- commscribe/docs/FILE_STORAGE_DEPRECATION_REPORT.md\n- commscribe/tests/test_no_file_storage.py\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 1 \u2014 STRUCTURE AUDIT\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Parse communicate.md:\n   - Identify consistent entry boundaries.\n   - Extract:\n        REQ ID\n        DATE\n        TITLE\n        OBJECTIVE\n        STATUS\n        ARTIFACTS\n        VERIFICATION BLOCK\n        LOG ENTRIES\n   - Detect inconsistencies or malformed entries.\n\n2. Parse communicate.json:\n   - Identify schema fields.\n   - Compare with communicate.md.\n   - Detect divergence.\n\n3. Check for outputs.md usage:\n   - Search repo for read/write references.\n   - Determine if active, legacy, or dead.\n\n4. Produce structured schema table:\n\n   Table: requests\n   Table: verification_blocks\n   Table: artifacts\n   Table: status_history\n   Table: logs\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 2 \u2014 STORAGE AUTHORITY DETERMINATION\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDetermine:\n\n- Is SQLite engine authoritative?\n- Are file writes still occurring?\n- Are any runtime paths still reading from communicate.md?\n- Is communicate.json redundant?\n- Is outputs.md redundant?\n\nClassify each file as:\n- Active authoritative\n- Transitional\n- Dead\n- Archival only\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 3 \u2014 DECISION BRANCH\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIF file-based storage still active:\n    - Produce exact migration plan.\n    - Do not remove files yet.\n    - Implement dual-write detection.\n    - Then execute migration.\n\nIF DB-backed engine fully authoritative:\n    - Remove write paths to:\n        communicate.md\n        communicate.json\n        outputs.md\n    - Convert communicate.md to:\n        ARCHIVE_ONLY.md\n    - Move legacy files to:\n        commscribe/archive/legacy/\n    - Add hard guard:\n        Fail if system attempts to write to legacy files.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 4 \u2014 IMPLEMENTATION\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Remove file write operations.\n2. Remove file read operations.\n3. Update communicate CLI to use DB exclusively.\n4. Add regression test:\n   - Assert no file writes occur.\n5. Add static test:\n   - Search for \"open('communicate.md'\" or similar.\n   - Fail if found.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 5 \u2014 VALIDATION\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nRun:\n- Full test suite.\n- Confirm:\n    - REQ lifecycle works.\n    - UI loads from DB.\n    - CLI functions normally.\n    - No file storage side effects.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nDELIVERABLES\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFiles Modified\nFiles Removed\nSchema Table Definition\nStorage Authority Determination\nMigration/Removal Summary\nTest Commands Executed + Results\n\n--- VERIFICATION REPORT ---\nObjectives Addressed\nQuality Checks\nFile Storage Removal Confirmed\nSchema Integrity Confirmed\nOutstanding Risks\nFinal Status\n\nEND REQ",
