      "request_text": "**NOTE** : THIS NEW FORMAT IS REQUIRED FOR YOU TO FOLLOW. UPDATE THE REQUIRED FORMAT FOR RESPONSES, LOGGING AND THE UI. ALL PROCESSES SHOULD BE UNIFIED AS FAR AS UNDERSTANDING THE STRUCTURE. ... (PROCEED. KEEP THOSE CONSIDERATIONS)\n\nREQ ENTRY\nID: DOC-AUTHORITY-MATRIX-001\nDATE: 2026-02-18\nTITLE: Documentation Authority Matrix Construction and Canonical Governance Infrastructure\nOBJECTIVE:\nConstruct a Documentation Authority Matrix that identifies a single canonical authority per domain, detects conflicts and drift, links documentation to implementation and tests, and establishes a controlled deprecation protocol. No runtime code changes permitted.\n\nSCOPE:\n- All documentation files (.md and similar)\n- Roadmap documents\n- Governance documents\n- Architecture documents\n- Realism specifications\n- Communicate engine documentation\n- Testing strategy documents\n- CI documents\n- Any ADR-style or spec documents\n\nOUT OF SCOPE:\n- Modifying application runtime code\n- Refactoring business logic\n- Changing database schema\n- Modifying CI configuration\n- Deleting files\n- Moving files to archive\n\nSOURCE OF TRUTH:\n- Repository documentation\n- Test files\n- Code references\n- Communicate logs\n\nFILES ALLOWED TO MODIFY:\n- Creation of:\n    docs/governance/document_graph.md\n    docs/governance/document_authority_matrix.md\n    docs/governance/deprecation_log.md\n    docs/canonical/*.md\n\nFILES FORBIDDEN:\n- All runtime code\n- All test files\n- All CI configuration\n- All database schema files\n\nSUCCESS CRITERIA:\n\nPhase 1 \u2013 Documentation Graph:\n- Produce docs/governance/document_graph.md\n  For each document:\n    - Path\n    - Declared purpose\n    - Domains referenced\n    - References to other docs\n    - References to code\n    - References to tests\n    - Claims about implementation state\n\nPhase 2 \u2013 Domain Extraction:\n- Produce explicit domain list derived from actual content.\n- No invented domains.\n\nPhase 3 \u2013 Authority Matrix:\n- Produce docs/governance/document_authority_matrix.md\n  Table columns:\n    Domain\n    Canonical File (max 1)\n    Supporting Files\n    Implementation Linked (YES/NO/UNKNOWN)\n    Tests Linked (YES/NO/UNKNOWN)\n    Conflicts (explicit file paths)\n    Drift Detected (YES/NO/UNKNOWN)\n    Status (STABLE / CONFLICT / MISSING AUTHORITY / UNKNOWN)\n\nRules:\n- If multiple canonical candidates \u2192 mark CONFLICT.\n- If none \u2192 mark MISSING AUTHORITY.\n- No silent merging.\n\nPhase 4 \u2013 Canonical Drafts:\n- For each domain with CONFLICT or MISSING AUTHORITY:\n  Create docs/canonical/<domain>_canonical_v1.md\n  Including:\n    - Scope\n    - Invariants\n    - Implementation linkage\n    - Test linkage\n    - Source lineage\n    - Conflict notes\n\nPhase 5 \u2013 Deprecation Log:\n- Produce docs/governance/deprecation_log.md\n  Including:\n    - Deprecated file path\n    - Replacement canonical file\n    - Reason\n    - Date\n\nVERIFICATION REQUIRED:\n- Confirm no existing documentation was deleted.\n- Confirm no runtime code modified.\n- Confirm each domain has at most one canonical file.\n- Confirm all conflicts are explicitly listed.\n- Confirm no domain was invented without document evidence.\n\nINFERENCE POLICY:\n- Do not assume implementation state from documentation.\n- If test linkage unclear \u2192 mark UNKNOWN.\n- If authority ambiguous \u2192 mark CONFLICT.\n- No silent reconciliation.\n- No file deletion.\n\nSTATUS:\nPENDING\n\nARTIFACTS:\n- docs/governance/document_graph.md\n- docs/governance/document_authority_matrix.md\n- docs/governance/deprecation_log.md\n- docs/canonical/*.md (as required)",
